s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/commits/4fe2623c8e386b7b3f6b2753e42bacbfe8f6b258/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T04:08:56Z","email":"guillegmo@hotmail.com","name":"Guillermo Montoya Ocampo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T04:08:56Z","email":"guillegmo@hotmail.com","name":"Guillermo Montoya Ocampo"},"message":"feat(auth): mostrar/ocultar contraseña y loader al activar cuenta\n\n- LoginPage y ActivatePage: botón de ojo junto a cada campo de contraseña\n  para alternar entre texto oculto y visible, así el usuario puede validar\n  que escribió lo que quería (en ActivatePage, cada campo — nueva y\n  confirmación — tiene su propio toggle independiente).\n- ActivatePage: el botón \"Crear mi contraseña y entrar\" ahora muestra un\n  spinner (Loader2) mientras procesa, en vez de solo cambiar el texto —\n  mismo patrón que ya usaba el botón de login.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0177VXzr6jYBDEDht9LCF4E5","tree":{"sha":"cc1f512dfc77b42a046d87107c4953cb5232ad62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/git/trees/cc1f512dfc77b42a046d87107c4953cb5232ad62"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/git/commits/4fe2623c8e386b7b3f6b2753e42bacbfe8f6b258","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54384673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo","id":54384673,"login":"guillegmo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0Mzg0Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo/appingles/commit/4fe2623c8e386b7b3f6b2753e42bacbfe8f6b258","node_id":"C_kwDOT5AOd9oAKDRmZTI2MjNjOGUzODZiN2IzZjZiMjc1M2U0MmJhY2JmZThmNmIyNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo/appingles/commit/2a962598d1a93d0e6d85791a595f0e383f782f1c","sha":"2a962598d1a93d0e6d85791a595f0e383f782f1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/commits/2a962598d1a93d0e6d85791a595f0e383f782f1c"}],"sha":"4fe2623c8e386b7b3f6b2753e42bacbfe8f6b258","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/commits/4fe2623c8e386b7b3f6b2753e42bacbfe8f6b258"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54384673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo","id":54384673,"login":"guillegmo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0Mzg0Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/commits/2a962598d1a93d0e6d85791a595f0e383f782f1c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T03:54:53Z","email":"guillegmo@hotmail.com","name":"Guillermo Montoya Ocampo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T03:54:53Z","email":"guillegmo@hotmail.com","name":"Guillermo Montoya Ocampo"},"message":"fix(hotmart): un fallo de SMTP ya no se reporta como correo enviado\n\nEncontrado probando manualmente el flujo real: cuando falla la\nautenticación SMTP (credenciales vencidas, bloqueo temporal del proveedor,\netc.), sendActivationEmail cae a dry-run para no perder el enlace — correcto\n— pero seguía devolviendo transport:''smtp''. processHotmartEvent y\nresendActivationForEmail decidían \"¿se envió?\" comparando\nmail.transport === ''smtp'', así que un fallo real de SMTP se reportaba como\nactivationEmailSent:true (falso positivo) y el evento de analítica quedaba\nmal etiquetado como activation_email_sent en vez de _failed — sin ninguna\nalerta visible de que un cliente real se quedó sin su correo de activación.\n\nAhora mailer.js devuelve transport:''dryrun'' cuando el envío SMTP falla (ya\ntiene sent:false, que es lo que realmente importa), y ambos callers deciden\npor mail.sent en vez de por el valor de transport. Cubierto con un test que\nsimula un fallo de autenticación SMTP real.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0177VXzr6jYBDEDht9LCF4E5","tree":{"sha":"0d5b9cbc48fefebbbec4acdb1a93e8b1c849354a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/git/trees/0d5b9cbc48fefebbbec4acdb1a93e8b1c849354a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/git/commits/2a962598d1a93d0e6d85791a595f0e383f782f1c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54384673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo","id":54384673,"login":"guillegmo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0Mzg0Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo/appingles/commit/2a962598d1a93d0e6d85791a595f0e383f782f1c","node_id":"C_kwDOT5AOd9oAKDJhOTYyNTk4ZDFhOTNkMGU2ZDg1NzkxYTU5NWYwZTM4M2Y3ODJmMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo/appingles/commit/0ae5717adafec183a82950d66b8f62242d147a1b","sha":"0ae5717adafec183a82950d66b8f62242d147a1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/commits/0ae5717adafec183a82950d66b8f62242d147a1b"}],"sha":"2a962598d1a93d0e6d85791a595f0e383f782f1c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/commits/2a962598d1a93d0e6d85791a595f0e383f782f1c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54384673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo","id":54384673,"login":"guillegmo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0Mzg0Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/commits/0ae5717adafec183a82950d66b8f62242d147a1b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T03:48:19Z","email":"guillegmo@hotmail.com","name":"Guillermo Montoya Ocampo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T03:48:19Z","email":"guillegmo@hotmail.com","name":"Guillermo Montoya Ocampo"},"message":"fix(provisioning): nunca manda a un cliente real un enlace de activación a localhost\n\nDetectado en pruebas manuales: un script de prueba local heredó por error\nACTIVATION_URL=http://localhost:5173/... y el correo de activación salió\ncon ese enlace roto. activationUrl() ya caía a la URL real de producción\nsi la variable faltaba, así que el riesgo real para clientes es bajo, pero\nse agrega una red de seguridad explícita: en NODE_ENV=production,\ngenerateActivationLink ahora falla ruidosamente (se registra como\nactivation_email_failed, el cliente puede pedir el reenvío) si la URL\nresuelta apunta a localhost/127.0.0.1, en vez de arriesgarse a mandar un\nenlace que no lleva a ningún lado.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.