l":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/commits/a09cd19dad4dba8f6b71a6fb2ef676d25b17697d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T05:03:02Z","email":"guillegmo@hotmail.com","name":"Guillermo Montoya Ocampo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T05:03:02Z","email":"guillegmo@hotmail.com","name":"Guillermo Montoya Ocampo"},"message":"feat(stats): reemplaza tokens consumidos por sesiones con el tutor\n\n\"Tokens consumidos\" era una métrica técnica sin valor para el usuario final.\nSe reemplaza por el conteo de sesiones con el tutor IA (stats.ai.totalSessions),\nmás legible, y se simplifica el tooltip.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0177VXzr6jYBDEDht9LCF4E5","tree":{"sha":"0ec14c1c8ee40c61bb30de20bbd65ab2083ce75f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/git/trees/0ec14c1c8ee40c61bb30de20bbd65ab2083ce75f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/git/commits/a09cd19dad4dba8f6b71a6fb2ef676d25b17697d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54384673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo","id":54384673,"login":"guillegmo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0Mzg0Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo/appingles/commit/a09cd19dad4dba8f6b71a6fb2ef676d25b17697d","node_id":"C_kwDOT5AOd9oAKGEwOWNkMTlkYWQ0ZGJhOGY2YjcxYTZmYjJlZjY3NmQyNWIxNzY5N2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo/appingles/commit/f45a63e2633d3524f118ca04f018e2b091db9780","sha":"f45a63e2633d3524f118ca04f018e2b091db9780","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/commits/f45a63e2633d3524f118ca04f018e2b091db9780"}],"sha":"a09cd19dad4dba8f6b71a6fb2ef676d25b17697d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/commits/a09cd19dad4dba8f6b71a6fb2ef676d25b17697d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54384673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo","id":54384673,"login":"guillegmo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0Mzg0Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/commits/f45a63e2633d3524f118ca04f018e2b091db9780/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T05:02:53Z","email":"guillegmo@hotmail.com","name":"Guillermo Montoya Ocampo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T05:02:53Z","email":"guillegmo@hotmail.com","name":"Guillermo Montoya Ocampo"},"message":"fix(tutor): fuerza siempre la voz nativa de inglés en las lecturas de audio\n\nLa voz en español de este sistema pronuncia muy mal el inglés, así que las\nlecturas del Tutor IA (respuesta automática y botón \"escuchar\") ahora usan\nspeak(text, { lang: ''en'' }) para forzar un único idioma en vez de la\ndetección bilingüe por segmentos (pensada para las tarjetas de vocabulario,\ndonde sí alternan ejemplo en inglés / traducción en paréntesis).\n\nSe añade pickEnglishVoice() como bypass deliberado de pickVoicePair(): esa\nfunción exige encontrar una voz en español Y una en inglés del MISMO\ngénero para emparejarlas, y si ninguna voz en inglés instalada coincidía en\ngénero con una en español, el emparejamiento fallaba entero y devolvía\nenVoice: null — cayendo al comportamiento por defecto del navegador, que en\nun sistema con voces en español instaladas podía terminar leyendo en\nespañol pese al lang forzado. pickEnglishVoice() elige directamente la\nmejor voz en inglés disponible, sin depender de esa lógica de pareja.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0177VXzr6jYBDEDht9LCF4E5","tree":{"sha":"56cc6839230c305503e1fc3e3b616d576b522a49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/git/trees/56cc6839230c305503e1fc3e3b616d576b522a49"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/git/commits/f45a63e2633d3524f118ca04f018e2b091db9780","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54384673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo","id":54384673,"login":"guillegmo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0Mzg0Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo/appingles/commit/f45a63e2633d3524f118ca04f018e2b091db9780","node_id":"C_kwDOT5AOd9oAKGY0NWE2M2UyNjMzZDM1MjRmMTE4Y2EwNGYwMThlMmIwOTFkYjk3ODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo/appingles/commit/4cb0ce55a1add3d949f53a63a862837024f09a1b","sha":"4cb0ce55a1add3d949f53a63a862837024f09a1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/commits/4cb0ce55a1add3d949f53a63a862837024f09a1b"}],"sha":"f45a63e2633d3524f118ca04f018e2b091db9780","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/commits/f45a63e2633d3524f118ca04f018e2b091db9780"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54384673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo","id":54384673,"login":"guillegmo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0Mzg0Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/commits/4cb0ce55a1add3d949f53a63a862837024f09a1b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T05:02:30Z","email":"guillegmo@hotmail.com","name":"Guillermo Montoya Ocampo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T05:02:30Z","email":"guillegmo@hotmail.com","name":"Guillermo Montoya Ocampo"},"message":"feat(tutor): elimina el historial de conversación de Firestore\n\nEl Tutor IA ya no lee ni escribe una colección `conversations` por mensaje\n(GET /tutor/history eliminado). La memoria de la conversación vive solo en\nel estado del componente: el frontend manda los últimos turnos ya en\npantalla (role/content) en el body de cada request, y el backend los\nsanitiza (solo user/assistant, nunca system, con límite de longitud y\nventana de contexto) antes de pasarlos al modelo.\n\nSe pierde el historial al recargar o cambiar de modo — contrapartida\naceptada a cambio de dejar de leer/escribir Firestore en cada turno del\nchat.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0177VXzr6jYBDEDht9LCF4E5","tree":{"sha":"d674650e0af977bdf63c48b1fca590bc4483fff7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/git/trees/d674650e0af977bdf63c48b1fca590bc4483fff7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/git/commits/4cb0ce55a1add3d949f53a63a862837024f09a1b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54384673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo","id":54384673,"login":"guillegmo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0Mzg0Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo/appingles/commit/4cb0ce55a1add3d949f53a63a862837024f09a1b","node_id":"C_kwDOT5AOd9oAKDRjYjBjZTU1YTFhZGQzZDk0OWY1M2E2M2E4NjI4MzcwMjRmMDlhMWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo/appingles/commit/592ad146dd5b99aa89e9012acfaf639fb02d13b2","sha":"592ad146dd5b99aa89e9012acfaf639fb02d13b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/commits/592ad146dd5b99aa89e9012acfaf639fb02d13b2"}],"sha":"4cb0ce55a1add3d949f53a63a862837024f09a1b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/commits/4cb0ce55a1add3d949f53a63a862837024f09a1b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/54384673?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guillegmo","id":54384673,"login":"guillegmo","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU0Mzg0Njcz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guillegmo","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/commits/592ad146dd5b99aa89e9012acfaf639fb02d13b2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-02T05:01:47Z","email":"guillegmo@hotmail.com","name":"Guillermo Montoya Ocampo"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-02T05:01:47Z","email":"guillegmo@hotmail.com","name":"Guillermo Montoya Ocampo"},"message":"fix(review): calificar con quality < 3 ya no revienta con 500\n\nrecordResult solo leía `progress` cuando quality >= 3, pero el objeto de\nrespuesta devolvía progress.totalXp sin importar el resultado. Calificar\nuna tarjeta como \"no la sabía\" o \"difícil\" (quality 0-2) — el caso más\ncomún al repasar — dejaba progress en null y explotaba con TypeError,\nprovocando un 500 real en POST /review/:id/result.\n\nSe lee progress siempre (transaccional, sin escribirlo si quality < 3, así\nque el XP no cambia). Cubierto con dos tests de regresión: quality baja con\ny sin progreso previo en Firestore.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0177VXzr6jYBDEDht9LCF4E5","tree":{"sha":"e27f29d56a6e8da0b0dd1c57eecfc63d80517a52","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/git/trees/e27f29d56a6e8da0b0dd1c57eecfc63d80517a52"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guillegmo/appingles/git/commits/592ad146dd5b99aa8