hub.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vercel%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/melissa-pd/design-playground/commits/f1db2bcae7789babc0fc7c1c64e05bd344574adf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T02:48:58Z","email":"vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vercel"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T02:48:58Z","email":"vercel[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Vercel"},"message":"Install and Configure Vercel Web Analytics\n\nImplemented Vercel Web Analytics for Next.js App Router project\n\nSummary:\nSuccessfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart\n\nChanges Made:\n\n1. Package Installation:\n   - Installed @vercel/analytics package using npm\n   - Updated package.json with new dependency\n   - Updated package-lock.json with dependency tree\n\n2. Code Integration:\n   - Modified initiatives/headway/app/layout.tsx:\n     * Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from \"@vercel/analytics/next\";`\n     * Added <Analytics /> component inside the <body> tag\n     * Preserved existing code structure and formatting\n     * Maintained proper Next.js App Router patterns\n\n3. Verification:\n   - Build completed successfully (npm run build)\n   - No new linting errors introduced in layout.tsx\n   - TypeScript compilation successful\n   - Static pages generated correctly\n\nImplementation Details:\n- Used the Next.js App Router specific implementation (@vercel/analytics/next)\n- Analytics component placed at the end of the body tag as per best practices\n- All existing functionality preserved\n- Code follows existing project conventions\n\nThe Analytics compo