"sha":"0410d1c9d4b1d024921cfc43da10a3d442ea95b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/0410d1c9d4b1d024921cfc43da10a3d442ea95b7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/6cfeb4301bb963f594639a51f5baa7b05673e6bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T03:55:20Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T13:05:23Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"feat: roles scope what you can do, not which solutions you can see\n\nEvery org role now reaches every satellite. What a role may do inside\none is declared per screen and per action; what it sees is a set of\nsections added to the shared screen.\n\nBefore this, three satellites each declared a satellite-level `roles`\nceiling and the registry declared it again. Finance could not open Fleet\nor Depots at all, engineering could not open Depots, platform could not\nopen Orders -- a role bounced off a whole solution with no way to learn\nwhy. Hiding the solution was never the requirement; gating the\noperations inside it was.\n\n  registry + all three manifests: satellite-level `roles` removed\n  orders.create / update / attach / edit -> engineering\n  orders.delete -> leadership\n  orders.approve (finance/leadership), depots.close (platform) unchanged\n\nEvery write names a role in BOTH the manifest and the registry. The\nmanifest is the check a person clicking the button meets; the registry\n`tools` entry governs the agent/MCP/public path, and a mismatch would\nlet a model propose a write the form refuses.\n\nNaming all of them matters more than it looks. With no satellite ceiling\nthere is nothing behind an action that declares nothing, so silence now\nmeans \"any role\" rather than \"the satellite''s roles\". A code review\ncaught that the first cut of this change gated only orders.create and\nthereby opened update, attach and delete to every role -- a platform\nprincipal could have deleted an order it previously could not open. Two\ntests lock it: one per write, and one that fails if a NEW write is added\nwithout a gate.\n\nRole-specific sections, additive and never subtractive:\n\n  finance      a graph   -- value by status, spare capacity by region,\n                            distance by depot\n  platform     metrics   -- throughput, estate spread, headroom\n  engineering  a table   -- work queue, service queue, capacity pressure\n\nA principal holding none sees precisely the screen that existed before.\nThe satellite decides this rather than the hub, because a hub filter\nwould mean the figures had already crossed the wire to be discarded, and\na number nobody was entitled to is not made safe by not drawing it.\nExternal principals get none of it: `authorize` skips the role check for\npartners, and the public façade would otherwise project the work queue''s\npriority and dueBy as a brokered collection.\n\nThe platform sections are a KeyValueList, not StatTiles, because the hub\nheadlines the first four StatTiles on a summary screen. As tiles they\nchanged the front page: a platform principal saw \"Currencies\" as the\nfourth figure on the Orders card while everyone else saw three.\n\nAlso: signing in and out. The logout route existed and worked; nothing\nin the shell reached it. The first cut offered a Sign out button only\nwhen a session existed -- which on the dev stub is never, and the stub is\nhow compose runs by default, so the common path still had no way out and\nno way IN either (the login route is reachable only through a middleware\nredirect the stub deliberately skips). The bar now always offers one or\nthe other. The route moved GET -> POST and checks the origin: POST alone\ndoes not stop this, because a cross-origin form POST is a simple request\nany page can auto-submit. `readSession` is memoised per request with\nReact `cache`, since the layout asks twice.\n\ne2e: `table.r-table` and `.r-chart svg[role=application]` are no longer\nunique on a screen, so both get a helper taking the first -- the shared\none, guaranteed first by the additive invariant.\n\nAnd playwright.config.ts now loads `.env`. `docker compose` reads it; a\nhost-side `pnpm test:e2e` did not, so two tests that skip screen\ncomposition when PORTAL_MODEL_PROVIDER is ollama could never fire and\nfailed instead. That one line is why main looked like it had nine broken\ntests.\n\nVerified:\n  pnpm verify:ci  green -- unit 1160, integration 160, python 47,\n                  C# 41 + 29\n  e2e             91 passed, 0 failed, 4 skipped\n                  (main baseline was 9 failed / 84 passed)\n  mutation        re-opening orders.delete, leaking sections to external\n                  principals, leaking the platform section to all roles,\n                  dropping the logout origin check, and putting the\n                  platform metrics back as StatTiles -- each caught\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01A9YJ3SvhfYFnJ8yCHQofh7","tree":{"sha":"d2d1bffa7f5c98d11a6dab03564bfa505d1f3dff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/d2d1bffa7f5c98d11a6dab03564bfa505d1f3dff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/6cfeb4301bb963f594639a51f5baa7b05673e6bd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/6cfeb4301bb963f594639a51f5baa7b05673e6bd","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDZjZmViNDMwMWJiOTYzZjU5NDYzOWE1MWY1YmFhN2IwNTY3M2U2YmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/ece22bc07bcf03314c528663804d3dcf4afc1ea9","sha":"ece22bc07bcf03314c528663804d3dcf4afc1ea9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/ece22bc07bcf0