"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/2d2e6747bc9e3863e08b9e2a38fe17b18e104736","sha":"2d2e6747bc9e3863e08b9e2a38fe17b18e104736","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/2d2e6747bc9e3863e08b9e2a38fe17b18e104736"}],"sha":"b5df126ec03db1206c171a76894b7927dc695d98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/b5df126ec03db1206c171a76894b7927dc695d98"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/2d2e6747bc9e3863e08b9e2a38fe17b18e104736/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T23:14:42Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T23:14:42Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Say in PLAN.md what the code now does\n\nCorrected one commit ago and stale again by the end of it: PLAN.md read \"no\n`thinking` parameter is sent\", which described the state between the two\ncommits on this branch rather than either of them. It sends\n`{type: \"disabled\"}`, and the distinction is the whole point — omitting the\nparameter leaves adaptive thinking on.\n\nThird time this week a comment has gone stale faster than the code it\ndescribes, and the second time in one branch.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cac6f015cbcd113595ab1d84e0d1d837118b2858","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/cac6f015cbcd113595ab1d84e0d1d837118b2858"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/2d2e6747bc9e3863e08b9e2a38fe17b18e104736","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/2d2e6747bc9e3863e08b9e2a38fe17b18e104736","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDJkMmU2NzQ3YmM5ZTM4NjNlMDhiOWUyYTM4ZmUxN2IxOGUxMDQ3MzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/cfe079a99b894c3d1c32887458ea0e6cb8c7730f","sha":"cfe079a99b894c3d1c32887458ea0e6cb8c7730f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/cfe079a99b894c3d1c32887458ea0e6cb8c7730f"}],"sha":"2d2e6747bc9e3863e08b9e2a38fe17b18e104736","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/2d2e6747bc9e3863e08b9e2a38fe17b18e104736"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/cfe079a99b894c3d1c32887458ea0e6cb8c7730f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T23:11:37Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T23:11:37Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Turn thinking off, rather than assuming that deleting a line did\n\nThe review caught the central claim of this branch being wrong, and it was.\n\nDeleting `thinking: { type: \"adaptive\" }` does not stop the model thinking.\n`claude-opus-5` thinks adaptively when the parameter is absent — measured\ndirectly: a bare request comes back with a `thinking` block and non-zero\n`thinking_tokens`. So the first commit here changed nothing at all except on\nthe models that used to 400, and the evidence offered for it (\"Opus composes\n2/2 without it\") was consistent with thinking still running, because it was.\n\n`thinking: { type: \"disabled\" }` says what was actually wanted. Checked before\nusing it: accepted by `claude-haiku-4-5` as well as `claude-opus-5`, so it does\nnot reintroduce the version problem that started this, and composition still\nworks 3 times in 3 with it off. What makes a composed screen trustworthy here\nis the strict `render_screen` schema and the grounding validator, not a\nreasoning budget.\n\n**The failure log is narrowed to the message.** Everywhere else this codebase\nis careful about what reaches a log — `withoutCredentials` strips userinfo from\na URL, the startup line counts opted-out tenants rather than naming them — and\nan `Error` carries a cause chain, headers and the request that made it, while\nthis catch also sees tool failures on a path PLAN.md says regulated data\ntravels. Not a complete answer, and the comment says so: `ollama.ts` puts up to\n500 characters of an upstream body into its message deliberately.\n\nAlso from the review, all documentation that had gone stale against the code:\nPLAN.md still specified adaptive thinking and \"a token budget is rejected\noutright\", which is the sentence this branch deleted — the next person adding a\nmodel client would have followed it straight back into the 400. DEMO.md said\nunsetting `PORTAL_MODEL_PROVIDER` gets you the hosted model, which loses *every*\nassistant beat without a key rather than just beat 6, and claimed the stack runs\nthe local model \"by default\" when `.env.example` ships that commented out and\ncalls it opt-in, never a fallback.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cf423231c4a954251ce6602cf77799d706834072","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/cf423231c4a954251ce6602cf77799d706834072"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/cfe079a99b894c3d1c32887458ea0e6cb8c7730f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/cfe079a99b894c3d1c32887458ea0e6cb8c7730f","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKGNmZTA3OWE5OWI4OTRjM2QxYzMyODg3NDU4ZWEwZTZjYjhjNzczMGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/7a2060ab334e1d7602841653b721ef4a47e6955e","sha":"7a2060ab334e1d7602841653b721ef4a47e6955e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/7a2060ab334e1d7602841653b721ef4a47e6955e"}],"sha":"cfe079a99b894c3d1c32887458ea0e6cb8c7730f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/cfe079a99b894c3d1c32887458ea0e6cb8c7730f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/7a2060ab334e1d7602841653b721ef4a47e6955e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T22:58:22Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T22:58:22Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Stop asking for adaptive thinking, and log why a turn failed\n\nTwo files of behaviour. #44 was four times this size and most of it was\nspeculative.\n\n**Adaptive thinking is gone rather than gated.** `thinking: { type: \"adaptive\" }`\nis a 4.6-and-later feature, and asked of anything older the API refuses the\nwhole request — which is why pointing the portal at `claude-haiku-4-5` made\nevery single turn fail. The alternative was a predicate that reads versions out\nof model names across two naming eras; a review found it misreading any name\nwith a prefix, and a wrong guess there silently removes thinking from a model\nthat wanted it. Deleting the parameter deletes that entire class of bug.\n\nVerified it costs nothing before removing it: `claude-opus-5` composes the home\nscreen 2 times in 2 without it. What makes a composed screen trustworthy here\nis the strict schema and the grounding validator, not the model''s reasoning\nbudget.\n\n**An unexpected turn failure now leaves a trace.** The route catches, flushes\nthe audit and answers one sentence — right for the caller, and it was also all\nanyone got. The API had been saying \"adaptive thinking is not supported on this\nmodel\" for an afternoon with no way to see it: the audit records the calls a\nturn made, never why it died. A sentence to the caller, the error to the\noperator.\n\nThe deployment stays on the local model. Measured on the way through, and\nrecorded in `docs/DEMO.md` rather than in this message: the composed-home beat\nis 0/3 on `qwen2.5:7b` and 3/3 on `claude-opus-5`, and raising the turn budget\nto 20 did not move the local model at all — it is a capability limit, not a\nbudget one.\n\nThat is also why there is no turn-budget setting here. It was in #44 to rescue\nHaiku''s composition, it did not (3 in 6), and it does nothing for the local\nmodel either. A knob that turns nothing is the same mistake as a declaration\nnobody reads, and this repository has been bitten by that twice this week.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e00856c5085fc7298f7e0f567354a4e6b91688d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/e00856c5085fc7298f7e0f567354a4e6b91688d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/7a2060ab334e1d7602841653b721ef4a47e6955e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committe