","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/5427d3343844bc5e7a006483f0cba985e92a590b","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDU0MjdkMzM0Mzg0NGJjNWU3YTAwNjQ4M2YwY2JhOTg1ZTkyYTU5MGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/a594898c6922b58485de89e8891047105780f8ef","sha":"a594898c6922b58485de89e8891047105780f8ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/a594898c6922b58485de89e8891047105780f8ef"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/11974b4f53438b2459c3424eac9255520252aadd","sha":"11974b4f53438b2459c3424eac9255520252aadd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/11974b4f53438b2459c3424eac9255520252aadd"}],"sha":"5427d3343844bc5e7a006483f0cba985e92a590b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/5427d3343844bc5e7a006483f0cba985e92a590b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/60ba37cb1ab7478e8d58ff59b35d7ce86939eca0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T13:45:43Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T13:45:43Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Name the ground in a contrast failure, and stop overclaiming again\n\nReview follow-ups, all in the test file. No colour changed.\n\nA failure said `success 4.43:1 on its own 16% tint` and, now that two grounds\nare folded through one comparison, no longer said *which* ground was worst —\nwhich is the one thing a maintainer needs, because the card and the page are\nretuned differently. It now ends `over --bg`.\n\nThe inline comment said the two grounds were \"both grounds a badge can actually\nland on today\", six lines under a docblock explaining that a badge in an alert,\ntoast or table head lands on `--surface-sunken` today. This commit''s own stated\npoint was to stop the comment reading as a guarantee it does not make, and that\nline put the overclaim straight back.\n\nAnd the sunken band''s top is 4.49, not 4.48 — contoso light danger is 4.4887,\nwhich the file''s own `toFixed(2)` rounds up. I had read the figure off a list\ntruncated at fourteen of the fifteen rows. The count and the 4.02 floor were\nright.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4f9c74b71f8d9889ba9cccc02b0a6fd8c945c3f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/4f9c74b71f8d9889ba9cccc02b0a6fd8c945c3f2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/60ba37cb1ab7478e8d58ff59b35d7ce86939eca0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/60ba37cb1ab7478e8d58ff59b35d7ce86939eca0","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDYwYmEzN2NiMWFiNzQ3OGU4ZDU4ZmY1OWIzNWQ3Y2U4NjkzOWVjYTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/494809b2097c773c9cb02e17384dec1dc3e6dc90","sha":"494809b2097c773c9cb02e17384dec1dc3e6dc90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/494809b2097c773c9cb02e17384dec1dc3e6dc90"}],"sha":"60ba37cb1ab7478e8d58ff59b35d7ce86939eca0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/60ba37cb1ab7478e8d58ff59b35d7ce86939eca0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/494809b2097c773c9cb02e17384dec1dc3e6dc90/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T13:37:59Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T13:37:59Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Check a badge on the page, not only on a card\n\nThe contrast guard composited a badge''s wash onto `--surface` alone. But the\nwash is mixed with `transparent`, so what sits behind a badge is whichever\ncontainer it lands in — and nothing in the catalog constrains that. A satellite\ncan nest a `Badge` anywhere its screen has room for one, with no hub change and\nno review, so `--bg` is not a hypothetical ground.\n\nFive tone/scheme pairs cleared 4.5:1 on the card and did not on the page:\ncontoso warning 4.34, contoso info 4.36, default warning 4.42, default success\n4.43, contoso success 4.47 — all light-scheme, since the dark palettes sit on\ngrounds that are close together.\n\nDarkened in HLS as before, so hue and saturation are unchanged; the largest\nshift is four points of lightness and no colour reads differently. The guard\nnow takes the worst of the two grounds rather than the first, because a tone\nthat passes on a card and fails on the page is a tone that fails.\n\nMutation-tested against the previous commit''s own values: `--tone-success`\n`#1e7449` cleared the `--surface`-only check at 4.59 and fails here at 4.43,\nwhich is exactly the case the second ground exists to catch.\n\n`--surface-sunken` is still not covered and the comment says so with the\nnumbers — fifteen pairs between 4.02 and 4.48. Closing that one is retuning\ncolour across three palettes in both schemes, which is a design change rather\nthan a test fix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8672a889e6688d9e154f90273927add84e34098f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/8672a889e6688d9e154f90273927add84e34098f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/494809b2097c773c9cb02e17384dec1dc3e6dc90","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"logi