ps://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/441a4d1c3c08541e9e2d839478e4336aac47881b","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDQ0MWE0ZDFjM2MwODU0MWU5ZTJkODM5NDc4ZTQzMzZhYWM0Nzg4MWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/25dadb234ae84c0f8caa0f8a519ecf3b924e7ac5","sha":"25dadb234ae84c0f8caa0f8a519ecf3b924e7ac5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/25dadb234ae84c0f8caa0f8a519ecf3b924e7ac5"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/eda2bd7f68e67f3ddb1cf873440818251f9b1123","sha":"eda2bd7f68e67f3ddb1cf873440818251f9b1123","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/eda2bd7f68e67f3ddb1cf873440818251f9b1123"}],"sha":"441a4d1c3c08541e9e2d839478e4336aac47881b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/441a4d1c3c08541e9e2d839478e4336aac47881b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/eda2bd7f68e67f3ddb1cf873440818251f9b1123/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T18:18:18Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T18:18:18Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Fix what the review found, including a test that fails for free users\n\nThe sharpest finding lands where the cost conversation did. The composed\nhome''s e2e had no local-provider skip, unlike its sibling — and\n`assistantConfigured()` answers yes under a local model — so the run that\n`.env.example` documents as costing nothing gained a *failing* test\nrather than a skipped one. The two documents disagreed with the code, and\nthe code was wrong.\n\n`docker compose restart hub` does not apply an environment change. I\nsaid \"a restart rather than a rebuild\" for the brand in the runbook, the\ncompose file, `.env.example` and the README, and measured it here: after\n`restart` there is no brand attribute; after `up -d` there is. The\nregistry beat is unaffected — a bind mount is re-read on restart — which\nis why conflating them was easy and wrong.\n\n`PORTAL_BRAND` was unvalidated, and an unmatched attribute selects\nnothing, so `PORTAL_BRAND=Contoso` rendered the default palette while\nlooking configured. It fails at startup now with the accepted values\nnamed. And the alternate palette outscored dark mode while defining no\nchart tokens, so a branded portal in dark mode painted pastel series on a\nnear-white card.\n\nTwo on the composed home: under StrictMode the first fetch''s abort landed\nin the shared catch and tore the section out mid-load, and `aria-live` on\nthe whole section announced an entire dashboard unprompted. Also written\ndown: `/api/agent` does not observe `request.signal`, so a visitor who\nnavigates away mid-composition still pays for that turn.\n\nMy runbook claimed `docker compose down -v` removes volumes and costs a\ntwo-minute cold build. This compose file declares no volumes and images\nsurvive `down`. Rewritten.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"e89db0cab6c5d0ef2c1f3ab2e798493626d30151","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/e89db0cab6c5d0ef2c1f3ab2e798493626d30151"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/eda2bd7f68e67f3ddb1cf873440818251f9b1123","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/eda2bd7f68e67f3ddb1cf873440818251f9b1123","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKGVkYTJiZDdmNjhlNjdmM2RkYjFjZjg3MzQ0MDgxODI1MWY5YjExMjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/80298912dd81a83649b5ff7c9d1ac62173c9a9f0","sha":"80298912dd81a83649b5ff7c9d1ac62173c9a9f0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/80298912dd81a83649b5ff7c9d1ac62173c9a9f0"}],"sha":"eda2bd7f68e67f3ddb1cf873440818251f9b1123","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/eda2bd7f68e67f3ddb1cf873440818251f9b1123"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/80298912dd81a83649b5ff7c9d1ac62173c9a9f0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T17:50:10Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T17:50:10Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Build the demo: a home nobody wrote, a brand that flips, a runbook\n\nThe last M2 item and the two things a pilot pitch needs.\n\n**The composed home.** The agent reads across every solution an account\ncan see and composes a screen from what it finds — citing orders, fleet\nand depots, which is a TypeScript, a Python and a C# service in one view\nthat none of them could have produced. It is the clearest answer to \"what\nis the hub for beyond consistent styling\".\n\nAdditive, as PLAN.md requires. The launcher is server-rendered and\ncomplete on its own — 13 ms, measured — and the composed screen fills in\nafterwards or does not. With the assistant off, a tenant opted out or the\nmodel unreachable, the page is exactly what it was and says nothing about\na missing feature.\n\n**The brand.** \"Change a token here and every satellite''s screens change\nwith it\" was true and unprovable: one palette, no way to swap it.\n`PORTAL_BRAND` selects one at request time, so rebranding is a container\nrestart rather than a rebuild, and all three satellites wear it without\nbeing redeployed or told. The test reads the *computed* colour, because a\nbrand that is set and changes nothing would pass an attribute check.\n\n**And the runbook found a real bug in its own headline beat.** It says\nedit `config/satellites.yaml`, restart the hub, watch the portal change,\nzero deployments. It did not work: `COPY . .` bakes the registry into the\nimage, so the container re-read its own stale copy. The loudest claim\nthis design makes was false in the one setup anyone would try it in, and\nI would have demonstrated that live. The registry is mounted read-only\nnow, and a test asserts the mount.\n\nAlso moved the launcher''s inline styles into the stylesheet. \"The hub\nowns every pixel\" reads poorly when the hub''s own markup carries style\nattributes.\n\nRecorded in PLAN.md: the composed home asks on every visit, with no\ncache, which is slow and billable per view.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"99b93035854a361056a89f2c92592e261a845fd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/99b93035854a361056a89f2c92592e261a845fd3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/80298912dd81a83649b5ff7c9d1ac62173c9a9f0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/80298912