humblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/38a043c2d44b9bb5c21c4029e603912b75c13256/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:02:39Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T16:02:39Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Repair two blocks the rebase cut through\n\nBoth conflicts were additive — #35''s conditional-visibility work and this\nbranch''s upload work touched the same files without touching the same\nlines — but the conflict boundary landed mid-expression twice, leaving\n`optionValues` and one `it` block unterminated. Kept both sides and\nclosed them.\n\nCaught by typecheck rather than by reading the diff, which is the honest\naccount: a resolution that compiles is not the same as a resolution that\nis right, so the full suite ran after — 89 e2e, all four services.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"c764a39920c42630cbcc6bc30dbf938d656bdb5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/c764a39920c42630cbcc6bc30dbf938d656bdb5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/38a043c2d44b9bb5c21c4029e603912b75c13256","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/38a043c2d44b9bb5c21c4029e603912b75c13256","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDM4YTA0M2MyZDQ0YjliYjVjMjFjNDAyOWU2MDM5MTJiNzVjMTMyNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/d076ef85ab6c05b0ad5d3bae2b15f1084f80819a","sha":"d076ef85ab6c05b0ad5d3bae2b15f1084f80819a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/d076ef85ab6c05b0ad5d3bae2b15f1084f80819a"}],"sha":"38a043c2d44b9bb5c21c4029e603912b75c13256","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/38a043c2d44b9bb5c21c4029e603912b75c13256"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/d076ef85ab6c05b0ad5d3bae2b15f1084f80819a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T15:47:34Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T15:58:00Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Fix the upload path: a denial of service, a blind audit, a caller-chosen limit\n\nThree high findings, all mine, and the first is the worst thing I have\nwritten in this project.\n\n`request.formData()` was unbounded. `withinUploadLimit` read only\n`content-length`, and `Number(null) === 0` passes it — so a chunked\nrequest with no declared length was buffered in full before the 413. The\nreview measured 600 MB taking the hub from 694 MiB to 1.99 GiB. I\nre-measured 300 MB after the fix: refused in 0.17 seconds, memory flat at\n183 to 193 MiB, sender stopped rather than drained.\n\nWhat makes it worse is that `readBounded` has existed since the chunked\nbypass on #15 and exists precisely for this. I wrote a new path and did\nnot use it.\n\nThe audit was blind to uploads. `params: payload` handed a `FormData` to\nthe digest, `Object.entries` on one is empty, and so every upload hashed\nidentically — to each other and to an empty payload. The one control that\nanswers \"which records did this touch\" recorded nothing about the file.\nTwo different documents now produce two different digests; I checked.\n\nAnd the 10 MB ceiling was chosen by the caller''s own `content-type`\nrather than the action''s declaration, so any action could be posted as\nmultipart to get the larger limit. My comment claimed the opposite — that\nreading it from the request stopped a caller picking the limit by naming\nan action — which has the direction exactly backwards. The manifest is\nresolved first now, multipart on an action with no file parameter is 415,\nand an unknown or unauthorized action is refused before a byte is read.\n\nAlso from the review: the public façade''s `resolveOperation` did not\nmirror the catalog''s file exclusion, so an operation hidden from the\nlisting was still reachable by URL; the attach form was drawn for\nexternal principals the hub answers 404 to; `FileUpload` still rendered\n\"this file will not be sent\"; the multipart builder turned a `DateRange`\ninto the literal \"[object Object]\"; filenames and content types were\nstored verbatim; and an optional file parameter was published to agents\nas a plain string, which `checkArguments` accepts — so \"an agent cannot\nset this\" was a description rather than a boundary.\n\nThe action route had no tests at all, which is how both the unbounded\nparse and the limit selection shipped. It has six now, and the review\nchecked they fail against the code they replaced.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"44d1aa94d511eb345f5003feca022f4cd0714db6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/44d1aa94d511eb345f5003feca022f4cd0714db6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/d076ef85ab6c05b0ad5d3bae2b15f1084f80819a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/d076ef85ab6c05b0ad5d3bae2b15f1084f80819a","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKGQwNzZlZjg1YWI2YzA1YjBhZDVkM2JhZTJiMTVmMTA4NGY4MDgxOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/f23d2431b4423310f46675d1e7bed8a51b251f4e","sha":"f23d2431b4423310f46675d1e7bed8a51b251f4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/f23d2431b4423310f46675d1e7bed8a51b251f4e"}],"sha":"d076ef85ab6c05b0ad5d3bae2b15f1084f80819a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/d076ef85ab6c05b0ad5d3bae2b15f1084f80819a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/f23d2431b4423310f46675d1e7bed8a51b251f4e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T15:20:27Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T15:58:00Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Let a file cross the hub\n\n`FileUpload` has been in the catalog since M1. It rendered an input and\nhad nowhere to send what it collected — a component whose existence\nimplied a capability the protocol did not have. PLAN.md listed it as a\nknown limit and it was the last one a satellite team would hit in week\none.\n\nThe declaration side is a new `file` parameter type, and the interesting\npart is what the other projections do with it.\n\nThe agent surface refuses it: an action requiring a file is skipped, with\na reason, because no model can produce bytes. Offering the tool would put\na write on the surface that every call must fail, and a refusal at the\nsatellite reads as a broken integration rather than a deliberate\nboundary. An *optional* file is not a reason to skip — the rest of the\naction still works and the field is described as one a person fills in.\n\nThe public façade refuses it too, and differently: an operation carrying\na file is not published at all, even where a platform-team mapping named\nit. The façade is a JSON contract. Publishing without the field would\ndescribe a call that always fails validation; publishing with it would\ndescribe a call a partner cannot make. Absent is the only honest answer\nuntil the façade grows an upload of its own, which is a versioned change.\n\nTransport is multipart, browser to hub to satellite, with the satellite\nstoring what arrives — satellites own their data and the hub stays\nstateless. Uploads get their own ceiling: 256 KB is \"far past any form\"\nprecisely because a form is text, and a scanned purchase order is not.\nTen megabytes, checked from the header before reading and from the parsed\ntotal after, because a chunked request declares nothing.\n\nNo new dependency. Express has no multipart parser, but Node''s own\n`Request` does, so the raw body goes straight into one.\n\nTwo things the browser taught me. The encoding follows the form''s shape\nrather than what the user picked: deciding it from the files actually\nchosen meant an untouched upload posted JSON, and a satellite reading\nJSON on an action expecting multipart cannot tell \"no document\" from\n\"wrong content type\" — so it answered with a general failure where it\nmeant to point at the field. And `content-type` is left unset for\nmultipart, because the browser appends the boundary it generated and a\nheader written by hand declares one that does not match.\n\nThe e2e initially depended on a seeded order having no attachment, then\nfailed differently on the second run because its own first run had\nattached one. It creates its own order now.\n\nVerified beyond the tests: an 11 MB upload answers 413 and a small one\nstill works, both through the hub.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"8e7a706bbbfce88d9772be8f331e433bd5ebe286","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/8e7a706bbbfce88d9772be8f331e433bd5ebe286"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/f23d2431b4423310f46675d1e7bed8a51b251f4e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/f23d2431b4423310f46675d1e7bed8a51b251f4e","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKGYyM2QyNDMxYjQ0MjMzMTBmNDY2NzVkMWU3YmVkOGE1MWIyNTFmNGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/1a4c6fcaf5fa54924c72c150e291dff018bfa008","sha":"1a4c6fcaf5fa54924c72c150e291dff018bfa008","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/1a4c6fcaf5fa54924c72c150e291dff018bfa008"}],"sha":"f23d2431b4423310f46675d1e7bed8a51b251f4e","url":"https://api.githu