i.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/ad068dd3117a92c7c119b721b3caf7f9822a22cc","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKGFkMDY4ZGQzMTE3YTkyYzdjMTE5YjcyMWIzY2FmN2Y5ODIyYTIyY2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/43e0f4bb2af53824d42e9e2788c7793e561b7a07","sha":"43e0f4bb2af53824d42e9e2788c7793e561b7a07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/43e0f4bb2af53824d42e9e2788c7793e561b7a07"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/68545c62d87dd04a84d8f963858e1b5bbee5aefc","sha":"68545c62d87dd04a84d8f963858e1b5bbee5aefc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/68545c62d87dd04a84d8f963858e1b5bbee5aefc"}],"sha":"ad068dd3117a92c7c119b721b3caf7f9822a22cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/ad068dd3117a92c7c119b721b3caf7f9822a22cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/c756db6a7fc59859102adab3599350d365cf1137/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T02:21:01Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T02:21:01Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Fix the provider''s translation, and stop measuring the wrong thing\n\nThe review found a bug I would not have found, and it explains more than\nitself. qwen2.5''s prompt template is\n`{{ if .Content }}{{ .Content }}{{- else if .ToolCalls }}` — an *else*.\nMy provider sent an assistant turn''s prose and its tool calls together,\nso one word of preamble deleted every tool call from the model''s own\nhistory. Confirmed by reading the template out of `ollama show`. The\nprose is dropped now and the calls kept: grounding cites the call id, and\nthe preamble was filler.\n\nThree more of mine, all high or medium:\n\nThe fallback tool-call id counter lived in the client closure, but a\nclient is built per request while the conversation spans requests. Turn\ntwo re-minted `local_1`, the loop read an old call as answered, and the\ntool never ran. Minted off the conversation now.\n\n`isAgentEnabled()` gated on `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, so the quickstart this\nPR documents — `PORTAL_MODEL_PROVIDER=ollama docker compose up -d`, no\nkey — answered 404 and showed no assistant. The feature only worked if\nyou also supplied the paid key it exists to avoid. Verified fixed: with\nno key in the container at all, the portal answers \"There are 2 pending\norders.\"\n\nAn unrecognised provider fell through to the paid client, so\n`PORTAL_MODEL_PROVIDER=ollma` billed silently. It throws now.\n\nAlso: `tool_name` carried the call id rather than the tool''s name; a\nstopped daemon threw a bare `fetch failed` while the helpful message was\nreserved for the case where it *was* running; no `done_reason: \"length\"`\ncheck, so a generation truncated mid-tool-call would have been made with\nhalf its arguments; a trailing slash in the URL produced `//api/chat`;\nand `host.docker.internal` is Docker Desktop only.\n\n**And I corrected a claim I made confidently and wrongly.** I said\ncomposition worked locally on one branch and failed on another, and\nexplained it with `temperature: 0` determinism. The branch it \"worked\"\non has no local provider in its compose file — it was talking to\nAnthropic. I compared the hosted model to the local one and called it a\nprompt-sensitivity finding. The skip''s comment now says only what was\nmeasured: driven directly at qwen2.5 with these fixes in place, it still\nruns out of turns.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"5a8976ead99e4017ec658d41d136f626669a55d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/5a8976ead99e4017ec658d41d136f626669a55d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/c756db6a7fc59859102adab3599350d365cf1137","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/c756db6a7fc59859102adab3599350d365cf1137","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKGM3NTZkYjZhN2ZjNTk4NTkxMDJhZGFiMzU5OTM1MGQzNjVjZjExMzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/d26ce79040900345018c02f95210a5f78635d3a3","sha":"d26ce79040900345018c02f95210a5f78635d3a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/d26ce79040900345018c02f95210a5f78635d3a3"}],"sha":"c756db6a7fc59859102adab3599350d365cf1137","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/c756db6a7fc59859102adab3599350d365cf1137"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/68545c62d87dd04a84d8f963858e1b5bbee5aefc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T01:53:29Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T01:53:29Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Fix what the review found, including a parity failure I introduced\n\nThe high one is mine and it is exactly what three SDKs were meant to\nprevent: I taught C# about `string[]` and left Python behind. Its\n`ParamType` was a hand-written Literal, so a Python satellite could not\ndeclare the new type at all — and `action_param` refused `choices` on\nanything but `\"string\"`, which would have refused it twice over. Python\ngenerates `ParamType` from `ActionParamSchema` now, which is the rule\nthat file''s own docstring states and that I broke the first time the\nvocabulary moved.\n\nThe C# collision guard was too narrow. It covered the four protocol\nenums; the twenty-odd catalog-derived ones run through the same\ncollision-prone `pascal()` and had no guard at all. Both are covered now,\nand the protocol enum lists are hoisted so the members block and the\n`ToWire` switch cannot drift apart.\n\nThe public façade''s copy of the param conversion had **no tests**.\nDeleting its `string[]` branch made every partner-sent list fail type\nchecking on the externally published contract, silently. Mutation-tested:\nit now fails.\n\nThree of my comments asserted the opposite of what the code does. They\nsaid \"an agent cannot send it — `ActionParamSchema` has no array type\",\nwhich was true when I wrote them and is the thing this PR removes. The\nmerge in the update route survives for a different reason: `tags` is\noptional, so absent still has to mean \"leave them alone\" rather than\n\"clear them\". My own commit message on the previous change said the old\nthing too.\n\nAlso: reads now reject an array explicitly. Nothing can reach that branch\ntoday — screen params have no type — but it is one reordering away from\n`String([\"a\",\"b\"])` becoming `\"a,b\"`, which is a different request that\nlooks like a successful one.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"ff963c7f4031674105d206e0257ba7cb02264c89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/ff963c7f4031674105d206e0257ba7cb02264c89"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/68545c62d87dd04a84d8f963858e1b5bbee5aefc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/68545c62d87dd04a84d8f963858e1b5bbee5aefc","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDY4NTQ1YzYyZDg3ZGQwNGE4NGQ4Zjk2Mzg1OGUxYjViYmVlNWFlZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/a7e3413244f152be839a38fe2c669e39e8eb8300","sha":"a7e3413244f152be839a38fe2c669e39e8eb8300","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/a7e3413244f152be839a38fe2c669e39e8eb8300"}],"sha":"68545c62d87dd04a84d8f963858e1b5bbee5aefc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/68545c62d87dd04a84d8f963858e1b5bbee5aefc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/d26ce79040900345018c02f95210a5f78635d3a3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T01:38:48Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T01:38:48Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Say accurately why composition is skipped on a local model\n\nNot \"a 7B model cannot do this\". It can — three times out of three on one\nbranch. On another, with `tags` added to an unrelated tool''s schema, it\nfailed three out of three. The provider runs at `temperature: 0`, so\nthat is deterministic per prompt rather than flaky: the tool list changed,\nand the model''s path through it changed with it.\n\nWhich is worse than flaky, because it looks stable until something\nunrelated moves. The skip stands; the reason it gives now matches what\nwas measured.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"ef103c5d57420379f3f4915bc96c66726316fd37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/ef103c5d57420379f3f4915bc96c66726316fd37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/d26ce79040900345018c02f95210a5f78635d3a3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/d26ce79040900345018c02f95210a5f78635d3a3","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKGQyNmNlNzkwNDA5MDAzNDUwMThjMDJmOTUyMTBhNWY3ODYzNWQzYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/74689576a76b013c85651937dd5e2bb695f3bf09","sha":"74689576a76b013c85651937dd5e2bb695f3bf09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/74689576a76b013c85651937dd5e2bb695f3bf09"}],"sha":"d26ce79040900345018c02f95210a5f78635d3a3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/d26ce79040900345018c02f95210a5f78635d3a3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/52f8a05d39b2bedf0ce47f46cbe7d505491b3269/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T01:27:58Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T01:27:58Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Keep the conversation while you walk around the portal\n\nAsk a question, click into an order, and the thread was gone.\n\nThe panel is mounted in the layout, so client-side navigation would have\nleft it alone. But the renderer''s `Link` is a real anchor and an action''s\n`navigate` is a real navigation, both deliberately: deep links, the back\nbutton and copyable URLs are the things this design refuses to give up,\nand they are exactly what iframes and micro-frontends break. Every one of\nthose is a full page load, and a full page load takes React state with\nit. Routing around it client-side would have traded a stated architectural\npromise for a convenience.\n\nSo the conversation is kept in `sessionStorage` — which also survives a\nreload, and matches what was asked for: it lasts as long as the session.\nNot `localStorage`. The history carries tool results, which are real\ntenant data, and it has no business outliving the tab it was read in.\n\nRestored in the initial state rather than in an effect, so the panel does\nnot render empty and pop the conversation in a frame later — that reads\nas a bug even when it settles correctly. What comes back is shape-checked\nrather than trusted: it is storage a stale release or an extension could\nhave written, and a malformed restore would break the shell on every load\nwith no way out but devtools. Quota failures are swallowed, because a\nscreen result carries its whole UI tree and losing the ability to restore\na thread is a far smaller harm than throwing while rendering the page.\n\nIf a different person signs in on the same tab, the restored history is\nposted once, fails the signature check bound to its subject, and the\npanel clears itself on the 400 — the path that already existed, now load\nbearing.\n\nAlso adds \"New conversation\". Navigating away used to end a thread by\naccident; that was the bug, but it was also the only exit, and persisting\nwithout an exit would have been a worse portal than the one reported.\n\nBoth tests mutation-verified: without the restore, both fail.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"4f3287f0659ee4ce180ea59d2f0ac56934d73d71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/4f3287f0659ee4ce180ea59d2f0ac56934d73d71"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/52f8a05d39b2bedf0ce47f46cbe7d505491b3269","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/52f8a05d39b2bedf0ce47f46cbe7d505491b3269","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDUyZjhhMDVkMzliMmJlZGYwY2U0N2Y0NmNiZTdkNTA1NDkxYjMyNjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/43e0f4bb2af53824d42e9e2788c7793e561b7a07","sha":"43e0f4bb2af53824d42e9e2788c7793e561b7a07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/43e0f4bb2af53824d42e9e2788c7793e561b7a07"}],"sha":"52f8a05d39b2bedf0ce47f46cbe7d505491b3269","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/52f8a05d39b2bedf0ce47f46cbe7d505491b3269"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/74689576a76b013c85651937dd5e2bb695f3bf09/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T23:13:12Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T23:13:12Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Run the agent on a local model, for development\n\nTesting the assistant against a metered API turned a regression suite\ninto a bill, which is a poor incentive to test the agent. Nothing about\nthe portal was expensive to run; running a production-grade model as a\nregression harness was.\n\n`PORTAL_MODEL_PROVIDER=ollama` points the agent at a model on this\nmachine. 80 lines behind the same four-line `ModelClient` the vendor sits\nbehind, plus one branch in `modelClient()`. Nothing in the loop, the\ngrounding pass or the route knows which one it is talking to — which is\nthe clearest evidence yet that the seam PLAN.md argued for was worth\nhaving, since the model is rated the fastest-decaying dependency in the\nstack.\n\n**Six of the seven assistant tests pass locally**, including every\nsignature and governance test. Screen composition does not: `render_screen`\nis a 34-variant `oneOf` whose every data-bearing node must cite a tool\ncall grounding then verifies, and a 7B model answers in prose instead of\ncalling the tool. That test skips itself when a local provider is set,\nrather than being deleted or left red — a suite that is red by design\nteaches everyone to ignore it.\n\nTwo things this turned up.\n\nThe hub sent `model: \"\"` and Ollama rejected it in three milliseconds,\nwhile the route reported only that the assistant \"could not complete that\nrequest\". Compose writes `${VAR:-}` for every optional setting, so an\nunset variable arrives as an empty string, and `??` only catches null.\nEmpty is treated as absent now. The provider also reports the body of a\nfailed response rather than the status alone — a 400 with no reason\nleaves the caller guessing about a request they cannot see.\n\nAnd the loop returned an empty answer as an answer. A reply with no tool\ncall and no words put a blank bubble on the screen with nothing to say\nwhat went wrong; it is a failure with a sentence now. Weaker models do\nthis, but nothing about the bug was local — the hosted model could do it\ntoo, and the user would have been equally puzzled.\n\nThe default stays Anthropic deliberately. PLAN.md picks it because it is\nzero-data-retention eligible and regulated data reaches the model through\ntool results, which is a compliance decision before a capability one. A\nmodel on a laptop answers that question differently and nobody has\nreviewed it, so this turns on by choice and never by omission.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"71234d8d99c8704f17cf78307f8d01a7e55e92ff","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/71234d8d99c8704f17cf78307f8d01a7e55e92ff"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/74689576a76b013c85651937dd5e2bb695f3bf09","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/74689576a76b013c85651937dd5e2bb695f3bf09","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDc0Njg5NTc2YTc2YjAxM2M4NTY1MTkzN2RkNWUyYmI2OTVmM2JmMDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/43e0f4bb2af53824d42e9e2788c7793e561b7a07","sha":"43e0f4bb2af53824d42e9e2788c7793e561b7a07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/43e0f4bb2af53824d42e9e2788c7793e561b7a07"}],"sha":"74689576a76b013c85651937dd5e2bb695f3bf09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/74689576a76b013c85651937dd5e2bb695f3bf09"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/a7e3413244f152be839a38fe2c669e39e8eb8300/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T22:16:45Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T22:16:45Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Let an action declare a list, which its form could always show\n\nThe CRUD review turned up a hole only building both surfaces could\nproduce: `ActionParamSchema` allowed string, number and boolean, so an\naction carrying a list had no way to declare one. The orders form offered\n`tags` as a MultiSelect and the agent surface could not express it, which\nmeant an agent''s update always omitted the field — and the satellite had\nto guess whether absent meant \"unchanged\" or \"cleared\". It guessed wrong\nonce already: a model could strip the handling notes off a hazmat order\nbecause the rule was judged against a list the caller never sent.\n\nSo `string[]` is a declarable type now. Deliberately not a general array:\na list of strings is what `MultiSelect` produces, and anything richer\ninvites nesting, which is what keeps a schema out of strict structured\noutputs. `enum` constrains the elements rather than the list, because a\nmodel reading the choices as constraining the array would think one value\nwas the whole answer.\n\nAdding it made three projections refuse to compile, which is the type\nsystem doing its job: the MCP shim, the argument validator both the\ngateway and the public façade share, and the façade''s own param type. The\nvalidator needed its own branch — `typeof [] === \"object\"`, so the\nexisting check would have accepted `{}` as a list and handed it to a\nsatellite.\n\nThen the drift check refused the build, and it was right to. The C#\ngenerator pascal-cases protocol values, `string[]` lost its brackets to\n`String`, and it emitted an enum with two members of that name whose\n`ToWire` mapped *every plain string parameter* to `\"string[]\"` — a silent\ntype change on every action in the portal, in generated code nobody\nreads. `pascal` spells the suffix out now, and a `distinct` guard fails\ngeneration rather than emitting a plausible wrong answer. Verified by\nremoving the fix and watching it throw with both colliding values named.\n\nThe satellite keeps merging stored tags when the field is absent, but for\na different reason now: an omission has to mean \"leave them alone\" rather\nthan \"clear them\", or a caller changing one field would silently drop the\nlabels.\n\n**The assistant e2e could not run.** The API key''s credit balance is\nexhausted — a trivial request returns 400 `invalid_request_error`, so\nthis is not the change. The deterministic suite is green at 76.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"ce6fed742f6be09af2b2653307c1ef2fa1599426","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/ce6fed742f6be09af2b2653307c1ef2fa1599426"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/a7e3413244f152be839a38fe2c669e39e8eb8300","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/a7e3413244f152be839a38fe2c669e39e8eb8300","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKGE3ZTM0MTMyNDRmMTUyYmU4MzlhMzhmZTJjNjY5ZTM5ZThlYjgzMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/43e0f4bb2af53824d42e9e2788c7793e561b7a07","sha":"43e0f4bb2af53824d42e9e2788c7793e561b7a07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/43e0f4bb2af53824d42e9e2788c7793e561b7a07"}],"sha":"a7e3413244f152be839a38fe2c669e39e8eb8300","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/a7e3413244f152be839a38fe2c669e39e8eb8300"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/d