":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/43e0f4bb2af53824d42e9e2788c7793e561b7a07","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDQzZTBmNGJiMmFmNTM4MjRkNDJlOWUyNzg4Yzc3OTNlNTYxYjdhMDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/d48ad29f7cdb4690e97a9bb9fa0abe81c675d106","sha":"d48ad29f7cdb4690e97a9bb9fa0abe81c675d106","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/d48ad29f7cdb4690e97a9bb9fa0abe81c675d106"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/fa64b98f9a9cf7b20de47a7e08ccae018b77e6a0","sha":"fa64b98f9a9cf7b20de47a7e08ccae018b77e6a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/fa64b98f9a9cf7b20de47a7e08ccae018b77e6a0"}],"sha":"43e0f4bb2af53824d42e9e2788c7793e561b7a07","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/43e0f4bb2af53824d42e9e2788c7793e561b7a07"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/fa64b98f9a9cf7b20de47a7e08ccae018b77e6a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:56:16Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:56:16Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Fix what the review found, and stop showing customers buttons that 403\n\nThe best finding was one only building both surfaces could produce.\n`ActionParamSchema` has no array type, so an agent physically cannot send\n`tags` — and the update route then judged the hazmat-needs-notes rule\nagainst an empty list while the store kept the `hazmat` label. An agent\ncould strip the handling notes off a hazmat order and pass validation.\nThe route reads the stored order and merges its tags before validating\nnow. Mutation-verified: reverting the merge fails the new test.\n\nThat is worth naming as a protocol gap rather than a satellite bug. The\nform offers `tags` as a MultiSelect; the agent surface has no way to\nexpress an array at all. The two surfaces of the same action do not have\nthe same expressive range, and nothing in the protocol says so.\n\nAlso high: `Object.assign(order, draft)` left an absent optional in\nplace, so clearing the notes box was an edit the form could not make; and\n`Number.parseFloat` read a prefix, so \"250abc\" was accepted as 250.\n\nMedium: `asList`/`asBoolean` silently altered input rather than refusing\nit; cross-field rules overwrote per-field messages, telling the user the\nconsequence instead of the mistake; `#nextId` reissued a deleted order''s\nid to the next create; `{...order}` shared the store''s `tags` array with\nevery caller; a missing `id` answered `invalid({id})`, which renders on a\nHidden field and therefore nowhere; and the edit screen claimed editing\nwas refused for approved orders, which the repository allows.\n\nMy \"validates before it writes\" test was vacuous — the payload''s\ncustomer equalled the stored value, so it passed against an\nimplementation that wrote the whole draft through.\n\nBeyond the review: `orders.list` and `orders.detail` are external-facing,\nand this PR added three write affordances to them. Every write action is\ninternal-only, so a customer saw New, Edit and Delete and got 403 from\nall three. Pre-existing for Approve and widened here. The screen builders\ntake the principal''s audience now, with a test that the buttons are gone\nfor external *and* still present for internal — without the second half\nthe first passes against a builder that dropped them for everyone.\n\nLeft as reported: `today()` is UTC, so a user west of UTC in the evening\nis told today has already passed. The wire carries no timezone.\n\n103 integration tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"28343c541dfca654673f1d916651a6f31f66b45b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/28343c541dfca654673f1d916651a6f31f66b45b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/fa64b98f9a9cf7b20de47a7e08ccae018b77e6a0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/fa64b98f9a9cf7b20de47a7e08ccae018b77e6a0","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKGZhNjRiOThmOWE5Y2Y3YjIwZGU0N2E3ZTA4Y2NhZTAxOGI3N2U2YTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/e0487a911fc845fa5c92eed30e7e6b1554f8d1b1","sha":"e0487a911fc845fa5c92eed30e7e6b1554f8d1b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/e0487a911fc845fa5c92eed30e7e6b1554f8d1b1"}],"sha":"fa64b98f9a9cf7b20de47a7e08ccae018b77e6a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/fa64b98f9a9cf7b20de47a7e08ccae018b77e6a0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/e0487a911fc845fa5c92eed30e7e6b1554f8d1b1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:33:02Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:33:02Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Make orders a real CRUD application\n\nThe portal proved its read path three times over and its write path\nbarely at all: two mutations, both single-purpose state transitions, and\nevery text input in the catalog unrendered by any satellite. Nobody had\ntyped into this thing.\n\nMeasured before starting: 14 of 34 components were used by a real\nsatellite. The twenty unused ones included TextField, TextArea,\nNumberField, MultiSelect, DateField, DateRange, Checkbox, Switch and\nRadioGroup — the entire input vocabulary. The renderer implemented all of\nthem and no satellite had ever asked it to.\n\nOrders now creates, edits and deletes. One form builder serves create and\nedit, because two would drift and a field added to one and forgotten on\nthe other is a field a user can set and never change.\n\nThe part worth having is the validation. Three rules no single input can\nexpress — an expedited order cannot be standard priority, a hazmat order\nneeds notes, a critical order must be expedited — because every real form\nhas rules like those, and if a fixed vocabulary could not carry them that\nwould be the ceiling this architecture is bet against. Every message is\nkeyed to the `name` of an input the form actually renders, and a test\nwalks the rendered form asserting exactly that: a message keyed to a\nfield that does not exist renders nowhere, so the user is told something\nis wrong and never which.\n\nGovernance follows the registry, not the satellite. Create and update are\nagent-visible and pause for a person; delete is `agentVisible: false`,\nwhich is stronger — confirmation is someone reading a card, invisibility\nis the model never raising it, and for an irreversible write the second\nis the one worth having.\n\nTwo things this turned up.\n\nThe gateway fixture claimed to match the committed registry and nothing\nchecked, so it had gone stale. It now loads the real file and compares.\n\nEvery screen becomes an agent tool, including forms. `orders.new` is a\nblank form a model can call and learn nothing from. That follows from the\nshim making screens agent-visible by default, which is deliberate —\nper-screen registry entries would mean adding a screen needed a hub\ndeploy. Asserted rather than tolerated quietly, and recorded in PLAN.md:\nat three satellites it is noise, at twenty it is surface every model pays\nfor on every turn.\n\n21 integration tests and 6 browser tests that fill the form in, including\na server-side error landing on the field that caused it and the delete\nconfirmation the hub draws itself.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"8bc4ef01cca2e45e3c0413056f207dd799645b75","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/8bc4ef01cca2e45e3c0413056f207dd799645b75"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/e0487a911fc845fa5c92eed30e7e6b1554f8d1b1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/e0487a911fc845fa5c92eed30e7e6b1554f8d1b1","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKGUwNDg3YTkxMWZjODQ1ZmE1YzkyZWVkMzBlN2U2YjE1NTRmOGQxYjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/d48ad29f7cdb4690e97a9bb9fa0abe81c675d106","sha":"d48ad29f7cdb4690e97a9bb9fa0abe81c675d106","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/d48ad29f7cdb4690e97a9bb9fa0abe81c675d106"}],"sha":"e0487a911fc845fa5c92eed30e7e6b1554f8d1b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/e0487a911fc845fa5c92eed30e7e6b1554f8d1b1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/d48ad29f7cdb4690e97a9bb9fa0abe81c675d106/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:04:45Z","email":"15125586+myhumblecoder@users.noreply.github.com","name":"MyHumbleCoder"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:04:45Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Merge pull request #30 from myhumblecoder-dev/feat/satellite-depots\n\nAdd a C# satellite, and let the conformance kit judge it","tree":{"sha":"1697101efab1cc7f5fde25ceb7d3349ff673b295","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/1697101efab1cc7f5fde25ceb7d3349ff673b295"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/d48ad29f7cdb4690e97a9bb9fa0abe81c675d106","verification":{"payload":"tree 1697101efab1cc7f5fde25ceb7d3349ff673b295\nparent 3a6cc64f5bb6e60682b6a20b967f35239e92778