{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/d48ad29f7cdb4690e97a9bb9fa0abe81c675d106","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKGQ0OGFkMjlmN2NkYjQ2OTBlOTdhOWJiOWZhMGFiZTgxYzY3NWQxMDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/3a6cc64f5bb6e60682b6a20b967f35239e927781","sha":"3a6cc64f5bb6e60682b6a20b967f35239e927781","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/3a6cc64f5bb6e60682b6a20b967f35239e927781"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/08cc27c6e315f400e3b374dc6cfee7dc159e1f12","sha":"08cc27c6e315f400e3b374dc6cfee7dc159e1f12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/08cc27c6e315f400e3b374dc6cfee7dc159e1f12"}],"sha":"d48ad29f7cdb4690e97a9bb9fa0abe81c675d106","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/d48ad29f7cdb4690e97a9bb9fa0abe81c675d106"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/08cc27c6e315f400e3b374dc6cfee7dc159e1f12/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T20:38:24Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T20:38:24Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Fix what the review found, and correct why one of them was wrong\n\nThe high one was real and my own tests could not have caught it. The\nclose action returned `patch: [\"depots-table\"]`, but that node lives on\nthe dashboard while the only route to the action is the form on the\ndetail screen. `applyPatches` refuses a target that is not on the screen,\nso a successful close paired a success toast with a screen that never\nchanged. My test asserted the envelope shape, which is exactly why it\npassed. It navigates now, as `orders.approve` does. Confirmed live.\n\nA `text/plain` or bodyless POST answered 500 rather than a validation\nenvelope: `ReadFromJsonAsync` throws `InvalidOperationException` on a\nmissing content type, not `JsonException`, and only the latter was\ncaught. Also a cross-language divergence — `express.json()` degrades to\nan empty object. Confirmed live: now a validation outcome.\n\n`Repository.Close` wrote through `if (depots is List<Depot>)`, and a\ncollection expression yields an array — so the write was a silent no-op\nwhile `Close` still returned the \"updated\" record. The test that should\nhave caught it asserted only the response envelope; it now asserts the\nchange persisted.\n\n**The duplicate-claim finding was wrong, and I repeated it before\nchecking.** The review said `TryGetProperty` returns the first occurrence\nwhile `JSON.parse` and `json.loads` keep the last, making one signed\ntoken mean two tenants. Measured in all three: every one of them keeps\nthe last. There was no divergence.\n\nThe refusal stays, because nothing that mints these can emit a duplicate\n— they all serialise from a map — so a token carrying one did not come\nfrom the hub. But it is now labelled as the deliberate extra strictness\nit is, including the honest cost: orders and fleet accept such a token\nand this refuses it, which is worth porting to them rather than dropping\nhere.\n\nAlso from the review: `.dockerignore` scoped .NET output to the SDK only,\nso the satellite''s host `obj/` rode into its image; forwarded headers were\nenabled with no known-proxy list on a port published to the host, and\nbought nothing; `N0` formatting used the current culture; the declared\naudience was hardcoded rather than read from the manifest; and the\nconformance e2e block covered orders and fleet but not depots, leaving\nthis PR''s headline claim manual-only.\n\n28 satellite tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"1697101efab1cc7f5fde25ceb7d3349ff673b295","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/1697101efab1cc7f5fde25ceb7d3349ff673b295"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/08cc27c6e315f400e3b374dc6cfee7dc159e1f12","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/08cc27c6e315f400e3b374dc6cfee7dc159e1f12","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDA4Y2MyN2M2ZTMxNWY0MDBlM2IzNzRkYzZjZmVlN2RjMTU5ZTFmMTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/8a03af9982f489720d5547b5ae3d134a56fc215a","sha":"8a03af9982f489720d5547b5ae3d134a56fc215a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/8a03af9982f489720d5547b5ae3d134a56fc215a"}],"sha":"08cc27c6e315f400e3b374dc6cfee7dc159e1f12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/08cc27c6e315f400e3b374dc6cfee7dc159e1f12"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/8a03af9982f489720d5547b5ae3d134a56fc215a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T20:15:25Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T20:38:24Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Add a C# satellite, and let the conformance kit judge it\n\nThe third language, and the first satellite written against an SDK rather\nthan against the wire format. Node, Python and C# now share no library\nexcept one generated from the hub''s own catalog, and each verifies the\nhub''s principal itself.\n\nDepots rather than a second orders: it gives the agent a question no\nsingle solution can answer, and its data is disjoint from both.\n\nTwo things this was built to test, and both found something.\n\n`pnpm conformance http://127.0.0.1:4003` refused it: the manifest\nrequired a bearer token. The kit fetches it with no headers, because the\nmanifest is a *declaration* — ids, titles, nav placement, no tenant data\n— and the hub reads it at boot, before any user has arrived and so before\nit has a principal to present. The other two satellites already served it\nunauthenticated. Every one of my own tests passed throughout, because\nevery one of them sent a token. That is the conformance kit doing exactly\nwhat PLAN.md says it is for, against a language it has never seen.\n\nFixing it then broke four tests that were asserting 401/403 on the\nmanifest — the contract inverted under them and I had not re-run them.\nThey now target a screen, and two new tests pin the manifest as public\nand assert it carries nothing belonging to anybody.\n\nThe SDK earned its keep at compile time too: `ActionParam(\"id\", \"string\")`\ndoes not build, because the generated signature takes a `ParamType`.\n\nVerified beyond the unit tests: conformance passes 8 checks with 0\nfailures; the hub renders the screen showing this tenant''s depots and not\nglobex''s; and the agent answered \"which depots are at capacity\" from real\nfigures through a shim the satellite never wrote.\n\nThe registry test that pinned the satellite list to [fleet, orders]\nfailed, which is a guard behaving correctly rather than a nuisance.\n\n26 C# satellite tests. e2e 74 pass with the assistant on, 69 with it off.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"bd7d1fb05d2aa739f92647278e79acfed194050a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/bd7d1fb05d2aa739f92647278e79acfed194050a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/8a03af9982f489720d5547b5ae3d134a56fc215a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://a