.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/3a6cc64f5bb6e60682b6a20b967f35239e927781","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDNhNmNjNjRmNWJiNmU2MDY4MmI2YTIwYjk2N2YzNTIzOWU5Mjc3ODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/fe07b2a7c1c2cc242f754fbc822830a171950dbe","sha":"fe07b2a7c1c2cc242f754fbc822830a171950dbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/fe07b2a7c1c2cc242f754fbc822830a171950dbe"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/dc8780f42dc0482b1abbb359643a3622099916d9","sha":"dc8780f42dc0482b1abbb359643a3622099916d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/dc8780f42dc0482b1abbb359643a3622099916d9"}],"sha":"3a6cc64f5bb6e60682b6a20b967f35239e927781","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/3a6cc64f5bb6e60682b6a20b967f35239e927781"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/dc8780f42dc0482b1abbb359643a3622099916d9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T19:36:27Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T20:28:31Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Give the Python SDK the check its tests cannot perform\n\nI told you the TypeScript SDK was the least complete of the three,\ncounting helpers. That was wrong, and the count was the wrong measure.\nEvery TS builder parses its result against the real protocol schema and\nvalidates screens against the catalog, with its input types derived from\nthose schemas. It needs no `crumb` or `param` helper because those are\nplain objects the envelope parse already checks. It is the most rigorous\nof the three, not the least.\n\nSo parity runs the other way: Python and C# should validate, not grow\nhelpers. Their hand-written guards are partial by construction.\n\nExporting JSON Schema for them to validate against was the obvious answer\nand is a bad one. I checked before building it: converting ManifestSchema\ndrops the duplicate-id rule, the nav-entry-names-a-real-screen rule and\nthe audience-subset rule, and degrades `screen.ui` to a shallow node with\nno vocabulary. A validator that silently loses the protocol''s sharpest\nrules is a control that looks present and is not.\n\nWhat works is the probe: build one of everything in Python, print it,\nparse it with the real Zod schemas. Refinements included, because the\nschemas do the work rather than a translation of them.\n\nThe coverage claim took three attempts to become true, and each failure\nwas the same shape — a check reporting more than it did.\n\n`ui.py` carries `from __future__ import annotations`, so every annotation\nis a string and `get_args` returns nothing: the first version filled enum\nprops with \"x\" and swept zero enum values while reporting success.\n\nThe review then found the sample table keyed on PascalCase while the\nlookup passed snake_case, so three list props were silently empty and\nvalidated fine because none has a minimum length; and `_literals`\nfiltered on `isinstance(str)`, dropping `Heading.level`''s four integer\nvalues. An unmapped list prop now raises rather than defaulting to `[]`.\n\nAnd the coverage gate itself was measuring the rendered tree, where the\nenum sweep''s variants mask a component the builder loop never built —\ndropping `badge` still reported 34/34. It counts what was built now, and\ndropping a component fails naming it.\n\n34/34 components, 69 enum values, 106 nodes.\n\nAlso ports the guards the C# review found, adds the two helpers Python\nlacked — `action_descriptor` and `action_param`, without which a\nsatellite cannot declare the one thing that decides whether an agent can\ncall a write — and refuses `choices` on a non-string parameter, which\n`ActionParamSchema` rejects and which reads as callable and is not.\n\nThe CI step I added would have failed every run: it called pnpm from the\npython job, which has no Node. It now sets up both.\n\nThis commit replaces one that carried 161 files of .NET build output —\n5.6MB of assemblies, PDBs and vendored test-platform DLLs. They were left\non disk by the sdk-csharp branch, and once that branch''s .gitignore went\naway with the checkout, `git add -A` swept them up. Rewritten rather than\nfollowed with a deletion, because none of it belongs in the history.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"c8b9f3a323967fd30587bcd87f2931557530af00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/c8b9f3a323967fd30587bcd87f2931557530af00"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/dc8780f42dc0482b1abbb359643a3622099916d9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/dc8780f42dc0482b1abbb359643a3622099916d9","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oA