ttps://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/dc50a0ac854112597f16644e7faeb94c0a2aea4b","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKGRjNTBhMGFjODU0MTEyNTk3ZjE2NjQ0ZTdmYWViOTRjMGEyYWVhNGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/a8ece3112bd0044bec54afad1f8ec0c298615ec1","sha":"a8ece3112bd0044bec54afad1f8ec0c298615ec1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/a8ece3112bd0044bec54afad1f8ec0c298615ec1"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/836553448a95b03fd82a874a2adf947aa9e7a098","sha":"836553448a95b03fd82a874a2adf947aa9e7a098","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/836553448a95b03fd82a874a2adf947aa9e7a098"}],"sha":"dc50a0ac854112597f16644e7faeb94c0a2aea4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/dc50a0ac854112597f16644e7faeb94c0a2aea4b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/836553448a95b03fd82a874a2adf947aa9e7a098/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T14:57:03Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T14:57:03Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Generate the protocol vocabulary too, and refuse uncitable nodes\n\nThe review found `failed()` emitting `{\"level\": \"danger\"}`. The protocol''s\ntoast levels are success/info/warning/**error**; `danger` is a component\ntone. I had retyped the vocabulary into Python and got one word wrong, and\nno satellite here ships an action, so nothing caught it — the envelope was\nrejected outright by `ActionResponseSchema`.\n\nFixing the word is not the fix. Three languages means three hand-copies of\nthe same vocabulary and three chances to make that mistake, so the\nconstants now come from `@portal/protocol` the way the builders come from\nthe catalog: version, toast levels, action outcomes and audiences are\nemitted into `portal_sdk/protocol.py`, and `pnpm sdk:check` covers both\ngenerated files. C# will inherit this rather than repeat it.\n\nAlso from the review, as a design call it left open: `withSource` now\nrefuses a component that cannot carry a citation. Only four of the\nthirty-four declare `source` and every schema is strict, so my previous\nfix turned a silently inert call into a node the hub rejects. Neither is\nright — it throws at the call site now, naming the components that can\ncarry one. The citable set is generated from the catalog in both SDKs, and\na test compares it against the builders that actually take the parameter,\nso a component gaining or losing `source` cannot leave the two disagreeing.\n\nThe review also noted the CI workflow ran neither `pnpm sdk:check` nor the\nSDK tests — only the local script did, which made this PR''s \"CI fails if\nthe file differs\" claim false. Both steps are in the workflow now.\n\nAnd `packages/sdk-python` had no tsconfig, so `generate.ts` was never\ntypechecked at all: `tsx` runs TypeScript, it does not check it. Added and\nverified by planting a type error, which the build now catches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"051ff401a4054f8da022d4b8a1a4a3b883575f33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/051ff401a4054f8da022d4b8a1a4a3b883575f33"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/836553448a95b03fd82a874a2adf947aa9e7a098","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/836553448a95b03fd82a874a2adf947aa9e7a098","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDgzNjU1MzQ0OGE5NWIwM2ZkODJhODc0YTJhZGY5NDdhYTllN2EwOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/e92dfef6ed525d9ee81c75cca887c3a48762ddd3","sha":"e92dfef6ed525d9ee81c75cca887c3a48762ddd3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/e92dfef6ed525d9ee81c75cca887c3a48762ddd3"}],"sha":"836553448a95b03fd82a874a2adf947aa9e7a098","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/836553448a95b03fd82a874a2adf947aa9e7a098"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/e92dfef6ed525d9ee81c75cca887c3a48762ddd3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T14:37:05Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T14:37:05Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Add a Python SDK, generated from the catalog\n\nFleet was the satellite that proved the polyglot claim and had the worst\nauthoring experience in the repository: nested dicts where a misspelled\n\"StatTile\" or \"tone\" surfaced as a rejected response from the hub, at\nrequest time, in a process the satellite could not see.\n\nGenerated rather than written. A second SDK is a second place the\nvocabulary lives and a second place it can drift, which is the exact\nfailure this architecture exists to prevent — so `ui.py` is emitted from\nthe same COMPONENTS the hub validates against, the way sdk-node already\nderives its surface. `pnpm sdk:check` fails if the checked-in file does\nnot match what the catalog would produce today.\n\nThat check took two attempts. The first regenerated the file and asked\ngit whether it had changed, which can never fail: regenerating fixes the\nfile before the diff looks at it, and git sees nothing at all for a file\nit is not yet tracking. A guard that passes because it destroyed the\nevidence is worse than no guard, because it reads as coverage. `--check`\ncompares without writing. Verified against both real cases — a stale\nchecked-in file, and a catalog change with no regeneration.\n\nPorting Fleet found two bugs.\n\n`withSource` in the TypeScript SDK wrote to the wrong place. Grounding\nand every provenance mark in the renderer read `props.source`; it set a\ntop-level `node.source` that nothing reads. A satellite following the\ndocumented way to cite a tool call got no mark on screen and no credit\nfrom grounding — and the test passed throughout, because it asserted the\nsame field the function set. Both SDKs now write the prop, and the test\ngoes through the catalog instead.\n\n`DateRange.from` cannot be a Python parameter name; the module would not\nparse. The generator renames the parameter and keeps the wire name, and a\ntest walks every generated signature asserting no parameter is a keyword,\nso the next such prop fails here rather than at import.\n\nThe port is proven equivalent, not assumed: manifest, dashboard and\ndetail all serialise byte-identically to what the hand-written module\nproduced, modulo a deliberate 1.0 -> 1.1 bump.\n\nAlso fixes the Python image, which flattened the app into /app so an\neditable path dependency resolved above the build context, and adds the\nPython cache excludes .dockerignore never had — without them the SDK''s\nlocal __pycache__ and .venv ride into the image.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"a2e2e388058e939ed638da8229624a7195d32475","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/a2e2e388058e939ed638da8229624a7195d32475"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/e92dfef6ed525d9ee81c75cca887c3a48762ddd3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/e92dfef6ed525d9ee81c75cca887c3a48762ddd3","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKGU5MmRmZWY2ZWQ1MjVkOWVlODFjNzVjY2E4ODdjM2E0ODc2MmRkZDM","p