Q3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/a8ece3112bd0044bec54afad1f8ec0c298615ec1","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKGE4ZWNlMzExMmJkMDA0NGJlYzU0YWZhZDFmOGVjMGMyOTg2MTVlYzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/8a049b256dd7a5d7a285b03619afb17a13bfb7ba","sha":"8a049b256dd7a5d7a285b03619afb17a13bfb7ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/8a049b256dd7a5d7a285b03619afb17a13bfb7ba"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/056d024373847b540be5e9530210fc6777215eb8","sha":"056d024373847b540be5e9530210fc6777215eb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/056d024373847b540be5e9530210fc6777215eb8"}],"sha":"a8ece3112bd0044bec54afad1f8ec0c298615ec1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/a8ece3112bd0044bec54afad1f8ec0c298615ec1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/056d024373847b540be5e9530210fc6777215eb8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T02:01:04Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T02:01:04Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Stop issuing a conversation the hub will refuse\n\nThe review took the size cap and asked the question I had not: what the\ncap applies to. Every other route in the hub bounds a single submission.\nThis one bounds a conversation, and a conversation accumulates. So the\n\"forty times the real thing\" in my own comment compared one turn against\na limit that applies to the sum — it is about forty *turns*, and fewer\nwhen a tool returns a few hundred rows.\n\nThe consequence is the sharp end: the hub returns 200 with a signed\nhistory and then refuses that same history on the very next turn, wiping\na session mid-sentence for a user who did nothing wrong. Raising the\nnumber would only move the cliff.\n\nSo the conversation is trimmed on the way out, before signing, dropping\nthe oldest whole turns. Never inside a turn: trimming there would mean\nediting a `tool_result` that grounding cites, and a citation resolving to\na doctored result is worse than a conversation that ends. The cut only\never lands on a real question, because a `tool_result` is a user-role\nmessage and one whose `tool_use` has been trimmed away is an orphan the\nAPI rejects outright.\n\nAlso from the review: `JSON.parse(\"null\")` succeeds and yields null, so\nthe catch never fired and the next line threw with nothing to catch it.\nConfirmed against the running hub — `-d ''null''` was a bodyless 500, which\nthe panel reports as \"could not reach the assistant\" and does not clear\nfrom. Now a 400 envelope.\n\nAnd the coverage the review named plainly: deleting `readBounded` from\nthis route passed CI, because the e2e that covers it needs an API key CI\ndoes not have and `readBounded` had no unit test anywhere. It has nine\nnow, including the chunked sender that declares nothing and a multi-byte\ncharacter split across two chunks. Both new guards mutation-tested:\nremoving the streaming limit fails three, cutting the trim at any user\nturn fails two. These run in the unit tier, so they run in CI.\n\nAn oversized `ask` is now the only route left to a 413, so the panel\nrefuses one locally rather than spending a good conversation on a paste.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"be5ec3378771887209405baf70f4595ced0b01a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/be5ec3378771887209405baf70f4595ced0b01a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/056d024373847b540be5e9530210fc6777215eb8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/056d024373847b540be5e9530210fc6777215eb8","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDA1NmQwMjQzNzM4NDdiNTQwYmU1ZTk1MzAyMTBmYzY3NzcyMTVlYjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/3104bac1c9b07ed87d44ba42c4669dd82f334acd","sha":"3104bac1c9b07ed87d44ba42c4669dd82f334acd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/3104bac1c9b07ed87d44ba42c4669dd82f334acd"}],"sha":"056d024373847b540be5e9530210fc6777215eb8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/056d024373847b540be5e9530210fc6777215eb8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/3104bac1c9b07ed87d44ba42c4669dd82f334acd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T01:46:33Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T01:46:33Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"Count the agent body before parsing it\n\nEvery route in the hub that takes a body reads it through `readBounded`\nand refuses past 256 KB. The agent route was the exception, and the\nconversation is the worst place to have made one: the history arrives as\nclient input on every turn, and the signature that decides whether to\ntrust it can only be checked after the parse. The hub therefore paid the\ncost of an arbitrarily large body before it had any reason to believe the\nbody was its own.\n\nThe same constant rather than a new one. A screen composition — the\nlargest turn this portal produces — measures about 5 KB against a live\nstack, so the ceiling is roughly forty times the real thing, and a second\nnumber would only drift from the first.\n\nBoth refusal paths verified against the running hub: the declared\n`content-length` and, separately, a chunked sender that declares nothing,\nwhich is the case a header check alone never covered.\n\nThe panel now clears its conversation on 413 as it already did on 400.\nThe history is the one part of this that only ever grows, so it is the\none refusal a user can reach without doing anything wrong, and answering\nit by keeping the conversation that caused it would be a dead end of the\npanel''s own making.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0198VEh84szLssJuB1PpJF6p","tree":{"sha":"d466494cbadaad982cad12f8ed9773a188340457","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/d466494cbadaad982cad12f8ed9773a188340457"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/3104bac1c9b07ed87d44ba42c4669dd82f334acd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/3104bac1c9b07ed87d44ba42c4669dd82f334acd","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDMxMDRiYWMxYzliMDdlZDg3ZDQ0YmE0MmM0NjY5ZGQ4MmYzMzRhY2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/8a049b256dd7a5d7a285b03619afb17a13bfb7ba","sha":"8a049b256dd7a5d7a285b03619afb17a13bfb7ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/8a049b256dd7a5d7a285b03619afb17a13bfb7ba"}],"sha":"3104bac1c9b07ed87d44ba42c4669dd82f334acd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/3104bac1c9b07ed87d44ba42c4669dd82f334acd"}