wing_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/232e02d4061c2ad15758a2bf6643f23f1290630d","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDIzMmUwMmQ0MDYxYzJhZDE1NzU4YTJiZjY2NDNmMjNmMTI5MDYzMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/5a31ffef8a52de4b4a031520212e3327c990ad7d","sha":"5a31ffef8a52de4b4a031520212e3327c990ad7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/5a31ffef8a52de4b4a031520212e3327c990ad7d"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/01a871941eb3bf814fcbd2f59f2b69ece42a5fec","sha":"01a871941eb3bf814fcbd2f59f2b69ece42a5fec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/01a871941eb3bf814fcbd2f59f2b69ece42a5fec"}],"sha":"232e02d4061c2ad15758a2bf6643f23f1290630d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/232e02d4061c2ad15758a2bf6643f23f1290630d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/01a871941eb3bf814fcbd2f59f2b69ece42a5fec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T22:58:02Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T22:58:02Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"fix(agent): my new error message told the model something untrue\n\nCode review of PR #24. Six findings, five applied, one left with a note.\n\nThe fix undercut itself\n------------------------\n`draw()` grounded against the conversation history, which does not yet hold the\ntool results collected earlier in the *same* turn — those sit in a local array\nuntil the turn is appended. The model writes its own `tool_use` ids, so it can\nfetch and draw in one assistant message, citing an id it has just emitted. The\nread runs, grounding sees nothing, and this PR''s brand-new message says \"No tool\ncall has happened yet in this conversation; fetch the data first.\"\n\nWhich is false, and burns exactly the turn the PR set out to save. I replaced a\nmessage that said nothing useful with one that said something wrong.\n\nFixed by grounding against the history plus the results collected so far.\nConfirmed by mutation: with the previous line restored, the regression test\nfails; with it, nineteen pass.\n\nThe e2e gating was worse than ungated\n--------------------------------------\nBoth `beforeAll` probes sent a full live agent turn — several model round trips\n— purely to decide whether to skip. Playwright caps a `beforeAll` at the config\ntimeout, thirty seconds, not the `timeout: 180_000` on the request; a slow\ncompose therefore fails the hook, and a failing hook fails every test in the\ndescribe including the ungated deterministic one. It also billed two model turns\nper run for nothing.\n\nThe probe posts an empty body now: the route checks whether the assistant is\nenabled before it parses one, so disabled answers 404 and enabled answers 400,\nwith no model call. And it accepts only those two — `!== 404` treated a 502 from\nan expired key as \"assistant configured\", which ran the live tests and failed\nthem with nothing pointing at the key.\n\nThe per-test `timeout: 240_000` was dead for the same reason; the describe\nraises the test timeout now.\n\nAnd one assertion checked the wrong thing\n------------------------------------------\n`toContain(\"ord-1001\")` asserted which *columns* the model chose. Grounding\nkeeps only the requested keys, so a table of customer, status and total is a\ncorrect grounded screen with no order id in it — precisely the \"assert a model''s\nwording\" mistake the describe''s own comment warns about. It asserts the rows\nwere substituted, which is the property that matters.\n\nLeft with a note: the agent route casts the posted conversation to `Message[]`\nwithout validating it, so a client can fabricate a `tool_result` and get a\nscreen with invented rows under a provenance citation. It was already in\nPLAN.md''s known limits; this PR is what makes the endpoint reachable in a\nrunning stack, so the entry now says so.\n\nVerified both configurations against the live stack, which the review could not:\nassistant on, 67 pass and 2 skip; assistant off, 66 pass and 3 skip.\n826 unit, 61 integration, 37 Python.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5460c174a49a2c42a1090678fe8fd12564cb79ab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/5460c174a49a2c42a1090678fe8fd12564cb79ab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/01a871941eb3bf814fcbd2f59f2b69ece42a5fec","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/01a871941eb3bf814fcbd2f59f2b69ece42a5fec","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDAxYTg3MTk0MWViM2JmODE0ZmNiZDJmNTlmMmI2OWVjZTQyYTVmZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/4f0c5876809189760435ba611846dba47bdc720d","sha":"4f0c5876809189760435ba611846dba47bdc720d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/4f0c5876809189760435ba611846dba47bdc720d"}],"sha":"01a871941eb3bf814fcbd2f59f2b69ece42a5fec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/01a871941eb3bf814fcbd2f59f2b69ece42a5fec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/4f0c5876809189760435ba611846dba47bdc720d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T22:44:12Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T22:44:12Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"fix(agent): the model was never told what a tool call id is\n\nThe key you added made the agent runnable, so I ran it. The first real\ncomposition burned every turn it had.\n\nThe bug\n-------\nGrounding requires each data-bearing node to cite `source.toolCallId`. Nothing\nin the system ever told the model what one looked like. It guessed the tool''s\nname — `orders__orders_list:0`, then `orders__orders_list` — was refused each\ntime, and ran out of turns.\n\nThe id was in the model''s own `tool_use` block the whole time, which turns out\nnot to be the same as being told. And every scripted test passed correct ids\nbecause I wrote them: the fixtures encoded the answer to the question the model\nactually had to answer.\n\nThree changes, one of them the fix\n-----------------------------------\nThe id now travels with the data it labels: a read''s result carries its own\n`toolCallId` beside the extracted data. That is the substantive one — the model\ncopies a value it can see rather than inferring a convention nobody stated.\n\nA failed citation now names the ids that exist, because \"that did not happen\" is\nunactionable on its own and a retry is just another guess. When nothing has been\nfetched at all it says so, which is a different mistake needing different advice.\n\nAnd the tool description says the id comes from the tool''s result and is not the\ntool''s name — the thing the model assumed twice.\n\nComposition now succeeds on the first attempt, with the table''s rows filled in\nby the hub from the cited call and a `StatTile` value checked against it.\n\nAlso here\n---------\nCompose passes `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` through from the root `.env`, which git\nignores. Absent still means no assistant.\n\nThe live path has e2e coverage that skips unless the running stack has a key: CI\nhas none and a suite that failed there would train everyone to ignore it. The\nassertions are shape-based, because asserting a model''s wording is asserting\nsomething nobody can fix. Both configurations were run — with a key, 67 pass and\nthe two \"switched off\" tests skip; without one, 66 pass and the three live tests\nskip.\n\nThose \"switched off\" tests needed gating too. They asserted the agent is absent,\nwhich was true only because compose had no key to pass. A developer with a key\nwas running the other configuration and being told their portal was broken.\n\nOne test of mine was wrong rather than the code: it asserted \"two orders are\npending\" while tests earlier in the same file approve one. It passed alone and\nfailed in a full run, for a reason that had nothing to do with the agent. It\nasks the satellite what is true now and compares against that.\n\nVerified: 825 unit, 61 integration, 37 Python, 67 e2e; and the audit log shows\nthe agent''s tool call recorded under the tenant''s key alongside the screen read.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f56851c0dba8f3c5dedd51267e44011eeb2e86fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/f56851c0dba8f3c5dedd51267e44011eeb2e86fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/4f0c5876809189760435ba611846dba47bdc720d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/4f0c5876809189760435ba611846dba47bdc720d","n