ithub.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/5a31ffef8a52de4b4a031520212e3327c990ad7d","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDVhMzFmZmVmOGE1MmRlNGI0YTAzMTUyMDIxMmUzMzI3Yzk5MGFkN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/191adaa8c812fa72100332d3c684f4d46a67c6b1","sha":"191adaa8c812fa72100332d3c684f4d46a67c6b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/191adaa8c812fa72100332d3c684f4d46a67c6b1"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/74960ac1203381a78b3e1cc2ac800f0765060d62","sha":"74960ac1203381a78b3e1cc2ac800f0765060d62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/74960ac1203381a78b3e1cc2ac800f0765060d62"}],"sha":"5a31ffef8a52de4b4a031520212e3327c990ad7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/5a31ffef8a52de4b4a031520212e3327c990ad7d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/74960ac1203381a78b3e1cc2ac800f0765060d62/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T22:13:29Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T22:13:29Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"fix: the guard I said was missing, and a claim that was still generous\n\nCode review of PR #23. Six findings, five applied by the review, one it skipped\nand I took.\n\nIt caught the thing the pull request was about\n-----------------------------------------------\nI wrote that the root cause was leaving nothing in the repository that would\ncatch the regression — \"no test, no check, just a sentence in a pull request\" —\nand then fixed only prose. Nothing read `.env.example`, so the same deletion\ncould land again with `verify:ci` fully green. There is a test now, and I\nconfirmed it goes red by commenting the key out.\n\nTwo more it found in the same shape as the bug being fixed. The README''s\nconfiguration table still listed one required setting — the more prominent\noperator-facing document, carrying the exact defect this PR exists to correct,\nbecause I fixed the file I was looking at. And `.gitignore` promised that\npointing `PORTAL_AUDIT_LOG` at the working tree \"must not put tenant data in a\ncommit\" while `*.audit.jsonl` did not match `portal-audit.jsonl` — the filename\nthis repository''s own compose file uses. A comment claiming a property the glob\ndid not have, in the pull request whose subject was a false claim.\n\nThe one it skipped\n------------------\n`auditConfig()` is lazy, so a hub with no key started, answered `/` — which\ntouches no audited path — passed compose''s healthcheck, and 500''d on every real\nrequest. `pnpm up` said the stack was healthy. That is the worst available\nfailure: whatever is watching reports green, and the thing that would have told\nyou is the log that is missing.\n\nNext''s `instrumentation` hook runs once per server instance, so the check lives\nthere now. Verified in a container: without the key, `/` answers 500, the\nhealthcheck cannot pass, and the reason is in the first lines of the log.\n\nAnd PLAN.md''s \"the hub refuses to serve\" was still generous after that, so it\nnow says what actually happens: the server fails to prepare, every request\nanswers 500, the container never becomes healthy — and the process stays up,\nwhich is why the sentence describes the behaviour rather than reaching for a\ntidier verb.\n\nVerified: 822 unit, 61 integration, 37 Python, 66 e2e; the keyless container\nobserved directly rather than reasoned about.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"57ffc433bb53dc8cb3847f0c3e5a87395d438b0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/57ffc433bb53dc8cb3847f0c3e5a87395d438b0d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/74960ac1203381a78b3e1cc2ac800f0765060d62","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/74960ac1203381a78b3e1cc2ac800f0765060d62","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDc0OTYwYWMxMjAzMzgxYTc4YjNlMWNjMmFjODAwZjA3NjUwNjBkNjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/51c974fa0cb4180a07ecb3304d882bc61eb28b49","sha":"51c974fa0cb4180a07ecb3304d882bc61eb28b49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/51c974fa0cb4180a07ecb3304d882bc61eb28b49"}],"sha":"74960ac1203381a78b3e1cc2ac800f0765060d62","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/74960ac1203381a78b3e1cc2ac800f0765060d62"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/51c974fa0cb4180a07ecb3304d882bc61eb28b49/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T21:59:06Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T21:59:06Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"fix: main told operators not to set the two settings it requires\n\n#21 added the mandatory audit key and sink. #22 removed them from\n`.env.example`, correctly, because they did not exist on the branch #22 was cut\nfrom. #22 merged second, so its note is what landed — and main now says:\n\n    So there is deliberately no PORTAL_AUDIT_LOG or PORTAL_AUDIT_KEY here\n\nwhile `apps/hub/src/lib/audit.ts` refuses to start without either, and the\ndigest it calls \"still an unkeyed SHA-256\" is an HMAC.\n\nEvery clause of that note is now false. An operator following the template gets\na hub that will not start and a document telling them the thing they need does\nnot exist. That is worse than the state before #22, which is the specific way a\nmerge-order hazard costs something.\n\nI flagged the ordering when I opened #22 and asked for #22 first, then #21. Both\nmerged, in the other order, and I had left nothing in the repository that would\ncatch it — no test, no check, just a sentence in a pull request. A correctness\nclaim that depends on humans reading merge instructions is not a control.\n\nFixed here: both settings are documented as mandatory with the reasoning, the\n\"one genuinely mandatory setting\" header is corrected to three, and\n`.gitignore`''s audit rule no longer describes itself as defensive ahead of work\nthat has since landed. PLAN.md''s note grouping the digest key with the\nconversation HMAC as \"the same open decision\" now says the first is decided and\nenforced and the second is not.\n\nVerified rather than asserted this time: removing either variable makes\n`auditConfig()` throw, checked for both, and the example''s own default log path\nis still ignored by git.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"666e3ba6d13a69bf6621a7c1d00fafbf1937cd2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/666e3ba6d13a69bf6621a7c1d00fafbf1937cd2b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/51c974fa0cb4180a07ecb3304d882bc61eb28b49","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/51c974fa0cb4180a07ecb