b.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/97218522605494268b5411c5203aa9d60f1d6f8d","sha":"97218522605494268b5411c5203aa9d60f1d6f8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/97218522605494268b5411c5203aa9d60f1d6f8d"}],"sha":"076b37bd5cec8bc7526197fac4ef60ad29684e33","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/076b37bd5cec8bc7526197fac4ef60ad29684e33"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/398b54612d5e974f9f7180a6b537268fb4c1f8e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T21:52:38Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T21:52:38Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"fix: a template that documented controls the branch does not have\n\nCode review of PR #22. Nine findings, all applied.\n\nThe one that would have cost someone something\n-----------------------------------------------\n`.dockerignore` excluded `**/.env` and `**/.env.local` while `hub.Dockerfile`\ndoes `COPY . .`. This PR widened the *git* rule to `.env.*` without widening\nthat one, so a `.env.production` created under the new convention would have\nbeen invisible to git and baked into an image layer permanently — where it does\nnot get deleted, only re-pushed. Widening one ignore file and not the other is\nworse than widening neither, because it looks handled.\n\nThe template described a system one branch over\n------------------------------------------------\nI documented `PORTAL_AUDIT_KEY` and `PORTAL_AUDIT_LOG` as required, with \"there\nis no unkeyed mode\" and advice to give the log its own volume. None of that is\ntrue on this branch: the digest here is still an unkeyed SHA-256 and the hub''s\naudit sinks are in-memory. Those settings exist in PR #21, which is open.\n\nAn operator reading this would have provisioned a volume, set both variables,\nbelieved every request was recorded, and had an empty file and a brute-forceable\ndigest. That is worse than saying nothing — a template is read as a statement of\nwhat the system does.\n\nThey are absent now, with a note saying what actually exists and why. The\ndocumentation belongs in the change that adds the feature, so it goes into #21.\nMerge #22 first; I will fold it in there.\n\nThe same false claim appeared in `.gitignore`''s own security section, and in the\nline saying three settings are mandatory when one is.\n\nThe rest, all checked against the code\n---------------------------------------\n`PORTAL_REGISTRY_PATH`''s default is `../../config/satellites.yaml` relative to a\ncwd of `apps/hub`, not `./config/...` — uncommenting the line as written was an\n`ENOENT` at startup. `PORTAL_ALLOW_DEV_SESSION` is compared to exactly `\"1\"`, so\n`true` silently yields no session. `PORTAL_DEV_AUDIENCE` only acts on\n`external`. And `PORT` was missing from a file I described as built by grepping\nevery variable the code reads — it is read by both satellites.\n\nVerified again after the edits: `.env` ignored, `.env.example` visible,\n`next-env.d.ts` tracked, zero already-tracked files newly ignored, and a\n`.env.production` excluded from both git and the Docker build context.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e45c19b0dbc9b19a7586f4970a43074ed902a0c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/e45c19b0dbc9b19a7586f4970a43074ed902a0c8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/398b54612d5e974f9f7180a6b537268fb4c1f8e3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/398b54612d5e974f9f7180a6b537268fb4c1f8e3","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDM5OGI1NDYxMmQ1ZTk3NGY5ZjcxODBhNmI1MzcyNjhmYjRjMWY4ZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/a93a36a13ae00aad5f471b72b67ac8389d536797","sha":"a93a36a13ae00aad5f471b72b67ac8389d536797","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/a93a36a13ae00aad5f471b72b67ac8389d536797"}],"sha":"398b54612d5e974f9f7180a6b537268fb4c1f8e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/398b54612d5e974f9f7180a6b537268fb4c1f8e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/a93a36a13ae00aad5f471b72b67ac8389d536797/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T21:42:18Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T21:42:18Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"chore: a .gitignore organised around what must never be committed\n\nThe key was never at risk — `.env` was already ignored, and the\n`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` matches in history are the variable name in `agent.ts`\nrather than any value. Checked before touching anything, because that is the\nquestion worth answering first.\n\nRewritten with the secrets at the top and everything else below, because those\ntwo halves are not the same kind of rule. Moving something out of the first\nsection should be a decision; moving something out of the second is a tidy-up.\n\nWhat changed that matters\n--------------------------\n`.env.*` rather than three specific variants, so `.env.production` and whatever\nsomeone invents next are covered — with `!.env.example` beside it, which is the\npairing that makes ignoring everything safe. Committing the *names* is how a\nnewcomer discovers that the hub refuses to start without\n`PORTAL_PRINCIPAL_SECRET` and `PORTAL_AUDIT_KEY`, instead of discovering it from\na leak.\n\nAudit logs are ignored. `PORTAL_AUDIT_LOG` is a path an operator chooses, the\nrecords carry principals, tenants and parameter digests, and pointing it at the\nworking tree during a local run should not put tenant data in a commit. The\nexample''s own default lands on that rule, which is checked rather than assumed.\n\nAlso keys and certificates, pnpm and yarn stores, the caches every tool here\nwrites (vitest, turbo, eslint, playwright, ruff, mypy), and the OS files that\nfollow a repository around.\n\nTwo deliberate exceptions\n--------------------------\n`next-env.d.ts` is not ignored: Next regenerates it and its own documentation\nsays to commit it. And `.vscode` is ignored except `extensions.json`, which is a\nstatement about what this repository needs rather than anyone''s preferences.\n\nVerified: `.env` still ignored, `.env.example` visible, `next-env.d.ts` still\ntracked, and no file that was already tracked is now ignored — that last one\nbeing the way a rewrite like this quietly breaks a repository.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aa324443b2eec6d55085e5a11918dbd8ba7ac182","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/aa324443b2eec6d55085e5a11918dbd8ba7ac182"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/a93a36a13ae00aad5f471b72b67ac8389d536797","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/a93a36a13ae00aad5f471b72b67ac8389d536797","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKGE5M2EzNmExM2FlMDBhYWQ1ZjQ3MWI3MmI2N2FjODM4OWQ1MzY3OTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/405d301d8df907d391acfd8dfaf40226b425a52e","sha":"405d301d8df907d391acfd8dfaf40226b425a52e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/405d301d8df907d391acfd8dfaf40226b425a52e"}],"sha":"a93a36a13ae00aad5f471b72b67ac8389d536797","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/a93a36a13ae00aad5f471b72b67ac8389d536797"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/97218522605494268b5411c5203aa9d60f1d6f8d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T21:13:08Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T21:13:08Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"fix(audit): fail closed meant crash the container\n\nCode review of PR #21. Eleven findings, eight applied by the review, three it\nleft me — all three taken.\n\nThe one that mattered\n---------------------\nAudit writes were started inside the gateway''s synchronous `onAudit` and only\nawaited a model round trip later, with no handler attached in between. Node''s\ndefault is `--unhandled-rejections=throw`, so a single `ENOSPC` on the audit\nfile during an agent turn exited the process.\n\n\"Fail closed\" became \"crash the container\", which is not the same thing and is\nstrictly worse: one request should have failed, and instead every in-flight\nrequest died with it. The rejection is caught the moment the write starts now,\nthe first failure is held, and `flush()` rethrows it — verified by a test that\nstarts a failing write, lets a turn''s worth of other work happen, and asserts it\nsurfaces as a rejection rather than an exit.\n\nThree the review left to me\n----------------------------\n**The public API had no audit trail at all.** The partner-facing projection\nreads the same regulated data the screens do, for principals outside the\norganization, and wrote nothing — while both PLAN.md and my pull request said\nevery path was covered. The most regulated consumer was the one omission. Fixed,\nand asserted end to end.\n\n**Refusals were not recorded**, contradicting \"including the refusals\" in the\nsame PR. The review declined to fix it for a good reason: auditing a request\nfrom someone we cannot identify, with writes that fail closed, hands an\nunauthenticated caller a way to fill the audit disk and take the hub down. So\nthe line is drawn where it belongs — a refusal is recorded once a principal is\nestablished, and not before. \"This principal was refused this screen\" is\nevidence; \"someone unauthenticated knocked\" is an access log''s job.\n\n**The audit suite wrote files from the unit tier**, which `vitest.config.ts`\ndefines as touching no filesystem. A suite that ignores the boundary its own\nconfig draws makes the boundary meaningless for everyone else, so it moved.\n\nThe rest\n--------\nAn audit failure after a successful mutation escaped as an HTML 500, so the\nrenderer reported \"could not reach this solution\" for a change that had already\napplied. It still fails closed, now inside the envelope with a message that says\nso. Pending writes were abandoned when an agent turn threw. `agentInvokerDeps`\nsat outside the try block written to stop exactly the error it can raise. And\n`screen()` in the SDK deep-cloned the tree that `ui.ts` works to avoid cloning,\nundoing an optimisation documented at length two files away.\n\nOne test was passing for the wrong reason: `auditKey` had been added to a raw\nobject handed to a strict schema, so \"rejects an unknown action kind\" was\nthrowing on the unknown top-level key instead of exercising the union.\n\nVerified: 822 unit, 52 integration, 37 Python, 66 e2e.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"26a3010121696b4b3bb8ad1c791b4a2bd0bdd57b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/26a3010121696b4b3bb8ad1c791b4a2bd0bdd57b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/97218522605494268b5411c5203aa9d60f1d6f8d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/97218522605494268b5411c5203aa9d60f1d6f8d","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDk3MjE4NTIyNjA1NDk0MjY4YjU0MTFjNTIwM2FhOWQ2MGYxZDZmOGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/67f17beb1d19f6962a07b2b24c0b35348500dc0c","sha":"67f17beb1d19f6962a07b2b24c0b35348500dc0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/67f17beb1d19f6962a07b2b24c0b35348500dc0c"}],"sha":"97218522605494268b5411c5203aa9d60f1d6f8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/97218522605494268b5411c5203aa9d60f1d6f8d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/67f17beb1d19f6962a07b2b24c0b35348500dc0c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T20:58:36Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T20:58:36Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"feat(audit): the log the schema was designed for in M1\n\nPLAN.md put the audit schema in M1 because retrofitting audit onto a system\nalready handling regulated data is a re-certification rather than a patch. The\nschema has been right since. It had nowhere to go: `screenRead`, `actionInvoke`\nand `agentCompose` had zero call sites anywhere in the repository, and the\ngateway built a valid `toolCall` for every call and dropped it.\n\nSo the deterministic portal was not audited at all, and the agent path was\naudited into a variable. That is a more comfortable kind of nothing than having\nno schema, and exactly as useless.\n\nMandatory, as asked\n-------------------\n`PORTAL_AUDIT_KEY` and `PORTAL_AUDIT_LOG` have no defaults and the hub refuses\nto serve without them. A default key produces a log that looks keyed and is\nnot; a default path produces one nobody knows to collect. Both look like\nsuccess, which is what makes them worse than refusing.\n\nThere is no unkeyed path left. `canonicalDigest` is gone; `auditDigest` takes a\nkey and `tenantAuditKey` derives one per tenant from a single configured secret\n— derived rather than configured per tenant, because an operator managing one\nsecret manages it well and an operator managing forty rotates none of them.\n\nPer tenant is the part that matters. It closes the hole the schema shipped with\nand documented: an unkeyed SHA-256 over a low-entropy parameter — an order id, a\nnational insurance number — is recoverable by anyone holding the log and a\ncandidate list, which is most people who would ever read it. Now a candidate\nlist is not enough, one tenant''s digests cannot be matched against another''s,\nand handing a tenant their own log tells them nothing about anyone else''s.\n\nFail closed\n-----------\nIf the record cannot be written, the request fails. That is the only posture\nconsistent with calling the audit mandatory: a system that carries on when it\ncannot record what it did has a log that is evidence of nothing. The cost is\nreal and is in PLAN.md''s known limits — a full audit disk is an outage rather\nthan a silent gap.\n\nEvery path, including the refusals\n-----------------------------------\nScreen reads, actions, and every tool call an agent or an MCP host makes. The\ngateway''s `InvokeDeps` now requires the key rather than accepting it, so a\ncaller cannot produce a log indistinguishable from a keyed one. Writes are\nstarted synchronously and awaited before the response leaves — a reply that went\nout before its record was on disk would make the log \"mostly complete\", which is\nthe one thing an audit log may not be.\n\nVerification item 11 is closed\n-------------------------------\n\"From the audit log alone, answer which records the agent read, for whom, when.\"\nAsserted end to end against the running stack: a screen read with satellite,\nscreen, principal, tenant, outcome and latency; an action; two tenants'' digests\ndiffering for the same request; and no scope and no parameter value anywhere in\nthe file.\n\nVerified: 831 unit, 42 integration, 37 Python, 64 e2e.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e4901597458094fa24fd3f0c2042bfb017866e17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/e4901597458094fa24fd3f0c2042bfb017866e17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/67f17beb1d19f6962a07b2b24c0b35348500dc0c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/67f17beb1d19f6962a07b2b24c0b35348500dc0c","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDY3ZjE3YmViMWQxOWY2OTYyYTA3YjJiMjRjMGIzNTM0ODUwMGRjMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/405d301d8df907d391acfd8dfaf40226b425a52e","sha":"405d301d8df907d391acfd8dfaf40226b425a52e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/405d301d8df907d391acfd8dfaf40226b425a52e"}],"sha":"67f17beb1d19f6962a07b2b24c0b35348500dc0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/67f17beb1d19f6962a07b2b24c0b35348500dc0c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User",