XytakVxrbLqTE+Pgq\n=9PN2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-17T20:52:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/405d301d8df907d391acfd8dfaf40226b425a52e","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDQwNWQzMDFkOGRmOTA3ZDM5MWFjZmQ4ZGZhZjQwMjI2YjQyNWE1MmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/5b66a9267aef0817270ae46afb34fedb245749af","sha":"5b66a9267aef0817270ae46afb34fedb245749af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/5b66a9267aef0817270ae46afb34fedb245749af"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/0a38d8c1d95cfa73ef0ee033f98f33712e54d44b","sha":"0a38d8c1d95cfa73ef0ee033f98f33712e54d44b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/0a38d8c1d95cfa73ef0ee033f98f33712e54d44b"}],"sha":"405d301d8df907d391acfd8dfaf40226b425a52e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/405d301d8df907d391acfd8dfaf40226b425a52e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/0a38d8c1d95cfa73ef0ee033f98f33712e54d44b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T17:09:17Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T17:09:17Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"fix(sdk-node): the builders nobody called, and a manifest input that typed nothing\n\nCode review of PR #20. Eleven findings, eight applied by the review, two more\ntaken here, one left with a note.\n\nTwo that went to this PR''s own claim\n-------------------------------------\n`ok`, `failed` and `invalid` had zero call sites. `app.ts` still hand-built all\nfour `ActionResponse` literals with `CURRENT_PROTOCOL_VERSION` copied into each\n— the exact case the SDK''s docstring calls \"the one that repays this most\", and\nthe case my pull request said was \"written through it\". Only `screens.ts` was.\nMigrated, byte-identical.\n\nWorse: `ManifestInput.screens` was `Record<string, unknown>[]`, so\n`declare({ screens: [{ id: \"orders.list\", titel: \"Orders\" }] })` compiled clean\nand threw at boot. That is precisely the failure this package exists to\neliminate, in the one builder every satellite calls. Derived from the protocol''s\nown schemas now, and the typo is `TS2561 … Did you mean to write ''title''?`.\n\nA package whose central claim fails at its own front door is worth more than an\napology, so: both were found by review rather than by me writing a test that\nwould have caught them. `ok()` having no callers was visible from `grep`.\n\nTwo I took that it reported and skipped\n----------------------------------------\n`screen()` validated the envelope and never the catalog. A subtree that did not\ngo through `ui.*` — a helper returning `UiNode`, a literal written in a hurry —\npassed here and was refused whole by the hub. The SDK''s promise is that a screen\nis valid before it leaves; that was the last way round it, and it is closed.\n\nAnd the cost comment was false. It said \"a Zod parse per node on a screen of a\nfew dozen\", which is true of every component except the one that matters:\n`Table.rows` is unbounded satellite *data*, so a ten-thousand-row screen\nvalidated ten thousand records and Zod deep-copied all of them. The parse result\nis discarded now rather than returned, so nothing is cloned — safe only while no\ncomponent declares a default, which a test holds true. The remaining cost is\nstated accurately, with the advice to cache a very large screen rather than\nbuild it per request.\n\nThe rest\n--------\n`ok()` hardcoded a `success` toast, making the protocol''s `info` level\nunreachable — so `orders.refresh`, which says \"Orders reloaded\", would have been\nturned into a congratulation by anyone porting it. `PropsOf` used the schema''s\noutput where a builder takes input. Optionals were spelled `?: T` under\n`exactOptionalPropertyTypes`, forcing spread gymnastics on callers.\n`InvalidEnvelopeError` formatted its issues into a string and discarded them.\nAnd `check()` took an explicit type argument that was never checked against the\nschema, so a builder could have claimed one envelope while validating another.\n\nLeft with a note: the SDK re-exports no protocol types, so a satellite imports\nfrom both. That is deliberate — PLAN.md treats the protocol package as the\ndurable asset authors should depend on directly.\n\nVerified: 817 unit, 42 integration, 37 Python, 60 e2e; the deployed satellite\nstill passes conformance 8/0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4bf3ad09abfffdefc073d343030eabfcad8393e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/4bf3ad09abfffdefc073d343030eabfcad8393e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/0a38d8c1d95cfa73ef0ee033f98f33712e54d44b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/0a38d8c1d95cfa73ef0ee033f98f33712e54d44b","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDBhMzhkOGMxZDk1Y2ZhNzNlZjBlZTAzM2Y5OGYzMzcxMmU1NGQ0NGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/c98ee270f4086c1816723f0dbd2161a8d790cf9e","sha":"c98ee270f4086c1816723f0dbd2161a8d790cf9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/c98ee270f4086c1816723f0dbd2161a8d790cf9e"}],"sha":"0a38d8c1d95cfa73ef0ee033f98f33712e54d44b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/0a38d8c1d95cfa73ef0ee033f98f33712e54d44b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/c98ee270f4086c1816723f0dbd2161a8d790cf9e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T16:56:16Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T16:56:16Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"feat(sdk-node): the compiler catching what the hub otherwise would\n\nM3 step 16 completed. The conformance kit tells a team what is wrong with their\nsatellite; this stops it being wrong.\n\nThe claim, demonstrated rather than asserted\n---------------------------------------------\n`{ type: \"Text\", props: { txt: \"hello\" } }` typed as a `UiNode` compiles clean —\n`props` is `Record<string, unknown>`, so the protocol cannot catch a typo in a\ncomponent''s vocabulary. Written as `ui.Text({ txt: \"hello\" })` it is a compile\nerror that names the component''s real props and suggests `text`.\n\nBoth halves verified by mutation on the real satellite, not argued from the\ntypes: the literal form accepted the typo, the SDK form failed with\n`TS2561 … Did you mean to write ''value''?`.\n\nWhat the compiler still cannot see, the builders throw on. A `Link.href` is a\nstring to TypeScript and an http(s) url to the catalog; data arriving from\nanywhere untyped lands there. Every builder parses as it builds, so the failure\nis on the line that wrote it rather than at the hub''s edge, three systems away.\n\nBuilders and nothing else\n--------------------------\nNo server, no router, no framework. A satellite is an ordinary HTTP service in\nwhatever stack its team already runs, and the moment this package has an opinion\nabout that it stops being adoptable by exactly the teams that most need it.\n\nThe builders are derived from the catalog rather than listed, for the same\nreason the agent''s schema is generated: a component added to the catalog gets a\nbuilder without anyone remembering, and the type is the whole catalog so it\ncannot drift.\n\n`satellite-orders` is written through it\n-----------------------------------------\nWhich is both the proof and the example — a package nobody uses is a package\nnobody has checked. The migration is behaviour-preserving and the existing\nsuites say so: 812 unit and 42 integration tests pass unchanged, the deployed\nsatellite serves the same screens, and the conformance kit still gives it 8\npassed, 0 failed.\n\nThe envelope builders repay themselves in the same file. `ActionResponse` has\ncoherence rules that are real and easy to violate — a `validation` outcome must\nname a field, a failed one must not carry a patch — and `ok`/`failed`/`invalid`\nmake the legal combinations the only ones expressible.\n\nVerified: 812 unit, 42 integration, 37 Python, 60 e2e.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0080f8b1d32b6194740aa2d19fec298ee8ebcc86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/0080f8b1d32b6194740aa2d19fec298ee8ebcc86"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/c98ee270f4086c1816723f0dbd2161a8d790cf9e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/c98ee270f4086c1816723f0dbd2161a8d790cf9e","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKGM5OGVlMjcwZjQwODZjMTgxNjcyM2YwZGJkMjE2MWE4ZDc5MGNmOWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/5b66a9267aef0817270ae46afb34fedb245749af","sha":"5b66a9267aef0817270ae46afb34fedb245749af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/5b66a9267aef0817270ae46afb34fedb245749af"}],"sha":"c98ee270f4086c1816723f0dbd2161a8d790cf9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/c98ee270f4086c1816723f0dbd2161a8d790cf9e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/5b66a9267aef0817270ae46afb34fedb245749af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T16:49:21Z","email":"15125586+myhumblecoder@users.noreply.github.com","name":"MyHumbleCoder"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17