ing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/5b66a9267aef0817270ae46afb34fedb245749af","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDViNjZhOTI2N2FlZjA4MTcyNzBhZTQ2YWZiMzRmZWRiMjQ1NzQ5YWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/19fa58c310f779d78ccac6e3c1fc6933b23788db","sha":"19fa58c310f779d78ccac6e3c1fc6933b23788db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/19fa58c310f779d78ccac6e3c1fc6933b23788db"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/44daf3df62d0f1c95e8abf03d091228c566ff947","sha":"44daf3df62d0f1c95e8abf03d091228c566ff947","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/44daf3df62d0f1c95e8abf03d091228c566ff947"}],"sha":"5b66a9267aef0817270ae46afb34fedb245749af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/5b66a9267aef0817270ae46afb34fedb245749af"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/44daf3df62d0f1c95e8abf03d091228c566ff947/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T16:41:17Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T16:41:17Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"fix(conformance): the audience check passed satellites that have none\n\nCode review of PR #19. Nine findings, eight applied, one answered with a\ncomment — and the first is the tool''s own headline claim.\n\nA tick that survived deleting the thing it checks\n--------------------------------------------------\n\"Refuses an undeclared audience\" treated a 403 as proof of an audience check.\nBut `authorize()` answers 403 for a missing *scope* just as readily, and the\nprobe''s default scopes are deliberately empty — so on every first run against a\nsatellite that requires any scope at all, the kit awarded a green tick that\nwould have survived deleting the satellite''s audience enforcement entirely.\n\nThis is the single most security-critical claim the kit makes, and my own file\nacknowledged the ambiguity forty lines further down, where it treats the same\n403 as \"cannot tell\". I trusted it in one place and doubted it in the other.\n\nIt establishes a baseline now: the correctly-audienced principal must be\n*accepted* on that path before a refusal of the foreign one means anything.\nVerified by mutation, independently of the suite the review added — a satellite\nthat refuses everyone equally gets \"unchecked\", one that actually distinguishes\ngets the pass. Both directions, because a check that never passes is as useless\nas one that always does.\n\nConfirmed against the running stack, too: with `fleet.read` the fleet satellite\nearns the tick; without it the kit now says the refusal proves nothing and names\nthe remedy.\n\nThat makes three checks in this session that looked like guards and guarded\nnothing — the cross-projection test, an e2e that asserted 200 and called it\ndenied, and this. The pattern is that I write the assertion I expect to pass\nrather than the one that would fail if the property were absent.\n\nThe rest\n--------\nThe timeout cleared as soon as headers arrived, so `response.json()` was\nunbounded — a satellite answering 200 and then stalling its body hung the CLI\nforever, with no output and no exit code, which is precisely what the timeout\nexists to prevent. `AbortSignal.timeout` stays armed through the body.\n\nThe auth probes always used `screens[0]`, so a satellite that validates its\nquery string before authenticating would have all three security checks report\ndefects it does not have. It picks a parameterless screen now. The fleet\nsatellite orders its screens favourably by luck.\n\nAn empty scope string produced a principal every satellite rejects with 401, and\nthe kit then blamed the satellite for its own malformed token. And the\nentry-point guard I added last commit was narrower than the class it claimed to\nclose: it missed conditional `exports`, missed `bin` entirely — on the very\npackage whose `bin` motivated it — and never scanned `apps/`.\n\nAlso: the CLI was committed non-executable, so the linked `portal-conformance`\nshim failed with EACCES; and an audience mismatch was reported with advice about\nscopes that no scope value could satisfy.\n\nLeft as documentation: `scopes` is ignored when a full `principal` is supplied.\nThat is intended — an override is an override — and now says so.\n\nVerified: 790 unit, 42 integration, 37 Python, 60 e2e against a rebuilt stack.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"93381d83d40c79cc051bf764c718e18116abbded","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/93381d83d40c79cc051bf764c718e18116abbded"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/44daf3df62d0f1c95e8abf03d091228c566ff947","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/44daf3df62d0f1c95e8abf03d091228c566ff947","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDQ0ZGFmM2RmNjJkMGYxYzk1ZThhYmYwM2QwOTEyMjhjNTY2ZmY5NDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/69fdaab9d82afa6d1f891018cf16a32790ea6f06","sha":"69fdaab9d82afa6d1f891018cf16a32790ea6f06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/69fdaab9d82afa6d1f891018cf16a32790ea6f06"}],"sha":"44daf3df62d0f1c95e8abf03d091228c566ff947","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/44daf3df62d0f1c95e8abf03d091228c566ff947"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/69fdaab9d82afa6d1f891018cf16a32790ea6f06/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T16:28:37Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T16:28:37Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"feat(conformance): the command a satellite team runs before we do\n\nM3 step 16, first half. `pnpm conformance http://localhost:4001` tells a team\nwhether the hub will accept their service, in a minute, from their own terminal\n— instead of from the hub failing strangely in an environment they cannot see.\nPLAN.md lists this beside the SDK as adoption ergonomics, and that is exactly\nwhat it is: the marginal cost of solution twenty has to equal solution three''s.\n\nIt checks what a schema cannot\n-------------------------------\nThat a satellite refuses an unsigned request, refuses a forged signature, and\nrefuses a principal from an audience it never declared are the claims the whole\ntenancy model rests on, and none of them are visible in a manifest. They are the\nfirst thing this probes, and both satellites pass — including the Python one,\nwhich shares no code with the kit and is still on protocol 1.0.\n\nA skip is never a pass\n----------------------\nFour states, and the distinction is the point. A screen behind a required\nparameter cannot be fetched without inventing a value. Tenant isolation cannot\nbe proved from outside with one tenant''s credentials. Both come back as\nunchecked, with a reason, and the run says so again at the end. A green result\nthat quietly omitted the half that mattered is worse than a red one.\n\nFound by running it on the real satellites\n-------------------------------------------\nThe first run failed `orders.list` with a 403 — and the satellite was right. The\nprobe held no scopes, because required scopes live in the hub''s registry rather\nthan the manifest, which a satellite team may not even have. The tool was\nblaming a satellite for its own ignorance. A 403 on a screen is now reported as\nunchecked with instructions, and `PORTAL_CONFORMANCE_SCOPES` lets an operator\nsupply them.\n\nThe default is still no scopes, deliberately: a satellite that serves a screen\nto a scopeless principal has a problem worth seeing.\n\nA gap the type system does not close\n-------------------------------------\nThis package shipped its first draft with no `index.ts` at all — two writes of\nit died on shell validation and nothing noticed. `tsc` passed, because it\ncompiles a directory rather than an entry point, so a `package.json` naming a\nfile nobody wrote is clean. The e2e import found it.\n\nThere is now a test asserting every workspace package''s declared `main`, `types`\nand `exports` resolve to a file that exists. Six packages, one assertion, and\nthe class of bug is closed rather than this instance of it.\n\nVerified: 786 unit, 42 integration, 37 Python, 60 e2e — the last including the\nkit run against both deployed satellites and against the hub, which is not a\nsatellite and fails once, clearly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"876ce0129abec308790f1459ee72162d4147de6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/876ce0129abec308790f1459ee72162d4147de6e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/69fdaab9d82afa6d1f891018cf16a32790ea6f06","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/69fdaab9d82afa6d1f891018cf16a32790ea6f06","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDY5ZmRhYWI5ZDgyYWZhNmQxZjg5MTAxOGNmMTZhMzI3OTBlYTZmMDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/19fa58c310f779d78ccac6e3c1fc6933b23788db","sha":"19fa58c310f779d78ccac6e3c1fc6933b23788db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/19fa58c310f779d78ccac6e3c1fc6933b23788db"}],"sha":"69fdaab9d82afa6d1f891018cf16a32790ea6f06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/69fdaab9d82afa6d1f891018cf16a32790ea6f06"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/19fa58c310f779d78ccac6e3c1fc6933b23788db/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T16:17:00Z","email":"15125586+myhumblecoder@users.noreply.github.com","name":"MyHumbleCoder"},"comment_count":0,"committ