m/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/19fa58c310f779d78ccac6e3c1fc6933b23788db","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDE5ZmE1OGMzMTBmNzc5ZDc4Y2NhYzZlM2MxZmM2OTMzYjIzNzg4ZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/4ab171582c5b63bfa29ca3dbcb6fc3854848b8fc","sha":"4ab171582c5b63bfa29ca3dbcb6fc3854848b8fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/4ab171582c5b63bfa29ca3dbcb6fc3854848b8fc"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/6edfba08e7499d4ba4ef3354bfdb2adbd5f0d20e","sha":"6edfba08e7499d4ba4ef3354bfdb2adbd5f0d20e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/6edfba08e7499d4ba4ef3354bfdb2adbd5f0d20e"}],"sha":"19fa58c310f779d78ccac6e3c1fc6933b23788db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/19fa58c310f779d78ccac6e3c1fc6933b23788db"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/6edfba08e7499d4ba4ef3354bfdb2adbd5f0d20e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T15:54:43Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T15:54:43Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"fix(mcp-server): a compliance control the new endpoint did not honour\n\nCode review of PR #18. Nine findings, seven applied by the review, one I took\nthat it deferred to me, one left with a reason.\n\nA tenant that withdrew consent reached everything anyway\n---------------------------------------------------------\n`PORTAL_AGENT_DISABLED_TENANTS` is described in this repository as tenants who\n\"have not agreed to AI processing, or have withdrawn it\", and in PLAN.md as a\ncompliance control. `/api/agent` refuses them. `/api/mcp`, serving the identical\ntool surface to an arbitrary MCP host, did not — so a withdrawn tenant reached\nevery solution through Claude Desktop.\n\nThe review left the fix to me because `isAgentEnabled` is the wrong gate here:\nit returns false without `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, and the outward endpoint needs no\nkey of ours — the model belongs to whoever connects. That is exactly why the\ncombined check let it through. The two questions were one function, and the\nanswer to \"is our agent configured\" is not the answer to \"has this tenant\nagreed to be served by an agent\".\n\nSplit into `isAgentAllowedForTenant`, which governs the surface rather than\nwhose model reaches it, and unit-tested where it is decided — a container runs\nas one tenant, so an end-to-end test could only exercise the allowed path and\nwould assert nothing about the denied one. I had in fact written that vacuous\ne2e test first, asserting 200 and calling the variable `denied`; it is gone.\n\nA comment that asserted something about someone else''s code, untested\n---------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe double cast on the transport options was justified with \"omitting the key\nwould turn sessions on\". The review checked, by instantiating both: the\ntransport assigns `options.sessionIdGenerator` and later tests `=== undefined`,\nso omission and explicit undefined are byte-identical. The cast was unnecessary\nand it erased type checking across the whole options object — a typo in\n`enableJsonResponse` would have compiled and silently reverted to SSE, hanging\nevery JSON-mode host.\n\nComments claiming properties the code lacks is a habit I have been caught on\nrepeatedly. This is the first time the claim was about a dependency''s behaviour\nrather than my own, which makes it worse: it was checkable in one line and I\nasserted it instead.\n\nThe rest\n--------\n`buildAgentSurface` was unguarded, so a missing registry path or principal\nsecret escaped as Next''s HTML error page — to a client that speaks JSON-RPC. It\nanswers a JSON-RPC error now, the same rule the agent route already followed.\n\n\"Is this tool listed\" had two spellings, one filtering the listing and one\nscanning a freshly built copy of it per call. Two spellings of the rule that\nkeeps a governed write uncallable is how it stops being one. It is a predicate\nboth use now.\n\nAlso: `agentInvokerDeps` took two parameters and used neither; `agentInvoker`\nduplicated the block it returns; the package declared an SDK it never imports\nand omitted two workspace packages its tests do.\n\nLeft: `GET`/`DELETE` on the MCP route. A stateless server needs neither, the\nofficial client copes, and adding them means a second transport instance for a\n405 with a better header.\n\nVerified: 772 unit, 42 integration, 37 Python, 55 e2e against a rebuilt stack.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fcc9b21a49ca46c72566aeb8aa66faa8eb2fe206","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/fcc9b21a49ca46c72566aeb8aa66faa8eb2fe206"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/6edfba08e7499d4ba4ef3354bfdb2adbd5f0d20e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/6edfba08e7499d4ba4ef3354bfdb2adbd5f0d20e","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDZlZGZiYTA4ZTc0OTlkNGJhNGVmMzM1NGJmZGIyYWRiZDVmMGQyMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/3323a310e78786618358bbdd7799bc904a0e6ace","sha":"3323a310e78786618358bbdd7799bc904a0e6ace","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/3323a310e78786618358bbdd7799bc904a0e6ace"}],"sha":"6edfba08e7499d4ba4ef3354bfdb2adbd5f0d20e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/6edfba08e7499d4ba4ef3354bfdb2adbd5f0d20e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/3323a310e78786618358bbdd7799bc904a0e6ace/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T15:34:40Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T15:34:40Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"feat(mcp-server): the hub as one governed endpoint\n\nM3 step 13. A staff member points Claude Desktop or an IDE agent at\n`/api/mcp` and reaches every solution their account can reach — the same tools\nthe in-hub assistant gets, filtered by the same `entitle()` the screens use. The\ndifference is the wire, not the policy.\n\nVerified against the running stack over real JSON-RPC: initialize, tools/list\nacross both satellites — including the Python one, which ships no MCP server and\nis reached entirely through the shim — and tools/call returning a satellite''s\nactual rows.\n\nGoverned writes are absent, and refuse anyway\n----------------------------------------------\nA confirmation is a person being shown what is about to happen in a screen the\nhub renders. A host cannot render that, and handing the decision to a client we\ndo not control would leave the hub the choke point on paper and not in fact.\n\nSo they are not listed. Listing one would be worse than omitting it: a tool that\nalways refuses reads as a capability and is a dead end. But absence is not a\ngate — a host that guessed the name would walk straight around it — so calling\none by name is refused explicitly, with a message saying where to approve it.\n\nThe consequence, said plainly rather than discovered: the outward MCP surface is\nread-only except for writes a registry policy has explicitly ungoverned. The\nserver''s `instructions` name the missing actions and where they happen, because\nan agent that cannot see a tool will otherwise tell the user the thing is\nimpossible when it is merely elsewhere.\n\nStateless, one server per request\n----------------------------------\nNo session id, JSON responses, nothing kept between calls. Two replicas share\nnothing and a restart costs a host a reconnect. The surface is rebuilt per\nrequest for the same reason the agent''s is: a satellite that changed what it\noffers should be reflected on the next call, not whenever a session happens to\nend.\n\nTwo casts at the SDK boundary, both explained in place. The transport''s\nstateless mode is `sessionIdGenerator: undefined` — the SDK''s own documentation\nshows that call — but its type marks the property optional rather than\n`| undefined`, which `exactOptionalPropertyTypes` reads as \"may be absent, may\nnot be undefined\". Omitting the key turns sessions on, so the assertion is the\nsafer of the two available mistakes.\n\nVerified: 764 unit, 42 integration, 37 Python, 55 e2e.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6a37868865b86798ed13fff8b1b5be7f7cc4c4a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/6a37868865b86798ed13fff8b1b5be7f7cc4c4a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/3323a310e78786618358bbdd7799bc904a0e6ace","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/3323a310e78786618358bbdd7799bc904a0e6ace","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDMzMjNhMzEwZTc4Nzg2NjE4MzU4YmJkZDc3OTliYzkwNGEwZTZhY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/4ab171582c5b63bfa29ca3dbcb6fc3854848b8fc","sha":"4ab171582c5b63bfa29ca3dbcb6fc3854848b8fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/4ab171582c5b63bfa29ca3dbcb6fc3854848b8fc"}],"sha":"3323a310e78786618358bbdd7799bc904a0e6ace","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/3323a310e78786618358bbdd7799bc904a0e6ace"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/4ab171582c5b63bfa29ca3dbcb6fc3854848b8fc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T15:25:43Z","email":"15125586+myhumblecoder@users.noreply.github.com","name":"MyHumbleCoder"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T15:25:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Merge pull request #17 from myhumblecoder-dev/feat/entitlem