b.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/4ab171582c5b63bfa29ca3dbcb6fc3854848b8fc","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDRhYjE3MTU4MmM1YjYzYmZhMjljYTNkYmNiNmZjMzg1NDg0OGI4ZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/68816819c66899302af3da828e9ffcac7db03897","sha":"68816819c66899302af3da828e9ffcac7db03897","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/68816819c66899302af3da828e9ffcac7db03897"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/32e52f194a85d9863cb65ad63c00bd2741e66de8","sha":"32e52f194a85d9863cb65ad63c00bd2741e66de8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/32e52f194a85d9863cb65ad63c00bd2741e66de8"}],"sha":"4ab171582c5b63bfa29ca3dbcb6fc3854848b8fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/4ab171582c5b63bfa29ca3dbcb6fc3854848b8fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/32e52f194a85d9863cb65ad63c00bd2741e66de8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T14:43:25Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T14:43:25Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"fix: the guard would not have caught the bug it was written for\n\nCode review of PR #17. Eight findings, seven applied, one skipped with reason —\nand the first is the whole point of the change.\n\nThe headline guard guarded nothing\n-----------------------------------\nThe cross-projection test asserted that a projected tool''s audience was a subset\nof its satellite''s, and that a non-empty catalog implied an external satellite.\nNeither statement involves the layer the bug is in. A façade reading only the\naction''s audience and ignoring the registry tool policy — the exact bug this PR\nexists to fix — passes all sixty cases. So does a gateway that drops the\nmanifest layer entirely.\n\nVerified by mutation rather than by argument, twice, on the restored code:\nreintroducing the pre-PR `offered()` now fails 12 of 60; dropping the gateway''s\nmanifest layer fails 42. Before the strengthening, both passed clean.\n\nIt now resolves every published resource, operation and tool back to *all* of\nits enclosing layers and asserts containment against each. That is the\ndifference between a test shaped like a guard and a guard.\n\nWorth saying plainly: I wrote that test in the same commit where I corrected a\ntautology two lines above it, and described it as the fix for the class. A\nweak assertion and a vacuous one are the same failure at different scales, and\nI caught the small one while writing the large one.\n\nThe disagreement moved one declaration along\n---------------------------------------------\n`publishes()` omitted the tool-policy layer while `offered()` included it — so\nthe façade and the gateway still disagreed, now about *reads*. A registry entry\ngoverning `orders.list` pins that tool internal for an agent while the public\nAPI served the same screen to a partner and never demanded its scopes. Both\nnarrow identically now.\n\nThe rest\n--------\n`combine()` accepts a missing layer, so the \"or nothing\" branch for an optional\ntool policy is stated once instead of at each call site — which is the same\nclass of omission this PR is about, one level quieter. `satelliteLayer()` moved\ninto the entitlement module for the same reason: a PR arguing against\nrestatement had left two copies of the shape most likely to be miscopied.\n\nAlso: the effective audience is deduplicated, because `AudienceListSchema`\nchecks membership and emptiness but not uniqueness, and the result is serialised\ninto MCP tool descriptors; the destructuring cast is gone; the test uses the\n`isAudienceSubset` that already exists; and `offered()`''s comment said a\ngoverned write demands the policy''s scopes \"rather than\" the satellite''s, when\nthe union means it demands both.\n\nOne I fixed differently than skipping it: the guard-on-the-guard counted what\nthe sweep exercised using counters mutated across sibling tests, which fails\nunder a `-t` filter or a shuffled order — a false alarm on the one test whose\njob is to be trustworthy. It recounts by walking the cases itself now, and\nsurvives being run alone.\n\nVerified: 752 unit, 42 integration, 37 Python, 49 e2e.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2f038a86254b18982eb7ca0a57da2ab76fc69ccf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/2f038a86254b18982eb7ca0a57da2ab76fc69ccf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/32e52f194a85d9863cb65ad63c00bd2741e66de8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/32e52f194a85d9863cb65ad63c00bd2741e66de8","node_id":"C_kwDOT57zN9oAKDMyZTUyZjE5NGE4NWQ5ODYzY2I2NWFkNjNjMDBiZDI3NDFlNjZkZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commit/f6e10944887abb856c97f7b6652360ca1ff46d29","sha":"f6e10944887abb856c97f7b6652360ca1ff46d29","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/f6e10944887abb856c97f7b6652360ca1ff46d29"}],"sha":"32e52f194a85d9863cb65ad63c00bd2741e66de8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/32e52f194a85d9863cb65ad63c00bd2741e66de8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/commits/f6e10944887abb856c97f7b6652360ca1ff46d29/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T14:30:48Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T14:30:48Z","email":"thomasfgooch@gmail.com","name":"Thomas Gooch"},"message":"refactor: the narrowing rule, in one function instead of six\n\nSix times this rule has been applied to a call site rather than to the class,\nand six times it was wrong somewhere: the protocol''s screen check, the\nregistry''s tool check, the hub''s per-screen enforcement, the manifest-versus-\nregistry check, the MCP gateway, and — merged to main last week — the public\nfaçade, where a partner holding only a read scope could invoke a governed write.\nEvery one found by review. Every fix local. Which is precisely why there was\nalways a next one.\n\nThe rule\n--------\nAudience narrows: the effective audience is the intersection of every enclosing\nlayer, so an inner declaration can never widen an outer one. Scopes accumulate:\nthe union, because an inner policy adds a demand and never relieves the caller\nof an outer one.\n\n`entitle(principal, layers)` in `@portal/registry` states both once and returns\nthe effective audience alongside the decision, which is what makes the façade''s\nextra condition — \"and it must still be external\" — a one-line check on a real\nvalue rather than a seventh restatement. `combine(layers)` is the same narrowing\nwithout a principal, because the gateway builds descriptors long before it knows\nwho is asking.\n\n`toolPolicy()` goes with it. `tools[id]` is bare bracket access on a plain\nobject, `constructor` is a legal id, and reading `rbacScopes` off the `Object`\nfunction yields undefined — which a `?? []` turns into \"no scopes required\".\nThat was fixed in `shim.ts`, then reintroduced in `catalog.ts`, then fixed\nagain. It is one function now, so there is no third time.\n\nWhat the consolidation found\n----------------------------\nThe two projections disagreed. The façade read only the *action''s* audience\nwhile the gateway also narrowed by the registry tool policy''s, so the same\ndeclaration was internal to an agent and external to a partner. The governance\nfile''s silence meaning internal is the safer reading, so the façade tightened —\nand a test now pins it, because a behaviour change hidden inside a refactor is\nthe kind nobody notices until it matters.\n\nThe guard on the class\n----------------------\n`entitle()` fixes the code; a cross-projection test in the hub fixes the class.\nIt walks every legal combination of satellite, screen, action and tool-policy\naudience against both an internal and an external principal, and asserts that\nnothing an internal-only satellite declared reaches an external caller through\nany projection. Sixty cases.\n\nTwo things in it worth naming. Every assertion sits behind an `if`, so a\nrefactor that quietly emptied both projections would satisfy all of them and\nprove nothing — the suite counts what it exercised and fails if either\nprojection was never non-empty. And I had written\n`expect(principal.audience).toBe(principal.audience)`, which is a tautology and\nmy own most-repeated review finding; it asserts something now.\n\nVerified: 749 unit, 42 integration, 37 Python, 49 e2e. The existing suites\npassing unchanged is the evidence the refactor preserved behaviour everywhere it\nwas already right.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c860bdc700a711ccf04328a1a4e0839808fe1a7b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/trees/c860bdc700a711ccf04328a1a4e0839808fe1a7b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/myhumblecoder-dev/dynamic-portal/git/commits/f6e10944887abb856c97f7b6652360ca1ff46d29","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15125586?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/myhumblecoder","id":15125586,"login":"myhumblecoder","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MTI1NTg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/myhumblecoder