"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/edf7e65e8455a1091d4f9e27b0fa39dd4a4637f3","node_id":"C_kwDOT5_MGdoAKGVkZjdlNjVlODQ1NWExMDkxZDRmOWUyN2IwZmEzOWRkNGE0NjM3ZjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/d9f387dd08c6ed7d277d337b97f16b0f2bec8ecc","sha":"d9f387dd08c6ed7d277d337b97f16b0f2bec8ecc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/d9f387dd08c6ed7d277d337b97f16b0f2bec8ecc"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/3f34a493976e3766798f7abcf99ba08c7bedb6ea","sha":"3f34a493976e3766798f7abcf99ba08c7bedb6ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/3f34a493976e3766798f7abcf99ba08c7bedb6ea"}],"sha":"edf7e65e8455a1091d4f9e27b0fa39dd4a4637f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/edf7e65e8455a1091d4f9e27b0fa39dd4a4637f3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/3f34a493976e3766798f7abcf99ba08c7bedb6ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:05:41Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T13:05:41Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"message":"Stop diagnoseIdentity calling healthy office accounts unprovisioned\n\nAn `accounts`/`operations` account is filed only at\ncolleges/{collegeId}/officeStaff/{uid} — by design there is no users and no\nsuperadmins document for it. diagnoseIdentity decided \"does this account have\nan identity profile?\" from users and superadmins alone, so every correctly\nprovisioned office account was reported with the issue \"No identity profile\ndocument exists\" — and then, a few lines later, the same report displayed the\nvalid office roster row it had just found.\n\nThe report therefore contradicted itself, and it did so in the most expensive\nway available: it reads as a broken identity and invites a superadmin to run\nAccess Control → Identity repair against an account that needs no repair. That\nis the same false signal that sent the Fee Management investigation down the\nrepair path when the ledger problem was a rules-cost problem.\n\nThe check now runs after the roster lookup and counts a roster row as an\nidentity profile, via a new pure hasIdentityProfile() helper in\nidentityShared.ts alongside OFFICE_ROLES. A genuinely unprovisioned account —\nno users, no superadmins, no roster row — is still reported, unchanged.\n\nRole/college drift between the roster row and the token is still reported by\ndiagnoseIdentity''s own issues; this only fixes the false \"no profile at all\"\nverdict that existed alongside it.\n\nFour regression tests in officeStaff.test.ts, including the unprovisioned case\nthat must keep reporting.\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6044f5648700d0243584393dc1fdbbb99bccfd20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/git/trees/6044f5648700d0243584393dc1fdbbb99bccfd20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/git/commits/3f34a493976e3766798f7abcf99ba08c7bedb6ea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/3f34a493976e3766798f7abcf99ba08c7bedb6ea","node_id":"C_kwDOT5_MGdoAKDNmMzRhNDkzOTc2ZTM3NjY3OThmN2FiY2Y5OWJhMDhjN2JlZGI2ZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/25f3beb8280af977233d797dbedde489d567726b","sha":"25f3beb8280af977233d797dbedde489d567726b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/25f3beb8280af977233d797dbedde489d567726b"}],"sha":"3f34a493976e3766798f7abcf99ba08c7bedb6ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/3f34a493976e3766798f7abcf99ba08c7bedb6ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/25f3beb8280af977233d797dbedde489d567726b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:55:42Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T12:55:42Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"message":"Fix permission-denied on the fee student list by reordering rule operands\n\nThe Fee Management desk refused the top-level `students` read for the\nAccounts/Operations team while fee payments and structures loaded fine.\nThe rules were already live and current, the account was healthy, and the\nquery scope, ID-token college claim and profile college all matched, so no\namount of redeploying or identity repair could affect the outcome.\n\nThe cause was evaluation cost, not authorization outcome.\n\nisSuperadmin() ends in exists(superadmins/{uid}), so for any caller who is\nnot a claim-superadmin it costs one document access. It led both the\n`students` list rule and sameCollege(), so each candidate row was charged\ntwice — and || only short-circuits after the expensive operand has already\nrun. A list query evaluates its rule once per candidate document and\nFirestore permits at most 10 document accesses per request; the fee desk\nqueries the whole college roster, so the request ran far past the budget and\nFirestore refused the entire query. The refusal surfaces as a bare\n\"Missing or insufficient permissions\", indistinguishable from a genuine\ndenial, which is why it read as a permissions problem.\n\nTest the zero-cost claim-only predicates first so || short-circuits before\nany document access is spent. Both edits are pure operand reorderings of the\nsame || chains: no condition was added, removed or relaxed, and the boolean\nresult is identical for every input. isSuperadmin() still runs, and still\ngrants, for callers that genuinely fail the cheap check — including\nsuperadmins whose authority comes from a superadmins/{uid} document rather\nthan the claim.\n\nThis also removes a document access from every other sameCollege() caller.\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6eca6fc78dc60eaecf1da779521d0deb80e3c8b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/git/trees/6eca6fc78dc60eaecf1da779521d0deb80e3c8b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/git/commits/25f3beb8280af977233d797dbedde489d567726b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/25f3beb8280af977233d797dbedde489d567726b","node_id":"C_kwDOT5_MGdoAKDI1ZjNiZWI4MjgwYWY5NzcyMzNkNzk3ZGJlZGRlNDg5ZDU2NzcyNmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/54314365696af4f3b9a24ae8f5ddd96348486c80","sha":"54314365696af4f3b9a24ae8f5ddd96348486c80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/54314365696af4f3b9a24ae8f5ddd96348486c80"}],"sha":"25f3beb8280af977233d797dbedde489d567726b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/25f3beb8280af977233d797dbedde489d567726b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/54314365696af4f3b9a24ae8f5ddd96348486c80/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T11:08:08Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T11:08:08Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"message":"Make the accounts and operations teams visible and repairable\n\nThe Access Control page could not see the office teams at all: Identity repair\nwalked students/faculty/admins/hods/mentors/superadmins, and the audit looked\nup the same seven collections. `accounts` and `operations` are the only roles\nwith NO top-level profile collection — grantUserRole files them at\n`colleges/{collegeId}/officeStaff/{uid}` and nowhere else (\"Office roles have no\nprofile collection of their own\"). So every office account reported as having\nno profile document at all, which is false, and a superadmin had no way to\ndiagnose, deactivate or re-grant one from this page.\n\nThe same blind spot is in `syncMyIdentity`, and that is the part that bites:\nan office account whose claims went stale could not self-repair, so its only\nremedy was a superadmin — the exact loop this project has been trying to close.\n\n- `findOfficeRosterDocument`: a collectionGroup lookup on the roster, used only\n  when the users document is missing a piece the decision still needs, so a\n  healthy account pays nothing.\n- `resolveIdentityTarget` reads the roster''s `role` field. This is the one\n  deliberate exception to \"membership, never the document''s role field\", and\n  it is bounded three ways: the path holds two roles so membership genuinely\n  cannot say which; only PROVISIONABLE_ROLES in OFFICE_ROLES are accepted, so\n  a forged `superadmin` yields no role at all; and the callable still refuses\n  to raise an existing claim. The roster is written only by a superadmin\n  (grantUserRole and manageOfficeStaff refuse every other caller), so this is\n  a HIGHER trust bar than the `admins` collection already trusted above.\n  Pinned by six tests, including that a forged role mints nothing and that a\n  users document still wins over the roster so a demotion is not undone.\n- `diagnoseIdentity` now reports the roster row and names three real faults: an\n  office account with no roster row (unmanageable), a roster/claim role\n  disagreement, and a roster sitting under a different college than the claim.\n- `auditAndRepairIdentities` scans the roster as a subcollection — one `get`\n  when scoped to a college, a collectionGroup otherwise — and is in\n  DEFAULT_COLLECTIONS, with a dedicated \"Accounts / Operations only\" scope in\n  the UI rather than being folded into \"staff\", where it would silently walk\n  every college''s office staff on a pass scoped to admins and HODs.\n\nThis does not fix the open fee-ledger denial. The evidence there is conclusive\nand points elsewhere: the account is healthy and the query scope, token claim\nand profile all read PZIg0HN9vG2kMo4Sb0YM, yet\n`isOffice() && sameCollege(resource.data)` refuses the read — which only\nhappens if the deployed ruleset predates that clause. That is a rules deploy.\n\nVerified: root tsc clean, 575/575 client tests, functions tsc clean,\n1073/1073 functions tests (6 new), production build green.\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"62b567e7b4e17ba62c6ea5bb950d745e73cfd383","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/git/trees/62b567e7b4e17ba62c6ea5bb950d745e73cfd383"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/git/commits/54314365696af4f3b9a24ae8f5ddd96348486c80","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/54314365696af4f3b9a24ae8f5ddd96348486c80","node_id":"C_kwDOT5_MGdoAKDU0MzE0MzY1Njk2YWY0ZjNiOWEyNGFlOGY1ZGRkOTYzNDg0ODZjODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/a663dd38be963a6d53437bd785f5172b37f65fda","sha":"a663dd38be963a6d53437bd785f5172b37f65fda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/a663dd38be963a6d53437bd785f5172b37f65fda"}],"sha":"54314365696af4f3b9a24ae8f5ddd96348486c80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/54314365696af4f3b9a24ae8f5ddd96348486c80"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/a663dd38be963a6d53437bd785f5172b37f65fda/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:28:04Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T10:28:04Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"message":"Print the college scope on a refusal, not just the collection\n\nWith the account now proven healthy (role claim \"accounts\", collegeId claim\nmatching the users document, issues: []), and the labelled read proving that\nonly the top-level `students` list is refused while `colleges/{cid}/feePayments`\nand `feeStructures` are fine, the rule left to check is the one that authorises\nthat list: `isOffice() && sameCollege(resource.data)`.\n\n`isOffice()` and `canonicalRole(''accounts'')` both check out, so the rule as\nwritten should admit a college-scoped query. The one fact static analysis\ncannot settle is whether the two sides of the comparison are even the same\nvalue: the rule compares a document field against the CLAIM, while the query\nis pinned to the profile''s collegeId. When those disagree, the query matches\ndocuments the rules then refuse, and the denial is indistinguishable from a\nbroken account — which is exactly the confusion this branch was meant to end.\n\nThe refusal now prints all three ends:\n\n  the student list — Missing or insufficient permissions. (query scope:\n  PZIg0HN9vG2kMo4Sb0YM, token claim: PZIg0HN9vG2kMo4Sb0YM, profile:\n  PZIg0HN9vG2kMo4Sb0YM)\n\nEqual values mean the deployed rules are older than this file; unequal ones\nname the drift directly. Either way the next screenshot settles it without\nanother round of hypotheses.\n\nVerified: tsc clean, 575/575 client tests, production build green.\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"0975a7b03646a2c911cf56e50cbdaed8d9c7a805","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/git/trees/0975a7b03646a2c911cf56e50cbdaed8d9c7a805"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/git/commits/a663dd38be963a6d53437bd785f5172b37f65fda","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/a663dd38be963a6d53437bd785f5172b37f65fda","node_id":"C_kwDOT5_MGdoAKGE2NjNkZDM4YmU5NjNhNmQ1MzQzN2JkNzg1ZjUxNzJiMzdmNjVmZGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/de7e1d111095509ddc8c250680715405e1cf73a0","sha":"de7e1d111095509ddc8c250680715405e1cf73a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/de7e1d111095509ddc8c250680715405e1cf73a0"}],"sha":"a663dd38be963a6d53437bd785f5172b37f65fda","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/a663dd38be963a6d53437bd785f5172b37f65fda"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/de7e1d111095509ddc8c250680715405e1cf73a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T05:11:03Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T05:11:03Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"message":"Name WHICH fee read the rules refused\n\nThe identity audit came back clean for the accounts account: role claim\n\"accounts\", collegeId claim \"PZIg0HN9vG2kMo4Sb0YM\", an exact match with the\n`users` document, and `issues: []`. So every account-side cause is ruled out —\nmy three hypotheses were all wrong, and the refusal is in the rules for\nsomething the ledger actually reads.\n\nWhich brings the real defect to light: the ledger issues THREE reads\n(fee payments, fee structures, the student list) inside one `Promise.all`.\n`Promise.all` rejects on the first failure and discards the rest, so nothing\nanywhere recorded WHICH query the rules refused. The copy could only describe\na read generically, which is why this took a production identity audit to\neven narrow down.\n\n- the three reads are now settled independently and each carries a label\n- a new `LabelledReadError` names every refused read, not just the first: one\n  fault is common, but two are two different rules and two different fixes\n- it preserves `code`, so the classifier and the claim self-heal behave\n  exactly as before — pinned by a test, because a labelled error that stopped\n  looking like a denial would silently switch the self-heal off\n\nA test then caught a defect in this very commit: the `permission-denied`\nbranch of the copy dropped the detail entirely (only the `unknown` branch\never showed it), so the new labels would never have reached the screen. Both\nbranches now carry them — knowing the account is healthy does not tell you\nwhich collection''s rule is refusing.\n\nVerified: tsc clean, 575/575 client tests, production build green.\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2d88af8a387400f8d51855f924af23b259a71d40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/git/trees/2d88af8a387400f8d51855f924af23b259a71d40"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/git/commits/de7e1d111095509ddc8c250680715405e1cf73a0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/de7e1d111095509ddc8c250680715405e1cf73a0","node_id":"C_kwDOT5_MGdoAKGRlN2UxZDExMTA5NTUwOWRkYzhjMjUwNjgwNzE1NDA1ZTFjZjczYTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/7e84cbc32b37c6bcbccc227adf513ed4b5ad9c18","sha":"7e84cbc32b37c6bcbccc227adf513ed4b5ad9c18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/7e84cbc32b37c6bcbccc227adf513ed4b5ad9c18"}],"sha":"de7e1d111095509ddc8c250680715405e1cf73a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/de7e1d111095509ddc8c250680715405e1cf73a0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/7e84cbc32b37c6bcbccc227adf513ed4b5ad9c18/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T18:04:37Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T18:04:37Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"message":"Stop asking Firestore for more than 10,000 rows\n\nThe production desks reported:\n\n  invalid-argument: Limit value in the structured query is over the\n  maximum value of 10000\n\nThat is the new error copy earning its keep — it named the real cause where\nthe old one said \"check the browser console\". It is also a bug that was never\na permissions problem at all: Firestore validates `limit()` before the query\nruns, so every call above 10000 threw on every request, every time, since it\nwas written. The desks have been failing on these reads and reporting an\nunexplained \"could not load\".\n\nEight call sites, all in the office module — exactly the two desks that\nfailed (accounts reads libraryFines; operations reads libraryLoans, assets\nand more):\n\n  libraryApi.ts  libraryTitles, libraryCopies, libraryLoans x2,\n                 libraryFines, libraryVisits\n  inventoryApi.ts  assets, stockMovements\n\n- new `cappedLimit` / `warnIfTruncated` in shared/utils/firestoreLimits.\n  Clamping to the cap is strictly better than today: nothing that worked\n  before stops working, because nothing that worked before ever ran.\n- the desk-facing reads warn when a result comes back AT the cap, because a\n  silently truncated read is a different lie from one that throws — a\n  college with more than 10,000 rows would otherwise get a count that\n  looks complete and is quietly wrong. That is a pagination problem and\n  this says so instead of hiding it.\n\nAlso: a permission denial that SURVIVED the self-heal now says so. The\ncopy previously said \"press Retry\" even after the app had already called\nsyncMyIdentity and the read was still refused, walking the reader round the\nsign-out loop a second time. After a failed heal it names the account —\nIdentity repair, and the account row must name a college — because that is\nthe fix, and an account with no college on it cannot be repaired from the\npage at all. `useOfficeSelfHeal` exposes `hasHealed` for exactly this.\n\nVerified: tsc clean, 574/574 client tests (7 new), production build green.\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d240a41623b62304f0662c05a61bd93374a1db08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/git/trees/d240a41623b62304f0662c05a61bd93374a1db08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/git/commits/7e84cbc32b37c6bcbccc227adf513ed4b5ad9c18","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/7e84cbc32b37c6bcbccc227adf513ed4b5ad9c18","node_id":"C_kwDOT5_MGdoAKDdlODRjYmMzMmIzN2M2YmNiY2NjMjI3YWRmNTEzZWQ0YjVhZDljMTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/3bcfb271ddf704a0df68e4cfd17328e2d59fa6f8","sha":"3bcfb271ddf704a0df68e4cfd17328e2d59fa6f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/3bcfb271ddf704a0df68e4cfd17328e2d59fa6f8"}],"sha":"7e84cbc32b37c6bcbccc227adf513ed4b5ad9c18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/7e84cbc32b37c6bcbccc227adf513ed4b5ad9c18"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/3bcfb271ddf704a0df68e4cfd17328e2d59fa6f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T16:39:17Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T16:41:56Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"message":"Show curriculum coverage to the teacher, and say which side of a cohort mismatch is wrong\n\nTwo gaps, both visible on the retest screenshots.\n\n1. The faculty curriculum page showed the PLAN only. It had no coverage\n   concept at all — `FacultyCurriculumView` and `ParsedModule` carried no\n   completed/covered field, and `getFacultyCurriculum` never read the\n   `facultyTopics` ledger. So a teacher who marked topics covered on the\n   attendance page saw nothing change on the page that lists those topics;\n   the only place coverage was ever rendered was the student portal, which\n   the teacher never sees.\n\n   - new pure `curriculumCoverage.ts`: normalises topic keys, indexes the\n     ledger, classifies a module''s topics. No Firebase, so it is testable.\n   - `fetchFacultyTopicLedger` reads the ledger under BOTH id spellings a\n     teacher is filed under (auth uid and faculty/{doc}), because\n     `completeClassSession` writes rows under either and a uid-only query\n     silently drops half the history.\n   - overview cards show \"Topics done\"; each module gets a progress bar and\n     per-topic ticks, and a denied ledger says the badges are missing rather\n     than letting empty bars imply \"you have taught nothing\".\n   - a ledger row that names its subject is filed under that subject ONLY:\n     indexing it under the bare topic as well leaked one subject''s coverage\n     into every other subject sharing a title (\"Introduction\" is everywhere).\n\n2. The student curriculum said \"No curriculum has been mapped to your class\n   yet\" while the college had mapped subjects that were all being excluded by\n   the cohort filter. That is a false statement that points the reader at the\n   wrong side — the same one-sided advice the roster notice was giving.\n\n   - new `diagnoseCohortExclusion` asks the matcher a question the stored data\n     can answer: for each field, how many mappings would match if ONLY that\n     field were ignored. Returned as `cohortDiagnosis` and rendered as both\n     sides — \"your record: A · mapped subjects use: SEP · matching them just\n     on this would bring back 16 subjects\" — with the fix offered on either\n     side.\n   - a field blank on the mapping is a wildcard and can never be the excluding\n     one, so it is never named; a row that already matched is never counted as\n     \"recovered\"; rows wrong in two fields are reported as needing both.\n\nTests: 13 new client tests for the ledger join, 10 new functions tests for the\ndiagnosis. The diagnosis tests corrected two wrong assumptions of mine — a\nblank student field is a deliberate wildcard in the matcher, and blanking an\nalready-blank field recovers nothing — both now pinned.\nVerified: root tsc clean, 567/567 client tests, functions tsc clean,\n1067/1067 functions tests, production build green.\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f030e037f3deeb43b958a09ac2a306930f0da298","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/git/trees/f030e037f3deeb43b958a09ac2a306930f0da298"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/git/commits/3bcfb271ddf704a0df68e4cfd17328e2d59fa6f8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/3bcfb271ddf704a0df68e4cfd17328e2d59fa6f8","node_id":"C_kwDOT5_MGdoAKDNiY2ZiMjcxZGRmNzA0YTBkZjY4ZTRjZmQxNzMyOGUyZDU5ZmE2Zjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/9676e58e47521c339dc95b7f608994f6e8f95978","sha":"9676e58e47521c339dc95b7f608994f6e8f95978","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/9676e58e47521c339dc95b7f608994f6e8f95978"}],"sha":"3bcfb271ddf704a0df68e4cfd17328e2d59fa6f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/3bcfb271ddf704a0df68e4cfd17328e2d59fa6f8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/9676e58e47521c339dc95b7f608994f6e8f95978/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:50:33Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T12:50:33Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"message":"Let the office desks repair their own claims, and say what actually failed\n\nProduction retest of #93 found two failures that the code audit had missed.\n\n1. The accounts/operations desks and the fee ledger could not self-heal a\n   stale collegeId claim. The rules authorise those reads from the ID-token\n   claim (`isOffice()` is `role() in [''accounts'',''operations''] && collegeId()\n   != null`), while the college name in the header comes from the profile\n   document — so an account in that state shows a college and is refused\n   every tenant read, and the only remedy on the page was a manual sign-out.\n   The faculty pages already had the one-shot repair; the desks did not.\n   - new `useOfficeSelfHeal()`: one `ensureIdentityClaims()` attempt, then\n     one retry (the repair is a no-op when the token already agrees, and the\n     one-shot guard stops a broken account looping the callable per click).\n   - AccountsDesk / OperationsDesk run it inside the `OfficeReadError` retry,\n     before refetching: a retry on an unrepaired token fails identically.\n   - useFeeData runs the same attempt on a permission-denied load error and\n     retries once when claims were re-issued.\n   - the `permission-denied` copy now says to press Retry first, since the\n     app repairs the claim itself.\n\n2. A failed read must name its cause. The `unknown` branch ended \"the details\n   are in the browser console\", which is not an instruction a college office\n   can act on; it now carries the real `code: message` and the desk passes the\n   error through. Tested in officeLinkage.test.ts.\n\n3. The roster exclusion notice no longer advises a one-sided fix. It used to\n   say \"Fix the semester / division / section on those students\" without\n   showing either side of the comparison — but the same message appears when\n   the CLASS is the odd one out (a schedule slot carrying a semester the\n   college does not teach). It now shows what this class is, what the\n   excluded students are actually recorded as (including \"(none)\"), and\n   offers the correction on whichever side is wrong. Correcting 123 student\n   records must never be a UI''s unilateral advice.\n\nVerified: root tsc --noEmit clean, 554/554 root unit tests, root production\nbuild, 1056/1056 functions unit tests, functions tsc build.\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"4b86295eb3c9e746a02adb7004aec0b6b3eaf473","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/git/trees/4b86295eb3c9e746a02adb7004aec0b6b3eaf473"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/git/commits/9676e58e47521c339dc95b7f608994f6e8f95978","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/9676e58e47521c339dc95b7f608994f6e8f95978","node_id":"C_kwDOT5_MGdoAKDk2NzZlNThlNDc1MjFjMzM5ZGM5NWI3ZjYwODk5NGY2ZThmOTU5Nzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/126195f1f0ff571c36b802a723537890461b2cd7","sha":"126195f1f0ff571c36b802a723537890461b2cd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/126195f1f0ff571c36b802a723537890461b2cd7"}],"sha":"9676e58e47521c339dc95b7f608994f6e8f95978","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/9676e58e47521c339dc95b7f608994f6e8f95978"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/126195f1f0ff571c36b802a723537890461b2cd7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T11:01:24Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T11:01:24Z","email":"317562256+smanoj1813-collab@users.noreply.github.com","name":"smanoj1813-collab"},"message":"Fix two \"your account is broken\" failures that read as \"you have no data\"\n\n1. Faculty \"Mark topics covered\" → \"Only college administrators (admin,\n   principal, HOD) can generate or cancel class sessions.\"\n\n   A teacher is filed under two different ids: the timetable, the curriculum\n   mappings and every class session generated from them key them by their\n   FACULTY PROFILE document id, while ownership and the auth claim are the\n   Firebase Auth UID. The session callables compared the two with `===`, so\n   completeClassSession answered \"You can only complete your own class\n   sessions\" for a class the teacher had just taught — and the client rendered\n   every permission failure in the file with the admin-only sentence, so the\n   real reason was thrown away.\n\n   - functions/src/classSchedule.ts\n     * one identity chain for every callable: normalizeRole + pickCollegeId +\n       a legacy staff-profile fallback (the treatment resolvePaperStaff already\n       has), so a claim reading \"Teacher\" and a users doc storing `collegeID`\n       stop failing every check;\n     * alias-aware ownership in ensureClassSession / completeClassSession /\n       getCurriculumProgress, with the caller''s own id kept on the session so\n       the readers that query by it still find it;\n     * the ledger candidate read spans the teacher''s ids, so completing a class\n       flips the row they planned against instead of creating a duplicate;\n     * a session with no collegeId falls back to its parent weekly slot.\n   - src/shared/utils/sessionErrorMessage.ts (new, pure, tested): per-callable\n     copy, and the server''s own message is never dropped.\n   - FacultyAttendance.tsx: one-shot claim self-heal + single retry, mirroring\n     the attendance save.\n   - sessionTopicsApi.ts: a covered topic keeps its \"already covered\" flag when\n     the curriculum row wins the de-duplication.\n\n2. Finance/operations desks: a refused read rendered as an empty college.\n\n   Audited the office↔college chain end to end: account creation\n   (grantUserRole writes users/, the officeStaff roster and the claims), sign-in\n   resolution, the claim self-heal, the permission matrix, the route gate, the\n   rules (isOffice/isFinance/isOps/isBackOffice cover every office collection)\n   and the payment callable all take the tenant correctly. Two things did not:\n\n   - feeApi scoped every query by localStorage alone, while the operations side\n     uses the signed-in identity; the client now passes the verified collegeId\n     through;\n   - useFeeData console.error-ed every load failure and carried on, so a\n     permission denial, an unlinked account and a missing index all rendered as\n     \"No students found for this college.\" — sending the accounts team to audit\n     student imports instead of the account.\n\n   - src/modules/admin/utils/officeLinkage.ts (new, pure, tested): classifies the\n     failure and names the one action that fixes it.\n   - Fee Management, the Record Payment and Assign-a-fee modals and both desks\n     now show a failed read instead of an empty college, with a Retry.\n\nTests: functions 1056 pass, client 553 pass, tsc --noEmit clean in both, both\nproduction builds green.\n\nCo-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"86fd621d969c8d3c51acbd6cc5c311b8db09c416","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/git/trees/86fd621d969c8d3c51acbd6cc5c311b8db09c416"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/git/commits/126195f1f0ff571c36b802a723537890461b2cd7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/317562256?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab","id":317562256,"login":"smanoj1813-collab","node_id":"U_kgDOEu2dkA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smanoj1813-collab","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/126195f1f0ff571c36b802a723537890461b2cd7","node_id":"C_kwDOT5_MGdoAKDEyNjE5NWYxZjBmZjU3MWMzNmI4MDJhNzIzNTM3ODkwNDYxYjJjZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commit/d9f387dd08c6ed7d277d337b97f16b0f2bec8ecc","sha":"d9f387dd08c6ed7d277d337b97f16b0f2bec8ecc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/d9f387dd08c6ed7d277d337b97f16b0f2bec8ecc"}],"sha":"126195f1f0ff571c36b802a723537890461b2cd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/smanoj1813-collab/Vriddhi/commits/126195f1f0ff571c36b802a723537890461b2cd7"},{"author