ts{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber","id":257923838,"login":"dhynesmnk-cyber","node_id":"U_kgDOD1-a_g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/55c8a35b74d148c3dcbffc20e1a58945e5ef652b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T08:12:48Z","email":"d.hynes.mnk@gmail.com","name":"dhynesmnk-cyber"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T08:12:48Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Allow the browser to actually reach Supabase from the deployed site (#11)\n\nconnect-src ''self'' in the CSP blocked every REST, Storage and Edge\nFunction call to the Supabase project (a different origin), with\nnothing louder than a CSP violation in the console — silently taking\nout the whole backend in production, admin included.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e19d75dbdb29d69afc843be018629a6171e68d80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/git/trees/e19d75dbdb29d69afc843be018629a6171e68d80"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/git/commits/55c8a35b74d148c3dcbffc20e1a58945e5ef652b","verification":{"payload":"tree e19d75dbdb29d69afc843be018629a6171e68d80\nparent 187d9ad1b49edf50a913cec7de1c18d268c5e1fa\nauthor dhynesmnk-cyber <d.hynes.mnk@gmail.com> 1787559168 +1000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787559168 +1000\n\nAllow the browser to actually reach Supabase from the deployed site (#11)\n\nconnect-src ''self'' in the CSP blocked every REST, Storage and Edge\nFunction call to the Supabase project (a different origin), with\nnothing louder than a CSP violation in the console — silently taking\nout the whole backend in production, admin included.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqi/0ACRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAb7sQAAs1S38UxeQje/6+L/wuZ4D+\n9PzMmT/4qxtuDmklTzDa0cG6BvHxh4MTOdIWzo3vUCS377Mjy5WxDDVIdYwtqRKb\n4887a7059lo51w47Drz/TSOQMrHcZJM74N9oEXDHsF9cu74th2QkMIRUpFKNSUnb\niGdlDvV7bFYXU+w/jfN4y3Q/BEx94JTxx+EUx64sVSd6eVWbuUzwd9+0btlQQl+s\nWJ7dzaIQyM8c93v+hkt8tGyg9vffJAF1Jtk/k8lRUmDEOJDkosdA9+jIWEEkO+fF\nmtGZe231bNpiUElZGVCRyopZgFH8rNWd+u+76AZmXF2Z169ePc/n3wiSmZPo5av7\nrljMmTUDG8BJiilgdUGWKQ0EeqOk7egVIf2mRdyknZdl3gQQKNgysklebM9OGVrr\nMOtHmIki90tP1408eCs5DUXfvUUcvYez51FU5jbUSeycY2LQowmAT15JNU2eJWc0\nM4R0XisNkkSahc5sR6m2+dsua2yXt01moCgf3erKkSsKLDnKCg24LHQjphH6GgPu\nEM6Kw7YggjTKyTnRXEx2D23Vgb8j2/uPQYz+OPOSc0r24cJpTB7xMeWUDwZcwltV\nEE+RBV5/iuZx88mr++ZAt2sMY9Mf+Ej+jXQjpHAUkg9oYatkexy7YLhy3LCKmgOt\nnkJcIDy19fNAgfOyTZDy\n=AKKn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T08:12:49Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/55c8a35b74d148c3dcbffc20e1a58945e5ef652b","node_id":"C_kwDOT6lY9doAKDU1YzhhMzViNzRkMTQ4YzNkY2JmZmMyMGUxYTU4OTQ1ZTVlZjY1MmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/187d9ad1b49edf50a913cec7de1c18d268c5e1fa","sha":"187d9ad1b49edf50a913cec7de1c18d268c5e1fa","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/187d9ad1b49edf50a913cec7de1c18d268c5e1fa"}],"sha":"55c8a35b74d148c3dcbffc20e1a58945e5ef652b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/55c8a35b74d148c3dcbffc20e1a58945e5ef652b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257923838?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber","id":257923838,"login":"dhynesmnk-cyber","node_id":"U_kgDOD1-a_g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/187d9ad1b49edf50a913cec7de1c18d268c5e1fa/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T07:32:06Z","email":"d.hynes.mnk@gmail.com","name":"dhynesmnk-cyber"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T07:32:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Let clients upload their own photos everywhere, and expand the style editor into 4 seasons (#10)\n\n* Let clients replace stock photos across the site, and store uploads properly\n\nProduct photo uploads (and now every stock photo used on Home, Winery,\nWeddings, Events and Trade) go through a new storeImage()/removeStoredImage()\nlayer in lib/media.ts: a public Supabase Storage bucket when a backend is\nconnected, IndexedDB in demo mode as before. Previously uploaded photos only\never lived in the admin''s own browser and never reached real site visitors —\nthis fixes that for the catalogue and extends the same capability to the\n7 stock photos (vines/cellarDoor/wedding/longTable/barrels/granite/bottles)\nvia a new \"Photos across the site\" panel in admin, plus an \"upload your own\"\noption for the homepage hero.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PUeUCA8yDAUow1PjZtXeyU\n\n* Let clients upload their own journal post photos too\n\nExtends the same upload path (lib/media.ts storeImage/removeStoredImage) to\njournal posts: the editor now has a real \"Upload a photo\" button alongside\nthe existing library picker and paste-a-URL field, and every place a post''s\nphoto renders (cards on Home/Journal, the post page itself, the admin list)\nresolves it through useStoredImage so an uploaded or IndexedDB-backed image\ndisplays correctly wherever it shows up.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PUeUCA8yDAUow1PjZtXeyU\n\n* Expand the style editor''s colours and fonts, curated into 4 seasons\n\nReplaces the flat 2-palette / 3-font pickers with a curated catalog of 8\ncolour palettes and 8 display fonts (data.ts: PALETTE_CATALOG, FONT_CATALOG),\neach tagged with a season and grouped under season headings in the admin\npicker (Website content -> Colours & type). Palette and font stay independent,\nfreeform choices as before -- the seasons are just how the now-larger option\nset is organised, not a forced bundle. New display fonts are added to the\nGoogle Fonts link in index.html.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PUeUCA8yDAUow1PjZtXeyU\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"102edac4385822233369e6099a8920541c5f6bc7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/git/trees/102edac4385822233369e6099a8920541c5f6bc7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/git/commits/187d9ad1b49edf50a913cec7de1c18d268c5e1fa","verification":{"payload":"tree 102edac4385822233369e6099a8920541c5f6bc7\nparent e1ab560aa002c798866196487f80551d6dd0f465\nauthor dhynesmnk-cyber <d.hynes.mnk@gmail.com> 1787556726 +1000\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787556726 +1000\n\nLet clients upload their own photos everywhere, and expand the style editor into 4 seasons (#10)\n\n* Let clients replace stock photos across the site, and store uploads properly\n\nProduct photo uploads (and now every stock photo used on Home, Winery,\nWeddings, Events and Trade) go through a new storeImage()/removeStoredImage()\nlayer in lib/media.ts: a public Supabase Storage bucket when a backend is\nconnected, IndexedDB in demo mode as before. Previously uploaded photos only\never lived in the admin''s own browser and never reached real site visitors —\nthis fixes that for the catalogue and extends the same capability to the\n7 stock photos (vines/cellarDoor/wedding/longTable/barrels/granite/bottles)\nvia a new \"Photos across the site\" panel in admin, plus an \"upload your own\"\noption for the homepage hero.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PUeUCA8yDAUow1PjZtXeyU\n\n* Let clients upload their own journal post photos too\n\nExtends the same upload path (lib/media.ts storeImage/removeStoredImage) to\njournal posts: the editor now has a real \"Upload a photo\" button alongside\nthe existing library picker and paste-a-URL field, and every place a post''s\nphoto renders (cards on Home/Journal, the post page itself, the admin list)\nresolves it through useStoredImage so an uploaded or IndexedDB-backed image\ndisplays correctly wherever it shows up.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PUeUCA8yDAUow1PjZtXeyU\n\n* Expand the style editor''s colours and fonts, curated into 4 seasons\n\nReplaces the flat 2-palette / 3-font pickers with a curated catalog of 8\ncolour palettes and 8 display fonts (data.ts: PALETTE_CATALOG, FONT_CATALOG),\neach tagged with a season and grouped under season headings in the admin\npicker (Website content -> Colours & type). Palette and font stay independent,\nfreeform choices as before -- the seasons are just how the now-larger option\nset is organised, not a forced bundle. New display fonts are added to the\nGoogle Fonts link in index.html.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PUeUCA8yDAUow1PjZtXeyU\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqi/N2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgBUQAHXhrOYBNSXD9YO3myMp6Fwt\nyZF4D1Jpp9NdMIrrybiRscYo4A178E6ll3Jh4vseu+hDesWjLS8VpJKOYcHAI0lB\nRuqIqPb5AhuAUj1DgvCj7aLn9D3crZwAnrecNMu5dEQLTphXfan3+mPYzLiBO5W5\nqx39miRWCxTtYJ6/XyK88Bo89DpdLr23L83bHiFUUN7SWC0zk