"subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/7ef4de389aee92a412d0f23f883d7b5e5df527bb","node_id":"C_kwDOT6lY9doAKDdlZjRkZTM4OWFlZTkyYTQxMmQwZjIzZjg4M2Q3YjVlNWRmNTI3YmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/e275e123bcb5375559215ec0960ba8fac7dc371f","sha":"e275e123bcb5375559215ec0960ba8fac7dc371f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/e275e123bcb5375559215ec0960ba8fac7dc371f"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/d98f73103f61f69d8c944c66c3e9afaf009fe19a","sha":"d98f73103f61f69d8c944c66c3e9afaf009fe19a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/d98f73103f61f69d8c944c66c3e9afaf009fe19a"}],"sha":"7ef4de389aee92a412d0f23f883d7b5e5df527bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/7ef4de389aee92a412d0f23f883d7b5e5df527bb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/d98f73103f61f69d8c944c66c3e9afaf009fe19a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T15:13:06Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T15:13:06Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add real business discovery to BeeSearch (Google Places + contact lookup)\n\nReplaces the \"no web crawl\" gap called out earlier: BeeSearch can now\nsearch actual nearby businesses instead of only the hand-kept sample,\nwhen a live backend and a Google Places API key are configured.\n\n- supabase/functions/beesearch-discover: text-searches Places for\n  stockists or planners within ~90 minutes, ranks by real distance,\n  caches results in a new beesearch_candidates table (0003 migration)\n  so a repeat search doesn''t re-spend money or reset a dismissed/\n  contacted business back to \"new\".\n- supabase/functions/beesearch-enrich: on request, for one chosen\n  business at a time, checks robots.txt then its own homepage for a\n  public contact email. Never a bulk crawl, never invents an address;\n  falls back to a manual-entry field when nothing is found or the\n  site disallows it.\n- Both require a real signed-in session (JWT verification stays on,\n  unlike admin-login) and write to Postgres under the caller''s own\n  session, never a service-role key.\n- BeeSearch.tsx: live results render through a new LiveCandidateCard\n  (distance, real reasons, website link, contact lookup, manual email\n  fallback, dismiss) alongside the existing demo-card path, chosen by\n  whether a backend is connected. The transparency panel now states\n  plainly which mode is active instead of a single blanket claim.\n- BEESEARCH.md: setup steps, cost pointers, and an explicit callout\n  that Spam Act consent for contacting a found business is the\n  operator''s judgement call, not something the tool decides.\n\nDemo mode (no backend configured) is unaffected — verified end to end\nin a browser — since none of this can be exercised without a real\nGoogle Places key the operator has to obtain themselves.","tree":{"sha":"06a1e907194ceaf8c25a017cedea10c71c2d089c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/git/trees/06a1e907194ceaf8c25a017cedea10c71c2d089c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/git/commits/d98f73103f61f69d8c944c66c3e9afaf009fe19a","verification":{"payload":"tree 06a1e907194ceaf8c25a017cedea10c71c2d089c\nparent 3e24bde44c5a54207c45063597fb373649392bd1\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787152386 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787152386 +0000\n\nAdd real business discovery to BeeSearch (Google Places + contact lookup)\n\nReplaces the \"no web crawl\" gap called out earlier: BeeSearch can now\nsearch actual nearby businesses instead of only the hand-kept sample,\nwhen a live backend and a Google Places API key are configured.\n\n- supabase/functions/beesearch-discover: text-searches Places for\n  stockists or planners within ~90 minutes, ranks by real distance,\n  caches results in a new beesearch_candidates table (0003 migration)\n  so a repeat search doesn''t re-spend money or reset a dismissed/\n  contacted business back to \"new\".\n- supabase/functions/beesearch-enrich: on request, for one chosen\n  business at a time, checks robots.txt then its own homepage for a\n  public contact email. Never a bulk crawl, never invents an address;\n  falls back to a manual-entry field when nothing is found or the\n  site disallows it.\n- Both require a real signed-in session (JWT verification stays on,\n  unlike admin-login) and write to Postgres under the caller''s own\n  session, never a service-role key.\n- BeeSearch.tsx: live results render through a new LiveCandidateCard\n  (distance, real reasons, website link, contact lookup, manual email\n  fallback, dismiss) alongside the existing demo-card path, chosen by\n  whether a backend is connected. The transparency panel now states\n  plainly which mode is active instead of a single blanket claim.\n- BEESEARCH.md: setup steps, cost pointers, and an explicit callout\n  that Spam Act consent for contacting a found business is the\n  operator''s judgement call, not something the tool decides.\n\nDemo mode (no backend configured) is unaffected — verified end to end\nin a browser — since none of this can be exercised without a real\nGoogle Places key the operator has to obtain themselves.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIWg4QRB\npP3Vx8qZfI4pysOVsgUF4nOeed5X9TWvjCP67hiJpesfQOaMRBTLR+IT6AGCdXiNRAHlZTWgcDAw\ntw8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T15:13:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/d98f73103f61f69d8c944c66c3e9afaf009fe19a","node_id":"C_kwDOT6lY9doAKGQ5OGY3MzEwM2Y2MWY2OWQ4Yzk0NGM2NmMzZTlhZmFmMDA5ZmUxOWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/3e24bde44c5a54207c45063597fb373649392bd1","sha":"3e24bde44c5a54207c45063597fb373649392bd1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/3e24bde44c5a54207c45063597fb373649392bd1"}],"sha":"d98f73103f61f69d8c944c66c3e9afaf009fe19a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/d98f73103f61f69d8c944c66c3e9afaf009fe19a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/3e24bde44c5a54207c45063597fb373649392bd1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-19T14:29:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-19T14:29:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Rename Bee23 to BeeSearch and rebuild it around real transparency\n\nThe outreach tool no longer runs a fake \"AI thinking\" animation before\nhanding back two hardcoded suggestion lists. Matches now come from a\nsmall named prospect directory, scored with plain, visible reasons\n(\"30 minutes from the valley\", \"books events of 70-130 guests —\noverlaps your booked range\") instead of a hidden score, and a\npermanent \"How BeeSearch actually works\" panel spells out that\nthere''s no web crawl behind it.\n\nData presentation: a live metrics row (targets tracked, in the\noutbox, sent, reply rate, converted to enquiries) computed straight\nfrom store state, plus custom target profiles now pick a real\ndirectory (stockist/planner) instead of falling back to hardcoded\nsuggestions.\n\nWorkflow integration: the outbox gained Replied and Converted states\n— a positive reply becomes a real enquiry in the pipeline with one\npress, carrying the contact details and match reasoning across, and\nthe Today dashboard gets a \"BeeSearch waiting on you\" card alongside\nthe other daily queues.\n\nRenamed throughout: Bee23Profile -> BeeSearchProfile, lead source\n''bee23'' -> ''beesearch'', bee23_profiles table -> beesearch_profiles\n(new migration, 0001 left untouched), nav label, tour copy.","tree":{"sha":"cecf708155ee0a7680cf633284e663e12edddcbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/git/trees/cecf708155ee0a7680cf633284e663e12edddcbc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/git/commits/3e24bde44c5a54207c45063597fb373649392bd1","verification":{"payload":"tree cecf708155ee0a7680cf633284e663e12edddcbc\nparent e275e123bcb5375559215ec0960ba8fac7dc371f\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787149750 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787149750 +0000\n\nRename Bee23 to BeeSearch and rebuild it around real transparency\n\nThe outreach tool no longer runs a fake \"AI thinking\" animation before\nhanding back two hardcoded suggestion lists. Matches now come from a\nsmall named prospect directory, scored with plain, visible reasons\n(\"30 minutes from the valley\", \"books events of 70-130 guests —\noverlaps your booked range\") instead of a hidden score, and a\npermanent \"How BeeSearch actually works\" panel spells out that\nthere''s no web crawl behind it.\n\nData presentation: a live metrics row (targets tracked, in the\noutbox, sent, reply rate, converted to enquiries) computed straight\nfrom store state, plus custom target profiles now pick a real\ndirectory (stockist/planner) instead of falling back to hardcoded\nsuggestions.\n\nWorkflow integration: the outbox gained Replied and Converted states\n— a positive reply becomes a real enquiry in the pipeline with one\npress, carrying the contact details and match reasoning across, and\nthe Today dashboard gets a \"BeeSearch waiting on you\" card alongside\nthe other daily queues.\n\nRenamed throughout: Bee23Profile -> BeeSearchProfile, lead source\n''bee23'' -> ''beesearch'', bee23_profiles table -> beesearch_profiles\n(new migration, 0001 left untouched), nav label, tour copy.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHuGDjtM\nuacXo2m/Iqx/5OWMmwVB2B+KxobYVopl07RPCvt9q+ZLIvq4iZoJQoWaRXTl+3FVZyAM6RosjOjt\nUA8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-19T14:29:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/