"repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/7456fd49107892ecf6a8e4e91ed940319fe37b2d","node_id":"C_kwDOT6lY9doAKDc0NTZmZDQ5MTA3ODkyZWNmNmE4ZTRlOTFlZDk0MDMxOWZlMzdiMmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/a932497cba73181cd01ab55efcbee4c40a2d309a","sha":"a932497cba73181cd01ab55efcbee4c40a2d309a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/a932497cba73181cd01ab55efcbee4c40a2d309a"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/c7c51111e8eafd48ddcf95241d646d33495c8679","sha":"c7c51111e8eafd48ddcf95241d646d33495c8679","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/c7c51111e8eafd48ddcf95241d646d33495c8679"}],"sha":"7456fd49107892ecf6a8e4e91ed940319fe37b2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/7456fd49107892ecf6a8e4e91ed940319fe37b2d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/c7c51111e8eafd48ddcf95241d646d33495c8679/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:34:38Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:34:38Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Fix undersized click targets found auditing the rest of the admin\n\nSwept every control in the admin — nine tabs plus the sub-panels the earlier\npass never opened: lead detail, the add-product form, the sequence preview, all\nthree CMS tabs, and the outreach review and results. Checked each button, link\nand tab for a missing accessible name, a crushed icon, a clipped label, a target\nunder 24px, and text contrast below 4.5:1.\n\nNothing else was invisible. No unnamed buttons, no zero-width icons, no clipped\nlabels, no console errors anywhere. The empty-box bug was confined to the two\nCMS editors already fixed.\n\nWhat the audit did find was targets too small to hit reliably:\n\n- The walkthrough''s 13 progress dots were 6x6px each. They''re now 6px of paint\n  centred in a 24x24 button, so they look the same and can actually be clicked.\n  The row is 336px, comfortable inside the 380px card.\n- Four links in Today were 16-20px tall: \"View all N\", \"Calendar\", \"Trade inbox\"\n  and \"See all\". Given a 28px minimum height and a little horizontal padding,\n  pulled back with negative margin so the layout doesn''t shift.\n- The calendar''s booking chips sat exactly on 24px. Nudged to 26.\n\nAlso gave the sequence preview dialog an Escape handler. Every other dialog in\nthe admin had one; that one didn''t.\n\nA note on method: the first pass reported contrast failures on nearly every\ncontrol, which were my measurement''s fault, not the UI''s — the checker couldn''t\nparse oklab() colours and didn''t composite alpha, so it was comparing text\nagainst garbage. Rewrote it with a real oklab-to-sRGB conversion and ancestor\ncompositing. The two contrast warnings that survive are full-screen scrim\nclick-catchers with no visible text, and are not real.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016XhaERdXqTvzFucZ1cTa83","tree":{"sha":"abaf143a18bee4721f6e1f397b0ba847ae44131d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/git/trees/abaf143a18bee4721f6e1f397b0ba847ae44131d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/git/commits/c7c51111e8eafd48ddcf95241d646d33495c8679","verification":{"payload":"tree abaf143a18bee4721f6e1f397b0ba847ae44131d\nparent 5179fe1df891dc522335c68144b961e15634a8e9\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787088878 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787088878 +0000\n\nFix undersized click targets found auditing the rest of the admin\n\nSwept every control in the admin — nine tabs plus the sub-panels the earlier\npass never opened: lead detail, the add-product form, the sequence preview, all\nthree CMS tabs, and the outreach review and results. Checked each button, link\nand tab for a missing accessible name, a crushed icon, a clipped label, a target\nunder 24px, and text contrast below 4.5:1.\n\nNothing else was invisible. No unnamed buttons, no zero-width icons, no clipped\nlabels, no console errors anywhere. The empty-box bug was confined to the two\nCMS editors already fixed.\n\nWhat the audit did find was targets too small to hit reliably:\n\n- The walkthrough''s 13 progress dots were 6x6px each. They''re now 6px of paint\n  centred in a 24x24 button, so they look the same and can actually be clicked.\n  The row is 336px, comfortable inside the 380px card.\n- Four links in Today were 16-20px tall: \"View all N\", \"Calendar\", \"Trade inbox\"\n  and \"See all\". Given a 28px minimum height and a little horizontal padding,\n  pulled back with negative margin so the layout doesn''t shift.\n- The calendar''s booking chips sat exactly on 24px. Nudged to 26.\n\nAlso gave the sequence preview dialog an Escape handler. Every other dialog in\nthe admin had one; that one didn''t.\n\nA note on method: the first pass reported contrast failures on nearly every\ncontrol, which were my measurement''s fault, not the UI''s — the checker couldn''t\nparse oklab() colours and didn''t composite alpha, so it was comparing text\nagainst garbage. Rewrote it with a real oklab-to-sRGB conversion and ancestor\ncompositing. The two contrast warnings that survive are full-screen scrim\nclick-catchers with no visible text, and are not real.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016XhaERdXqTvzFucZ1cTa83\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHZYezUg\n6xqXLCl991LIK19NuJixn/i/hmsf7Fk2/n2nOLZ7wVvIH2X4wPPzJc2zbhnOq0vM5wOgYFMRAp1D\nGAo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T21:34:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/c7c51111e8eafd48ddcf95241d646d33495c8679","node_id":"C_kwDOT6lY9doAKGM3YzUxMTExZThlYWZkNDhkZGNmOTUyNDFkNjQ2ZDMzNDk1Yzg2Nzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/5179fe1df891dc522335c68144b961e15634a8e9","sha":"5179fe1df891dc522335c68144b961e15634a8e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/5179fe1df891dc522335c68144b961e15634a8e9"}],"sha":"c7c51111e8eafd48ddcf95241d646d33495c8679","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/c7c51111e8eafd48ddcf95241d646d33495c8679"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/5179fe1df891dc522335c68144b961e15634a8e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:22:43Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T21:22:43Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Fix delete buttons rendering as empty boxes, and the cascade bug behind it\n\nThe delete controls in the CMS were bordered boxes with nothing in them. They\nworked, which made them more confusing, not less.\n\nThe cause: the button computed `padding: 11.2px 24px` despite carrying `px-0`.\n48px of horizontal padding inside a 44px-wide button leaves no content box, so\nthe icon was laid out at zero width — present in the DOM, invisible on screen.\n\n`px-0` was being ignored because `.btn` was unlayered CSS. Unlayered rules\noutrank anything in a layer regardless of specificity, so every Tailwind utility\nwritten next to a `.btn` was silently swallowed. I hit this once before and\nmoved only `display` into @layer components; padding, background, colour and\nmin-height had the same problem and were still losing.\n\nSo the fix is the rest of that same move: `.btn` and its variants, `.field-*`\nand `.kicker` now live in @layer components, below utilities, where a caller\nasking for `px-0` or `bg-bone` gets it.\n\nThat repaired three more controls that were invisible or wrong for the same\nreason, none of which had been noticed:\n- the mobile menu close button, `text-bone border-bone/60` ignored, so it was\n  rendering granite-on-granite against a granite panel. Now 14:1 contrast.\n- \"Place a trade order\" on the dark winery band, `bg-bone` ignored, so a\n  transparent button with dark text sat on a dark background.\n- the cart quantity steppers, `min-h-[34px]` ignored, so they were 48px.\n\nThe delete buttons themselves are now labelled. A bare minus glyph doesn''t say\n\"delete\" even when it renders, so they read as a trash icon plus the word\nDelete, in garnet, with a title naming what will go. The last row keeps its\nexisting \"can''t remove me\" disabled state, now with a tooltip saying why.\n\nAlso removed the 00/01/02/03 numerals from the mobile menu. I said these were\ngone site-wide two commits ago and they weren''t — my check only walked the\nrendered pages, and this markup only exists while the menu is open. They now\ncarry the same garnet-to-ochre hairline as the section heads.\n\nSwept every button on five public routes at two widths and all nine admin tabs:\nno crushed icons, no collapsed heights, no overflow, no console errors. Deleting\nstill deletes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016XhaERdXqTvzFucZ1cTa83","tree":{"sha":"e0499e36e72ad279749208f76c184479cf428cc4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/git/trees/e0499e36e72ad279749208f76c184479cf428cc4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/git/commits/5179fe1df891dc522335c68144b961e15634a8e9","verification":{"payload":"tree e0499e36e72ad279749208f76c184479cf428cc4\nparent 59c3a99f1d1281c23eb7c8d19ccbd80207038a32\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787088163 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787088163 +0000\n\nFix delete buttons rendering as empty boxes, and the cascade bug behind it\n\nThe delete controls in the CMS were bordered boxes with nothing in them. They\nworked, which made them more confusing, not less.\n\nThe cause: the button computed `padding: 11.2px 24px` despite carrying `px-0`.\n48px of horizontal padding inside a 44px-wide button leaves no content box, so\nthe icon was laid out at zero width — present in the DOM, invisible on screen.\n\n`px-0` was being ignored because `.btn` was unlayered CSS. Unlayered rules\noutrank anything in a layer regardless of specificity, so every Tailwind utility\nwritten next to a `.btn` was silently swallowed. I hit this once before and\nmoved only `display` into @layer components; padding, background, colour and\nmin-height had the same problem and were still losing.\n\nSo the fix is the rest of that same move: `.btn` and its variants, `.field-*`\nand `.kicker` now live in @layer components, below utilities, where a caller\nasking for `px-0` or `bg-bone` gets it.\n\nThat repaired three more controls that were invisible or wrong for the same\nreason, none of which had been noticed:\n- the mobile menu close button, `text-bone border-bone/60` ignored, so it was\n  rendering granite-on-granite against a granite panel. Now 14:1 contrast.\n- \"Place a trade order\" on the dark winery band, `bg-bone` ignored, so a\n  transparent button with dark text sat on a dark background.\n- the cart quantity steppers, `min-h-[34px]` ignored, so they were 48px.\n\nThe delete buttons themselves are now labelled. A bare minus glyph doesn''t say\n\"delete\" even when it renders, so they read as a trash icon plus the word\nDelete, in garnet, with a title naming what will go. The last row keeps its\nexisting \"can''t remove me\" disabled state, now with a tooltip saying why.\n\nAlso removed the 00/01/02/03 numerals from the mobile menu. I said these were\ngone site-wide two commits ago and they weren''t — my check only walked the\nrendered pages, and this markup only exists while the menu is open. They now\ncarry the same garnet-to-ochre hairline as the section heads.\n\nSwept every button on five public routes at two widths and all nine admin tabs:\nno crushed icons, no collapsed heights, no overflow, no console errors. Deleting\nstill deletes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016XhaERdXqTvzFucZ1cTa83\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKZFmvqe\nqLWRj0HbLudqkgmKOeftMNrme5GfLNL8Ln+Em0c9gauSWT2AZNwHnN+U91onD4GWozU4hzCawFfM\nagA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T21:22:46Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/5179fe1df891dc522335c68144b961e15634a8e9","node_id":"C_kwDOT6lY9doAKDUxNzlmZTFkZjg5MWRjNTIyMzM1YzY4MTQ0Yjk2MWUxNTYzNGE4ZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/59c3a99f1d1281c23eb7c8d19ccbd80207038a32","sha":"59c3a99f1d1281c23eb7c8d19ccbd80207038a32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/59c3a99f1d1281c23eb7c8d19ccbd80207038a32"}],"sha":"5179fe1df891dc522335c68144b961e15634a8e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/5179fe1df891dc522335c68144b961e15634a8e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/59c3a99f1d1281c23eb7c8d19ccbd80207038a32/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T20:50:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T20:50:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add a Postgres backend and a server-checked admin passcode\n\nEverything lived in localStorage, so \"saving\" meant saving on one device in one\nbrowser. This puts the data in Postgres and puts a passcode on the door.\n\nBoth are optional. With no env vars the app behaves exactly as it did before —\nseeded demo data, any passcode opens the office — which keeps deploy previews\nand local dev working. Set VITE_SUPABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY and the\nsame UI is talking to a database.\n\nSchema (supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql)\nTen tables: scalar columns for anything filtered or sorted, jsonb for the\ngenuinely nested bits (order lines, sequence steps), and site_config as a single\npinned row because it is really one document. Row Level Security is the point:\nanon may read products and site_config, and insert an enquiry or an order, and\nnothing else. Customer names, emails and phone numbers are unreadable without a\nsession. Signed-in admins get everything.\n\nThe passcode\n9876 is a function secret, not a constant in the bundle. The browser posts the\ncode to the admin-login Edge Function, which compares it in constant time after\na fixed delay, then signs in the fixed admin account and returns a real\nSupabase session. Since every policy demands `authenticated`, the session is the\nsecurity boundary and the passcode is just a convenient way to get one — reading\nthe JS reveals the project URL and the anon key, both public, and no route to a\ncustomer record. Changing the code later is `supabase secrets set`, no redeploy.\n\nData layer\nEvery mutation already funnelled through one setState, so rather than rewriting\neighteen callbacks as async, remote.ts diffs the previous state against the new\none and writes only the rows that moved, debounced. Writes are per-row, so two\npeople editing different leads don''t clobber each other. Without a session the\nsync narrows to inserting the new enquiry or order, because that is precisely\nwhat RLS permits — upserting would need UPDATE rights the anon key lacks and\nwould just generate noise on every keystroke.\n\nGuards worth calling out\n- \"Reset demo data\" is hidden once a backend is live. The diff sync would have\n  read a wholesale reseed as \"delete every row\" and taken the real enquiries,\n  orders and website copy with it.\n- Hydration keeps local data when a remote collection comes back empty. On the\n  public site the admin tables are empty because they''re forbidden, not because\n  they''re deleted, and blanking the site over that would be wrong.\n- A badge in the admin bar says Demo, Connecting, Saved or Offline, so nobody\n  types into the void wondering whether it stuck.\n- The passcode form carries a hidden username field; Chrome flagged the lone\n  password input as an accessibility problem.\n\nVerified in Chromium against a stub that mimics the REST, auth and function\nendpoints: public pages hydrate from the backend, a wrong code is refused and\nstays put, the right code opens the office, the session survives a reload, an\nadmin edit writes only the table that changed, and a visitor''s enquiry produces\nexactly one insert into leads and nothing else. Demo mode re-checked separately.\n\nNot verified: the SQL and the RLS policies themselves, which need a real project\nto run against. See BACKEND.md for setup and for what this design deliberately\ndoes not do.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016XhaERdXqTvzFucZ1cTa83","tree":{"sha":"45fbb1a1273c23f0c44e8def89beed82b1999e20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/git/trees/45fbb1a1273c23f0c44e8def89beed82b1999e20"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/git/commits/59c3a99f1d1281c23eb7c8d19ccbd80207038a32","verification":{"payload":"tree 45fbb1a1273c23f0c44e8def89beed82b1999e20\nparent 9fc18555d3d1c9ba6ac190f0cc5efbaa852533ad\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787086240 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787086240 +0000\n\nAdd a Postgres backend and a server-checked admin passcode\n\nEverything lived in localStorage, so \"saving\" meant saving on one device in one\nbrowser. This puts the data in Postgres and puts a passcode on the door.\n\nBoth are optional. With no env vars the app behaves exactly as it did before —\nseeded demo data, any passcode opens the office — which keeps deploy previews\nand local dev working. Set VITE_SUPABASE_URL and VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY and the\nsame UI is talking to a database.\n\nSchema (supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql)\nTen tables: scalar columns for anything filtered or sorted, jsonb for the\ngenuinely nested bits (order lines, sequence steps), and site_config as a single\npinned row because it is really one document. Row Level Security is the point:\nanon may read products and site_config, and insert an enquiry or an order, and\nnothing else. Customer names, emails and phone numbers are unreadable without a\nsession. Signed-in admins get everything.\n\nThe passcode\n9876 is a function secret, not a constant in the bundle. The browser posts the\ncode to the admin-login Edge Function, which compares it in constant time after\na fixed delay, then signs in the fixed admin account and returns a real\nSupabase session. Since every policy demands `authenticated`, the session is the\nsecurity boundary and the passcode is just a convenient way to get one — reading\nthe JS reveals the project URL and the anon key, both public, and no route to a\ncustomer record. Changing the code later is `supabase secrets set`, no redeploy.\n\nData layer\nEvery mutation already funnelled through one setState, so rather than rewriting\neighteen callbacks as async, remote.ts diffs the previous state against the new\none and writes only the rows that moved, debounced. Writes are per-row, so two\npeople editing different leads don''t clobber each other. Without a session the\nsync narrows to inserting the new enquiry or order, because that is precisely\nwhat RLS permits — upserting would need UPDATE rights the anon key lacks and\nwould just generate noise on every keystroke.\n\nGuards worth calling out\n- \"Reset demo data\" is hidden once a backend is live. The diff sync would have\n  read a wholesale reseed as \"delete every row\" and taken the real enquiries,\n  orders and website copy with it.\n- Hydration keeps local data when a remote collection comes back empty. On the\n  public site the admin tables are empty because they''re forbidden, not because\n  they''re deleted, and blanking the site over that would be wrong.\n- A badge in the admin bar says Demo, Connecting, Saved or Offline, so nobody\n  types into the void wondering whether it stuck.\n- The passcode form carries a hidden username field; Chrome flagged the lone\n  password input as an accessibility problem.\n\nVerified in Chromium against a stub that mimics the REST, auth and function\nendpoints: public pages hydrate from the backend, a wrong code is refused and\nstays put, the right code opens the office, the session survives a reload, an\nadmin edit writes only the table that changed, and a visitor''s enquiry produces\nexactly one insert into leads and nothing else. Demo mode re-checked separately.\n\nNot verified: the SQL and the RLS policies themselves, which need a real project\nto run against. See BACKEND.md for setup and for what this design deliberately\ndoes not do.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016XhaERdXqTvzFucZ1cTa83\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD21P6v8\n531NP/AIgHUgTuUDwawA0oUKviRJiNAdx5t41iFEiNrXNvrWclabJPDoEUkq0EDm6l6orrzBCKMv\ntQM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T20:50:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/59c3a99f1d1281c23eb7c8d19ccbd80207038a32","node_id":"C_kwDOT6lY9doAKDU5YzNhOTlmMWQxMjgxYzIzZWI3YzhkMTljY2JkODAyMDcwMzhhMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/9fc18555d3d1c9ba6ac190f0cc5efbaa852533ad","sha":"9fc18555d3d1c9ba6ac190f0cc5efbaa852533ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/9fc18555d3d1c9ba6ac190f0cc5efbaa852533ad"}],"sha":"59c3a99f1d1281c23eb7c8d19ccbd80207038a32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/59c3a99f1d1281c23eb7c8d19ccbd80207038a32"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/9fc18555d3d1c9ba6ac190f0cc5efbaa852533ad/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T06:33:35Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T06:33:35Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Replace stat boxes and index numerals with typed reviews, editable in admin\n\nThe site was leaning on two SaaS habits: bands of big numbers in divided\nboxes, and a ghost numeral bolted to the left of every heading. Both are\ngone, and what people actually say about the place takes their spot.\n\nRemoved\n- All four stat bands — Home (both variants), Winery, Weddings — along with\n  the Stat component itself.\n- The num-ghost index numeral from SectionHead; the `index` prop is gone and\n  all nine call sites updated. A short garnet-to-ochre hairline now carries\n  the structure the numeral used to.\n- The same numeral from the Events per-section headings, the \"01 —\" prefixes\n  from seven kickers, and the numbered badges from the home triptych panels.\nLeft alone deliberately: the 404 numeral and the oversized ✓ on the order and\nenquiry success screens. Those are functional glyphs, not marketing counters.\n\nAdded\n- TypedLines: a typewriter that writes one line at a time, holds, deletes and\n  moves to the next. Typing is the slowest thing on the page so it reads as\n  considered rather than as a spinner. The caret sits solid while writing and\n  blinks once the line rests.\n- Lines live in config.typedLines, each tagged to a page. An empty author\n  reads as a feature line; a filled one reads as a review, in quote marks with\n  the name underneath.\n- A \"Reviews & features\" tab in the admin CMS: per-page lists with counts, a\n  live preview of the animation, reorder and remove, and an undo.\n\nAccessibility and motion\n- The animated text is aria-hidden; screen readers get the full set as a\n  static list, so nobody hears a line being spelled out.\n- Under prefers-reduced-motion the line renders whole and the caret is hidden.\n  The media query is watched at runtime, not just read once at mount.\n- Hovering or focusing the block pauses the cycle.\n\nAlso\n- loadState now merges seed config defaults over persisted config. Without it,\n  anyone with existing localStorage would have hit config.typedLines being\n  undefined and crashed on first paint — and the same trap was waiting for\n  every future config field.\n\nVerified in Chromium: typing advances on all four pages, no num-ghost or\nnumbered kickers survive on any page, admin edits reach the live site, an old\nlocalStorage state migrates cleanly, and nothing overflows at 360/768/1440.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016XhaERdXqTvzFucZ1cTa83","tree":{"sha":"8fd477b5a6642fe1a25238aea69d02b20d937d85","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/git/trees/8fd477b5a6642fe1a25238aea69d02b20d937d85"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/git/commits/9fc18555d3d1c9ba6ac190f0cc5efbaa852533ad","verification":{"payload":"tree 8fd477b5a6642fe1a25238aea69d02b20d937d85\nparent c18adf5966c6ab4ae52ddbfc7491363a40336259\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787034815 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787034815 +0000\n\nReplace stat boxes and index numerals with typed reviews, editable in admin\n\nThe site was leaning on two SaaS habits: bands of big numbers in divided\nboxes, and a ghost numeral bolted to the left of every heading. Both are\ngone, and what people actually say about the place takes their spot.\n\nRemoved\n- All four stat bands — Home (both variants), Winery, Weddings — along with\n  the Stat component itself.\n- The num-ghost index numeral from SectionHead; the `index` prop is gone and\n  all nine call sites updated. A short garnet-to-ochre hairline now carries\n  the structure the numeral used to.\n- The same numeral from the Events per-section headings, the \"01 —\" prefixes\n  from seven kickers, and the numbered badges from the home triptych panels.\nLeft alone deliberately: the 404 numeral and the oversized ✓ on the order and\nenquiry success screens. Those are functional glyphs, not marketing counters.\n\nAdded\n- TypedLines: a typewriter that writes one line at a time, holds, deletes and\n  moves to the next. Typing is the slowest thing on the page so it reads as\n  considered rather than as a spinner. The caret sits solid while writing and\n  blinks once the line rests.\n- Lines live in config.typedLines, each tagged to a page. An empty author\n  reads as a feature line; a filled one reads as a review, in quote marks with\n  the name underneath.\n- A \"Reviews & features\" tab in the admin CMS: per-page lists with counts, a\n  live preview of the animation, reorder and remove, and an undo.\n\nAccessibility and motion\n- The animated text is aria-hidden; screen readers get the full set as a\n  static list, so nobody hears a line being spelled out.\n- Under prefers-reduced-motion the line renders whole and the caret is hidden.\n  The media query is watched at runtime, not just read once at mount.\n- Hovering or focusing the block pauses the cycle.\n\nAlso\n- loadState now merges seed config defaults over persisted config. Without it,\n  anyone with existing localStorage would have hit config.typedLines being\n  undefined and crashed on first paint — and the same trap was waiting for\n  every future config field.\n\nVerified in Chromium: typing advances on all four pages, no num-ghost or\nnumbered kickers survive on any page, admin edits reach the live site, an old\nlocalStorage state migrates cleanly, and nothing overflows at 360/768/1440.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016XhaERdXqTvzFucZ1cTa83\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIl8sfXS\n3l5pjVzfOZGYWTSj6ZKV6gBZYg0d+59YBRQKRBUFhP3bvsXWaBWyOsrBB+21FKx/FNqLCqJ6Ok5e\nygc=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T06:33:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/9fc18555d3d1c9ba6ac190f0cc5efbaa852533ad","node_id":"C_kwDOT6lY9doAKDlmYzE4NTU1ZDNkMWM5YmE2YWMxOTBmMGNjNWVmYmFhODUyNTMzYWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/c18adf5966c6ab4ae52ddbfc7491363a40336259","sha":"c18adf5966c6ab4ae52ddbfc7491363a40336259","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/c18adf5966c6ab4ae52ddbfc7491363a40336259"}],"sha":"9fc18555d3d1c9ba6ac190f0cc5efbaa852533ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/9fc18555d3d1c9ba6ac190f0cc5efbaa852533ad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/c18adf5966c6ab4ae52ddbfc7491363a40336259/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T06:10:33Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T06:10:33Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Soften the UI motion and rebuild the admin walkthrough as a guided tour\n\nTwo things, plus the bugs they turned up.\n\nLuxury motion layer (src/index.css)\nThe brutalist bones are untouched — 2px rules, hard offsets, flat colour.\nWhat changes is the air around them. Every hard shadow now carries a soft\nambient companion, state changes glide on a long ease (--ease-lux) instead\nof snapping, and nothing moves more than a few pixels:\n\n- layered lift tokens, and a barely-there warm radial wash behind the bone\n- buttons get a slow background sheen (ridden on background-position, not a\n  pseudo-element, so the cart badge inside its button isn''t clipped) plus a\n  letter-spacing bloom\n- .lux-lift / .lux-card / .lux-zoom / .lux-sheen for surfaces and photography\n- reveals settle out of a 4px blur; .stagger walks children in sequence\n- routes and admin sections fade-rise on change rather than cutting\n- nav underline becomes a garnet-to-ochre hairline\nEvery addition has a prefers-reduced-motion counterpart.\n\nAdmin walkthrough (src/components/Walkthrough.tsx)\nReplaces the fixed six-step modal with a spotlight tour that has three\nshapes of step: anchored (cuts a hole around a [data-tour] element and docks\nthe card to whichever side has room), docked (light scrim, card in the\ncorner, so the section being described stays readable), and centred. Thirteen\nsteps now cover every section, switching tabs as they go. Keyboard driven\n(arrows, Esc), jumpable via the progress dots, and — new — replayable at any\ntime from \"Tour\" in the top bar, which it previously wasn''t once dismissed.\n\nFixes found along the way\n- Overview read t.items on a TradeOrder, which has `lines`. Any trade order\n  in the seed crashed the admin landing page. Now sums bottles from lines.\n- .btn set `display` from unlayered CSS, which outranks Tailwind''s utilities\n  layer, so `hidden sm:inline-flex` never hid a button. Moved just that\n  declaration into @layer components. This un-breaks the responsive header,\n  the mobile-only \"Back\" in Leads, and FieldArea''s min-height.\n- The admin top bar overflowed horizontally below 640px (609px of content in\n  a 360px bar). Controls now step up by breakpoint, with sign-out and the\n  live-site link moving into the mobile section drawer. No overflow at\n  360/390/640/768/1024/1280/1440.\n- Tour card is height-capped with its prose scrolling, so the controls stay\n  reachable on a short viewport.\n- Entry animations changed from `both` to `backwards` fill: a filled-forwards\n  animation outranks normal author rules, so `transform: none` was going to\n  lock out every hover zoom.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016XhaERdXqTvzFucZ1cTa83","tree":{"sha":"424db8edfb8ecfee80b7f136cdb6fca42ccf3292","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/git/trees/424db8edfb8ecfee80b7f136cdb6fca42ccf3292"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/git/commits/c18adf5966c6ab4ae52ddbfc7491363a40336259","verification":{"payload":"tree 424db8edfb8ecfee80b7f136cdb6fca42ccf3292\nparent a932497cba73181cd01ab55efcbee4c40a2d309a\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787033433 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787033433 +0000\n\nSoften the UI motion and rebuild the admin walkthrough as a guided tour\n\nTwo things, plus the bugs they turned up.\n\nLuxury motion layer (src/index.css)\nThe brutalist bones are untouched — 2px rules, hard offsets, flat colour.\nWhat changes is the air around them. Every hard shadow now carries a soft\nambient companion, state changes glide on a long ease (--ease-lux) instead\nof snapping, and nothing moves more than a few pixels:\n\n- layered lift tokens, and a barely-there warm radial wash behind the bone\n- buttons get a slow background sheen (ridden on background-position, not a\n  pseudo-element, so the cart badge inside its button isn''t clipped) plus a\n  letter-spacing bloom\n- .lux-lift / .lux-card / .lux-zoom / .lux-sheen for surfaces and photography\n- reveals settle out of a 4px blur; .stagger walks children in sequence\n- routes and admin sections fade-rise on change rather than cutting\n- nav underline becomes a garnet-to-ochre hairline\nEvery addition has a prefers-reduced-motion counterpart.\n\nAdmin walkthrough (src/components/Walkthrough.tsx)\nReplaces the fixed six-step modal with a spotlight tour that has three\nshapes of step: anchored (cuts a hole around a [data-tour] element and docks\nthe card to whichever side has room), docked (light scrim, card in the\ncorner, so the section being described stays readable), and centred. Thirteen\nsteps now cover every section, switching tabs as they go. Keyboard driven\n(arrows, Esc), jumpable via the progress dots, and — new — replayable at any\ntime from \"Tour\" in the top bar, which it previously wasn''t once dismissed.\n\nFixes found along the way\n- Overview read t.items on a TradeOrder, which has `lines`. Any trade order\n  in the seed crashed the admin landing page. Now sums bottles from lines.\n- .btn set `display` from unlayered CSS, which outranks Tailwind''s utilities\n  layer, so `hidden sm:inline-flex` never hid a button. Moved just that\n  declaration into @layer components. This un-breaks the responsive header,\n  the mobile-only \"Back\" in Leads, and FieldArea''s min-height.\n- The admin top bar overflowed horizontally below 640px (609px of content in\n  a 360px bar). Controls now step up by breakpoint, with sign-out and the\n  live-site link moving into the mobile section drawer. No overflow at\n  360/390/640/768/1024/1280/1440.\n- Tour card is height-capped with its prose scrolling, so the controls stay\n  reachable on a short viewport.\n- Entry animations changed from `both` to `backwards` fill: a filled-forwards\n  animation outranks normal author rules, so `transform: none` was going to\n  lock out every hover zoom.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016XhaERdXqTvzFucZ1cTa83\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOaWtxbq\nrBwSTO0M+DzDvqyaDDr47Gufr19PDq9CFstpJr0wokloO+bf6mXdr+44cvN0aeoiOkyf5X8rdeOh\naQA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T06:10:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/c18adf5966c6ab4ae52ddbfc7491363a40336259","node_id":"C_kwDOT6lY9doAKGMxOGFkZjU5NjZjNmFiNGFlNTJkZGJmYzc0OTEzNjNhNDAzMzYyNTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commit/a932497cba73181cd01ab55efcbee4c40a2d309a","sha":"a932497cba73181cd01ab55efcbee4c40a2d309a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/a932497cba73181cd01ab55efcbee4c40a2d309a"}],"sha":"c18adf5966c6ab4ae52ddbfc7491363a40336259","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/c18adf5966c6ab4ae52ddbfc7491363a40336259"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/257923838?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dhynesmnk-cyber","id":257923838,"login":"dhynesmnk-cyber","node_id":"U_kgDOD1-a_g","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dhynesmnk-cyber","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dhynesmnk-cyber/Harcourt-valley/commits/a932497cba73181cd01ab55efcbee4c40a2d309a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T04:04:00Z","email":"d.hynes.mnk@gmail.com","name":"dhynesmnk-cyber"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T04:04:00Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Merge pull request #2 from dhynesmnk-cyber/elegant-admin-interface-redesign-1fbfd\n\nUpdate from task 784299d6-61a9-40b9-9640-feae63c1fbfd","tree":{"sha":"1b8eeb3b1120f0dcd18a4770bf899ba24221752b","url":"https://api.github.