before the download lands\nstill streams the song, and a song already playing is never swapped out.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"29d20840c4f246a7c7c6c52ac7bc6517b6de6540","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/trees/29d20840c4f246a7c7c6c52ac7bc6517b6de6540"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/commits/a96a4cf295db9b27ce53db4d01433eae18938401","verification":{"payload":"tree 29d20840c4f246a7c7c6c52ac7bc6517b6de6540\nparent 0b19534a6cc981690fce88c82d70573c129b84b8\nauthor Liane Nguyen <101995278+lianenguyen150@users.noreply.github.com> 1791183553 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791183553 -0700\n\nfix(save-the-date): start the song as soon as the record is tapped (#29)\n\nOn a phone the song only began downloading when the record was tapped,\nholding the music back by about a second. Download it while the card\nopens and play it from memory instead. A tap before the download lands\nstill streams the song, and a song already playing is never swapped out.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw0rBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAlyEQAC8aozAPdzPzfZtwrkomPsfJ\nzpPT6Rm+LN6DG2y9mRGL/z/iWA/Nb1Yp97buckY9noQmlqgwQt3DKMcgSKv6qYY9\nB667BbXe7OsHw+pDPc6Wr2/Fq3VbAKokltvSoR8R8R23FgafLQCL/q7qAQffv0pK\nxuaiIiTfv1bFuUYl4cYJ/HJRV0NVzlfo5799jrLDAOot2f0ABkIuwpO/yyPoBmvx\nBjWTc3XaeY5I579FG2zhrRHGFyj6gdreAIX9ygWAFDIyXamy3vCDsJq65ANfY13E\ncZmOjYorAz3SkRjq9TZOhLu7TMqiER+uCXp9hKSvVr5Lv5P8VHQuxwVxtqRb66Ow\nrFMDHypxt/tsKwqVwzyQ25hoxKsrrIeG+5/lb6BLRHpUI5TjjrDmxCMCsEj/saW1\nMdAJ8LTzLs7YzgjQ8LpSCu9j7N1dKj2FKkm/PX2Dg8reeD7QAfTz4RhSuGTHioOz\nWpwK9VHDOBWTbkjueCBl4fOQAIggjyMwTnXZxycF0fjHgIG9p8oPvaYmIU2L4zwN\nJEnRDP819BdNfp0Qy7WMfByLYelA4N6VBqCJFLeLa6UhjDm5anLJwEUnuQa/xQi1\nbmXVRJRaG1tZS2QOX3FDRuR+JEtE7cWMOQusSjMyCjdqKazzU1O/2EWCJYmTqMNf\nROiL6ddXS5ZQiCyh2lD0\n=zod9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T06:59:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72/mocha/commit/a96a4cf295db9b27ce53db4d01433eae18938401","node_id":"C_kwDOT6yInNoAKGE5NmE0Y2YyOTVkYjliMjdjZTUzZGI0ZDAxNDMzZWFlMTg5Mzg0MDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72/mocha/commit/0b19534a6cc981690fce88c82d70573c129b84b8","sha":"0b19534a6cc981690fce88c82d70573c129b84b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/0b19534a6cc981690fce88c82d70573c129b84b8"}],"sha":"a96a4cf295db9b27ce53db4d01433eae18938401","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/a96a4cf295db9b27ce53db4d01433eae18938401"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101995278?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lianenguyen150","id":101995278,"login":"lianenguyen150","node_id":"U_kgDOBhRTDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/0b19534a6cc981690fce88c82d70573c129b84b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T06:46:32Z","email":"101995278+lianenguyen150@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Liane Nguyen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T06:46:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(save-the-date): stop the envelope shaking when tapped on a phone (#28)\n\nThe envelope''s hover lift and press squeeze watched any <button> in the stage, and\nthe opened invitation''s record, Add to calendar and open-again buttons live there too.\nPhones leave :hover stuck on whatever was tapped, so every tap jolted the envelope:\nup and back as it opened, up as it began to reseal, and down 3px once it had closed\nand the open-again button went away.\n\nThe lift, seal swell and press now follow only the envelope''s own button, and only on\ndevices with a fine, hovering pointer. The cards'' pointer parallax ignores touch, so a\ntap no longer drags them toward the finger and back.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"951d14003b38bddf0ffb1c39b3fb0d5aff9999b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/trees/951d14003b38bddf0ffb1c39b3fb0d5aff9999b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/commits/0b19534a6cc981690fce88c82d70573c129b84b8","verification":{"payload":"tree 951d14003b38bddf0ffb1c39b3fb0d5aff9999b2\nparent 21e05350240e74929e13bd2f9125449135434267\nauthor Liane Nguyen <101995278+lianenguyen150@users.noreply.github.com> 1791182792 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791182792 -0700\n\nfix(save-the-date): stop the envelope shaking when tapped on a phone (#28)\n\nThe envelope''s hover lift and press squeeze watched any <button> in the stage, and\nthe opened invitation''s record, Add to calendar and open-again buttons live there too.\nPhones leave :hover stuck on whatever was tapped, so every tap jolted the envelope:\nup and back as it opened, up as it began to reseal, and down 3px once it had closed\nand the open-again button went away.\n\nThe lift, seal swell and press now follow only the envelope''s own button, and only on\ndevices with a fine, hovering pointer. The cards'' pointer parallax ignores touch, so a\ntap no longer drags them toward the finger and back.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqw0fICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8xkQAFp7GCvTB2QdqexVOQ/0CNg9\n+z/qyLtD09svddxP9Wc2giY/Sixr/+pU21KpDZ+O+RFfj5AWW8weXyRKn56YCdGK\ngEAC/otr4H/0hgnXExIFbVm5ub3btgNt/V60lJeDQR9y6sn8t7gvZpuIGKKiv8qd\nVdjwCqeh1ZNjSP/tka2qcb5ryhirFeNVKfqgr1LTriduF4xTuR6vavHzpw3AOpoy\nXTw9HIwDKiW2XP9X8zGWEOJiR4Ro6p4Ljr/itpF8ncenhuHxZPxAGEk7phTApMR1\nW5uTh881xx+wEqwF9V1p0P5zJzCum891iNGJWzRUx5q++e5JHCw38q2IU8bO2fbD\nx3vgtxPZ3ko+0DeDchuiJ1LwfgaU5kl7nEFoi5CD2hHH/AlB6VZWZ5JeEJbjaviH\nqZSe3aiBowhu7jjIv/9Lx3hcj47bTp6PfZQ/3SFrBePcXcc3J+/PtZiLbuufrz+G\nuY96uskGbGj3lbCEKdq23hoX5K6/uCzBGRCi1AO/zXq6fUNVhC/SlIRIpL95ilqL\n+l73fKnScgiO63SnpHw0SOd+kGSAW5gKJ2hgLFyXc8q6rtyIlzNGC/UUdLgkUt4E\nKMc5kdXIQc+KMO5pi4InaJC9eP/HnZw3uBI8v/BS2jJLLPdtrhWVLXWpawzg2I7N\n3ZeT4m9tegK42/SE1wMF\n=HPn1\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T06:46:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72/mocha/commit/0b19534a6cc981690fce88c82d70573c129b84b8","node_id":"C_kwDOT6yInNoAKDBiMTk1MzRhNmNjOTgxNjkwZmNlODhjODJkNzA1NzNjMTI5Yjg0Yjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72/mocha/commit/21e05350240e74929e13bd2f9125449135434267","sha":"21e05350240e74929e13bd2f9125449135434267","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/21e05350240e74929e13bd2f9125449135434267"}],"sha":"0b19534a6cc981690fce88c82d70573c129b84b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/0b19534a6cc981690fce88c82d70573c129b84b8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101995278?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lianenguyen150","id":101995278,"login":"lianenguyen150","node_id":"U_kgDOBhRTDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/21e05350240e74929e13bd2f9125449135434267/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-05T06:02:22Z","email":"101995278+lianenguyen150@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Liane Nguyen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-05T06:02:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(save-the-date): smooth the envelope opening, resealing and card fan-out (#27)\n\n* fix(save-the-date): smooth the envelope opening and deal the cards front to back\n\nThe flap''s per-keyframe easing brought it to rest standing upright, so it hung\nat 82-95deg for about 250ms mid-open; its two halves now meet at the same speed.\n\nThe cards crawled into their peak for ~250ms on a quint ease-out, then jumped\nfrom rest to 700-1000px/s in one frame on a back-out curve. The rise now eases\nin more gently and the fan-out starts from rest, keeping the same ~3% overshoot.\n\nThe cards are now dealt front to back (Polaroid, date, announcement), so each\none uncovers the next; the overall timing and OPENING_DURATION_MS are unchanged.\n\nThe record''s tap target was 30-33px on phones; an invisible 8px ring brings it\npast 44px without changing how it looks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(save-the-date): stop the envelope and seal snapping when opening and resealing\n\nOpening switched the sealed envelope''s float off in one frame, dropping it up to\n~3.4px, and swapped the hover-swollen seal (104%) for the cracking halves at\n100%. The stage now records the float offset and seal scale at the click, and\nthe envelope layers and seal halves ease back from there.\n\nThe reseal''s seal press ran one overshooting curve across both halves of its\nsquash, so it sat still for ~70ms in the squash and then jumped. Each half now\nhas its own curve: in fast, straight back out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(save-the-date): open the flap without the wind-up\n\nThe flap tipped -4deg toward the guest before swinging open, which read as the\nenvelope opening a little, closing, then opening fully. It now swings straight\nopen, with the two easing curves still meeting at 90deg at the same speed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(save-the-date): stop petals, the pressed seal and #open reloads popping in\n\n- The petals that start mid-fall appeared at full strength the instant the\n  envelope opened; the scatter now fades in as the seal cracks.\n- The resealed seal''s fade rode its press curve and jumped 30% in one frame;\n  it now has its own gentle fade.\n- A hard load of /#open (a reload, or a link copied after opening) showed the\n  prerendered sealed envelope for ~1.3s on a slow phone, then snapped open. An\n  inline script marks the page before first paint, and the stage stays hidden\n  while sealed, then fades in already open.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"60fb1c95eb78a4f6856fbe26bfed25f7849a20b2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/trees/60fb1c95eb78a4f6856fbe26bfed25f7849a20b2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/commits/21e05350240e74929e13bd2f9125449135434267","verification":{"payload":"tree 60fb1c95eb78a4f6856fbe26bfed25f7849a20b2\nparent ec08ff5b616166112b0f022016cdb5f855639848\nauthor Liane Nguyen <101995278+lianenguyen150@users.noreply.github.com> 1791180142 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791180142 -0700\n\nfix(save-the-date): smooth the envelope opening, resealing and card fan-out (#27)\n\n* fix(save-the-date): smooth the envelope opening and deal the cards front to back\n\nThe flap''s per-keyframe easing brought it to rest standing upright, so it hung\nat 82-95deg for about 250ms mid-open; its two halves now meet at the same speed.\n\nThe cards crawled into their peak for ~250ms on a quint ease-out, then jumped\nfrom rest to 700-1000px/s in one frame on a back-out curve. The rise now eases\nin more gently and the fan-out starts from rest, keeping the same ~3% overshoot.\n\nThe cards are now dealt front to back (Polaroid, date, announcement), so each\none uncovers the next; the overall timing and OPENING_DURATION_MS are unchanged.\n\nThe record''s tap target was 30-33px on phones; an invisible 8px ring brings it\npast 44px without changing how it looks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(save-the-date): stop the envelope and seal snapping when opening and resealing\n\nOpening switched the sealed envelope''s float off in one frame, dropping it up to\n~3.4px, and swapped the hover-swollen seal (104%) for the cracking halves at\n100%. The stage now records the float offset and seal scale at the click, and\nthe envelope layers and seal halves ease back from there.\n\nThe reseal''s seal press ran one overshooting curve across both halves of its\nsquash, so it sat still for ~70ms in the squash and then jumped. Each half now\nhas its own curve: in fast, straight back out.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(save-the-date): open the flap without the wind-up\n\nThe flap tipped -4deg toward the guest before swinging open, which read as the\nenvelope opening a little, closing, then opening fully. It now swings straight\nopen, with the two easing curves still meeting at 90deg at the same speed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(save-the-date): stop petals, the pressed seal and #open reloads popping in\n\n- The petals that start mid-fall appeared at full strength the instant the\n  envelope opened; the scatter now fades in as the seal cracks.\n- The resealed seal''s fade rode its press curve and jumped 30% in one frame;\n  it now has its own gentle fade.\n- A hard load of /#open (a reload, or a link copied after opening) showed the\n  prerendered sealed envelope for ~1.3s on a slow phone, then snapped open. An\n  inline script marks the page before first paint, and the stage stays hidden\n  while sealed, then fades in already open.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwz1uCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4SQQAHYcwJQKOIS8SIkMsZQrdbmG\nGOwV0ejz9f1osv8Yqy6zIzOB6dmdJZhpv4vyTSMjHEBxccFBkNcs07kGskxzBE8Z\nGtsvE7XQ+wUqg2SG5N4juQ1tqBDGHVkzpard0qXZAWc5e7I44mLEqq58oncRFmPu\nvtmnjz4ja8OS0Qp9nD5Ti50qmXIVpO8Bby2DwiRjGKC7bOVDtjfRSEObn70pXaPj\n6tqtFPO6Cu2bBmnH8h/AwlP5xxIVOMlanD/X+i9MdfGXnpl6sdff7Qa8yQ4cp5jK\n9O82qHcRy9JshbKLQ9aQPSUTdfX1skRP8vaKgkjhNTMrxNsGYGWSC/6SMGBsGoIR\nr8QeRTxAh12x9+noZpR99841lOWO0OTeHZcKRF5KaoOwUQBsT529rxpzGpWt+n52\nY62x4wJDCSDeq70K8qNy64qS1Xtm8ylhOiivHJ0SHW7osb4/oCoA76x3x5a1acoC\nRWyij7i554z9JJsaaZI0EjxTURUXQIP6RxNET0hHQ7wVT1pMVmyrk4pKowlM5552\ntNL0LvV+R1cDBzUWoQiVnPguo6KSqErqZHSznsxwOrkh2Z2B66eSx66hvF2li80I\nndSNJEyKo/xQVQdRuk8Gv6FS0mPcStBgwAmBKmQf6pb+SRJrmtPVmaBcIYIwXxIp\nXYDXprgRnlMSFslN7rJI\n=Hma+\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-05T06:02:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/g