rivacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lianenguyen150","id":101995278,"login":"lianenguyen150","node_id":"U_kgDOBhRTDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/d3aa4956068bf3afc00273426270926988afda86/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T23:06:57Z","email":"101995278+lianenguyen150@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Liane Nguyen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T23:06:57Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(save-the-date): tuck the invitation back in when opening it again (#24)\n\n* docs(save-the-date): design for resealing the envelope\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(save-the-date): tuck the invitation back in when opening it again\n\n\"Open again\" used to snap straight back to the sealed envelope. A new closing\nphase now plays the way back: the note clears away, the cards tuck into the\npocket top card first, the flap folds down, and a fresh wax seal presses on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(save-the-date): gather the cards into a stack before tucking them in\n\nRunning the opening keyframes backwards sent each card high above the\nenvelope and back, and its z-index step made cards pass behind one another\nmid-air. Now the cards straighten into a stack above the pocket and slide\nin together.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"196014007c8521f67940b354cfa9f10299630a2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/trees/196014007c8521f67940b354cfa9f10299630a2d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/commits/d3aa4956068bf3afc00273426270926988afda86","verification":{"payload":"tree 196014007c8521f67940b354cfa9f10299630a2d\nparent 75ec41aab49a67de04a53fcc809b55192d29d93e\nauthor Liane Nguyen <101995278+lianenguyen150@users.noreply.github.com> 1791068817 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791068817 -0700\n\nfeat(save-the-date): tuck the invitation back in when opening it again (#24)\n\n* docs(save-the-date): design for resealing the envelope\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(save-the-date): tuck the invitation back in when opening it again\n\n\"Open again\" used to snap straight back to the sealed envelope. A new closing\nphase now plays the way back: the note clears away, the cards tuck into the\npocket top card first, the flap folds down, and a fresh wax seal presses on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(save-the-date): gather the cards into a stack before tucking them in\n\nRunning the opening keyframes backwards sent each card high above the\nenvelope and back, and its z-index step made cards pass behind one another\nmid-air. Now the cards straighten into a stack above the pocket and slide\nin together.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwYqRCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAS3wQAJEdpFAuYWXFGbNyihAa2WRa\nmueJRHfSaPeRaL4sc0EaM+/jVDog/+dyI2x3ryc/i77vKSXGCUBUZsEl6YbZJ