om/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72/mocha/commit/31b791b7fc39b04486f379c9ad643f5b112667e8","node_id":"C_kwDOT6yInNoAKDMxYjc5MWI3ZmMzOWIwNDQ4NmYzNzljOWFkNjQzZjViMTEyNjY3ZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72/mocha/commit/443c49eefbaf9e83a83448cee8f7972e52a15903","sha":"443c49eefbaf9e83a83448cee8f7972e52a15903","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/443c49eefbaf9e83a83448cee8f7972e52a15903"}],"sha":"31b791b7fc39b04486f379c9ad643f5b112667e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/31b791b7fc39b04486f379c9ad643f5b112667e8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101995278?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lianenguyen150","id":101995278,"login":"lianenguyen150","node_id":"U_kgDOBhRTDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/443c49eefbaf9e83a83448cee8f7972e52a15903/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T06:22:25Z","email":"101995278+lianenguyen150@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Liane Nguyen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T06:22:25Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(save-the-date): add a record that plays the couple''s song (#15)\n\nThe date card gets a small vinyl record in its open top-right corner.\nTapping it plays \"Dream\" by Suzy & Baekhyun from the official YouTube\nvideo. YouTube''s API policies forbid audio-only or hidden playback, so\nthe first tap opens a visible mini player (200px tall) portaled to the\nbody; the record then follows YouTube''s state, spins while playing,\ntoggles pause, and the song loops. The IFrame API loads only on the\nfirst tap and the player uses the youtube-nocookie host.\n\nAlso lines the \"Save / the Date\" lockup up with the first date of the\nweek below it.\n\nCo-authored-by: Liane Nguyen <lianenguyen@Lianes-Laptop.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ea51b4c2c94ffff460603e122c1ae2654a538025","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/trees/ea51b4c2c94ffff460603e122c1ae2654a538025"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/commits/443c49eefbaf9e83a83448cee8f7972e52a15903","verification":{"payload":"tree ea51b4c2c94ffff460603e122c1ae2654a538025\nparent b94e46681d13257d4890aff8a3d7a786a50b666a\nauthor Liane Nguyen <101995278+lianenguyen150@users.noreply.github.com> 1791008545 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1791008545 -0700\n\nfeat(save-the-date): add a record that plays the couple''s song (#15)\n\nThe date card gets a small vinyl record in its open top-right corner.\nTapping it plays \"Dream\" by Suzy & Baekhyun from the official YouTube\nvideo. YouTube''s API policies forbid audio-only or hidden playback, so\nthe first tap opens a visible mini player (200px tall) portaled to the\nbody; the record then follows YouTube''s state, spins while playing,\ntoggles pause, and the song loops. The IFrame API loads only on the\nfirst tap and the player uses the youtube-nocookie host.\n\nAlso lines the \"Save / the Date\" lockup up with the first date of the\nweek below it.\n\nCo-authored-by: Liane Nguyen <lianenguyen@Lianes-Laptop.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwJ8hCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA7MUQAHvxln8Z8VmBZP/5Oj9GF0nY\nrfiZ1/AymlJ6n9V02tnB7DN/lY4oIprWdocU3zTAFI0QdC5RMutKebTayBgDWuNs\n35n0RxGiuF8beaIBvPOTCUtohzyX4L1tf44y9VKXn9n6EVjjqAKDWJ4Ds7JRN2+s\nZ01jvVGoHTs/pzQuwTch5S94ANf1kFZ00pt2BUXKuMXOOedb9gy7PXI64tJa3UO3\nfpVw+qPNqublw0Dk8JCYCXh4Y8JRineJ0uU45wzqkZQz/k8t87BK9iNlz8ZoEZU6\nPBwdAmv9kgwqOd+CzOYDVMo2B/mBkv6w+3M6gqmhSORjkiLw8bLgZJhJ5HTAlMYj\nQvch7pvxYni8Z7/9/jR+/mMqIhlm13Klpd2ihFFa89Ou9dX5YGiifLYTeSAu/Ml/\n4H2AKXfPYJDRAFAFIoAlnQHIYF5hZFWhC/JRtImBk50HE5pUM5iumqn8Hp53SIyM\n3tOGTFEiKJT3ZqLCis3gLH8HXn8yR1DstJw3e7rYyFidOgdaKvFZmIJ8TRWCDCTm\nFcrBP6OFt2YaZFU1CBtMWPgLqG6xjJy05YKQHmm3hWzBo4v1xftZBnlVP3DVE8qH\n0T+Fdvwst14a7bYNLxgI0i7FPHVxI3qSjMrdvDLfYQdf3nC/epX/ww8SEEcfvdsN\n78Y55Vw1TuHYvc8UEWS1\n=0L2A\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T06:22:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72/mocha/commit/443c49eefbaf9e83a83448cee8f7972e52a15903","node_id":"C_kwDOT6yInNoAKDQ0M2M0OWVlZmJhZjllODNhODM0NDhjZWU4Zjc5NzJlNTJhMTU5MDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72/mocha/commit/b94e46681d13257d4890aff8a3d7a786a50b666a","sha":"b94e46681d13257d4890aff8a3d7a786a50b666a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/b94e46681d13257d4890aff8a3d7a786a50b666a"}],"sha":"443c49eefbaf9e83a83448cee8f7972e52a15903","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/443c49eefbaf9e83a83448cee8f7972e52a15903"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/101995278?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/lianenguyen150","id":101995278,"login":"lianenguyen150","node_id":"U_kgDOBhRTDg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lianenguyen150","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/b94e46681d13257d4890aff8a3d7a786a50b666a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:47:51Z","email":"101995278+lianenguyen150@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Liane Nguyen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T05:47:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(save-the-date): design pass — mail-style envelope, blush palette, live countdown (#13)\n\n* feat(save-the-date): consolidate typography to three faces\n\nReplace the five-face mix (Josefin Sans, Lora, Parisienne, Pinyon Script,\nAllura) with a three-face system: Parisienne for every script flourish,\nCormorant Garamond for the serif display and labels, and Montserrat for\nsmall caps controls, numerals, and form text. Sizes are tuned so the\ncard stays legible and the envelope lettering sits inside the flap.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(save-the-date): drop the address form, end on \"invitation to follow\"\n\nThe card now only needs to say who, when, and where, and that a formal\ninvitation will follow. Remove the /share-your-address page, the\nFormspree submission code, its tests, the form-only dependencies and\nstyle tokens, and replace the note and its CTA with a single\n\"Formal invitation to follow\" line between two gold rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(save-the-date): warm blush palette, postmark, seal crack and one-beat-at-a-time reveal\n\nRetune the card to the couple''s mood board: warm pastel blush, ivory and a\nhint of sage, with rose-pearl accents in place of gold. The opening now\ntells the four facts in turn — the names write on in rose-pearl foil, a\nheart draws itself around the 16th, the city rises over a sage ridgeline,\nand \"formal invitation to follow\" lands last.\n\nAlso adds a postmark with the city and date on the sealed envelope, a\nfloating envelope with a pearl sheen, a seal that cracks with sparkles,\nspringier card landings, a petal burst and drifting petals, a developing\nPolaroid with a handwritten caption, pointer parallax, a countdown, an\n\"Add to calendar\" .ics, an \"Open again\" replay, and a designed link\npreview image. Reduced motion turns every new animation off.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(save-the-date): polish the opening — no ribbon, nothing peeking, cleaner seal\n\n- Remove the ribbon that rode out with the cards; in the soft palette it\n  read as a scrollbar.\n- Start the cards higher inside the envelope and hold their floral sprigs\n  back until each card has cleared it, so nothing peeks below or over the\n  envelope before the cards rise.\n- Drop the printed \"P&L\" over the wax seal; the seal''s pressed rings and\n  laurel carry it.\n- Tighten the announcement card so \"are getting married!\" sits under the\n  names, centre the wedding-week row on the date card, and make the city\n  line''s spacing match during and after the animation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(save-the-date): balance the envelope''s lettering, prompt and seal\n\nShrink the lettering so it sits inside the flap without touching its\nedges, space the prompt evenly between it and the seal, and centre the\nseal on the flap''s point.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(save-the-date): stop clipping the names'' swashes, lift them slightly\n\nThe rose-pearl foil is painted with background-clip: text, which only\npaints glyphs inside the element''s box; Parisienne''s descenders (the\ntail of the y in Peyton) dropped below it. Pad the foil box generously\nand cancel the padding with negative margins so layout is unchanged.\nAlso move the names up a touch on the announcement card.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(save-the-date): even out line spacing on the announcement and date cards\n\n- Announcement: give both line pairs the same sideways step; on the\n  -9deg card a larger step read as a different gap even though the line\n  pitch was identical.\n- Date card: lower the week row and centre the heart on the 16 so it\n  clears the month above and the city below, with even space each side.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(save-the-date): only falling petals, and room for the y in Peyton\n\n- Replace the burst petals that came to rest on the page with a dozen\n  falling petals on staggered loops, some already mid-fall on open.\n- Give \"Liane\" a little extra room so its tall L clears the tail of the\n  y in \"Peyton\", matching the gap between \"are getting\" and \"married!\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(save-the-date): redesign the announcement card as centred stationery\n\nReplace the four staggered script lines with a centred composition: a\nsage-and-blush sprig, \"Peyton\" and \"Liane\" in rose-pearl foil joined by\na serif ampersand, a sage divider, and \"are getting married!\" in serif\nto match the date card. It all sits in the part of the card the Polaroid\nleaves uncovered, and still writes on line by line during the opening.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(save-the-date): announcement card in the small-caps direction\n\nThe couple picked direction A from a side-by-side of three: names in\nrose-pearl script joined by a serif ampersand under a small sprig, then\n\"ARE GETTING MARRIED\" in small spaced capitals that echo \"OCTOBER 2027\"\non the date card. The block sits higher, inside the card''s border and\nclear of the Polaroid.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(save-the-date): live countdown, and even spacing on the names card\n\n- Replace \"N days to go\" with a ticking DAYS : HOURS : MINUTES : SECONDS\n  countdown under \"The countdown is on!\", running to midnight Eastern on\n  the wedding day. Screen readers get one plain sentence rather than a\n  live region.\n- Bring the sprig down to sit just above \"Peyton\": the foil''s descender\n  padding was being added to the gap. The space above and below the names\n  now matches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(save-the-date): \"You have mail from Peyton & Liane\" on the sealed envelope\n\nMove the greeting off the envelope flap: above the envelope, \"YOU HAVE\nMAIL FROM\" and the couple''s names in rose-pearl script that writes on as\nthe page loads; below it, \"CLICK THE ENVELOPE TO OPEN\" (\"TAP\" on touch\nscreens). Both step aside as the envelope opens. The flap is left clean\napart from the seal and the postmark.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(save-the-date): clearer hierarchy and even rhythm under the cards\n\n\"Formal invitation to follow\" leads, the countdown is the feature\n(larger numerals, airier eyebrow and labels, matching colons), and the\nlinks drop to small spaced capitals with a fine underline so they no\nlonger compete. The three groups are evenly spaced.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(save-the-date): matte pink paper envelope, and centre the opened invitation\n\n- Restyle the envelope as solid matte pastel-pink stock with a felt-like\n  grain, a softly rounded die-cut flap, and faint fold lines instead of\n  pink outlines. Drop the pearl sheen.\n- Seat the postmark wholly on the flap so no envelope edge runs through\n  it, and even out the space above and below the sealed envelope.\n- Once the cards are out, the stage glides up slightly so the opened\n  invitation sits centred.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(save-the-date): blush envelope with a centred seal, postmark beside it\n\nReturn the envelope to the pale blush paper (keeping the grain and the\nrounded flap), deepen the flap so the wax seal sits in the middle of the\nenvelope''s face, and move the postmark back outside, by the top-right\ncorner, with room beneath the couple''s names.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Liane Nguyen <lianenguyen@Lianes-Laptop.local>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2a2b2a5001b33e8d42dfcd665d1ef66daef24327","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/trees/2a2b2a5001b33e8d42dfcd665d1ef66daef24327"},"url":