github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/2531f5c22b6da806b395400692b79e6a8bf07c42"}],"sha":"6c5f8be61e402d52db04c9ab7d489bce1e5e2526","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/6c5f8be61e402d52db04c9ab7d489bce1e5e2526"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81111936?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72","id":81111936,"login":"penguyen72","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTExOTM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/2531f5c22b6da806b395400692b79e6a8bf07c42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T04:59:21Z","email":"peytonn72@gmail.com","name":"Peyton Nguyen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T04:59:21Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(save-the-date): post address submissions to Formspree (#10)\n\n* docs: add the Save the Date address-submission design\n\nWires the address form to a hosted form service, posted to directly from the\nbrowser so the app stays statically prerendered. Records the Formspree contract\nas verified against their published client rather than their docs: failure is\nreported in the JSON body, not only the HTTP status, so an ok-status check alone\nwould reintroduce the silent-success bug this work exists to fix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* docs: add the Save the Date address-submission implementation plan\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* feat(save-the-date): post address submissions to Formspree\n\nReplaces the simulated 1400ms resolve with a real browser POST to\nhttps://formspree.io/f/{id}. The seam''s signature is unchanged, so address-form.tsx\nneeds no edit — its sending/success/error machine already handles every outcome.\n\nFailure is detected from the response body as well as the status, because Formspree\nreports validation errors in the body with a 200; their own client never checks\nresponse.ok. Checking the status alone would tell a guest their address arrived when\nit had not, which is the bug this change exists to remove. A missing endpoint fails\nthe same way rather than falling back to simulated success.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* docs: document Formspree setup for the Save the Date address form\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* fix(save-the-date): address code review on the Formspree submission\n\n- Port Formspree''s full response decision tree, not just its error predicate.\n  The reference client resolves success only on a `next` token and treats an\n  unrecognised body as \"Unexpected response format\" — an error. The first pass\n  implemented only the error branch and treated \"not error-shaped\" as success,\n  so a `{}` or a half-recognised body with a 200 would have been reported to a\n  guest as delivered. Acceptance now requires the success token, which also\n  removes the `errors.length > 0` divergence review flagged: an empty errors\n  array is a failure again, matching the reference exactly.\n- Pin every one of those decisions with a test. Empty errors array, 200 with no\n  success token, and a mixed errors array matching neither predicate were all\n  previously unconstrained; dropping the success-token check now kills two tests\n  and dropping the error logging kills a third.\n- Test an absent endpoint variable as well as an empty one.\n- Document that NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined at build time, so Vercel needs a\n  redeploy and the dev server a restart after the variable changes. This was the\n  likeliest real-world failure and its symptom actively misleads: the console\n  says the variable \"is not set\" when it has in fact been set, just not rebuilt.\n- Warn against rewriting the env read to an indexed lookup, which would leave\n  every test green while shipping `undefined` to the browser.\n- Note in the README that Formspree''s own spam filtering should be enabled and\n  the submission quota watched, and that a failing live test is more likely the\n  form''s captcha settings than this code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a5e1134fe04ffa414b1a6f984346b242d5672a32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/trees/a5e1134fe04ffa414b1a6f984346b242d5672a32"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/commits/2531f5c22b6da806b395400692b79e6a8bf07c42","verification":{"payload":"tree a5e1134fe04ffa414b1a6f984346b242d5672a32\nparent 5320993675969ba10697af55155a5f0799f6f568\nauthor Peyton Nguyen <peytonn72@gmail.com> 1790225961 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790225961 -0700\n\nfeat(save-the-date): post address submissions to Formspree (#10)\n\n* docs: add the Save the Date address-submission design\n\nWires the address form to a hosted form service, posted to directly from the\nbrowser so the app stays statically prerendered. Records the Formspree contract\nas verified against their published client rather than their docs: failure is\nreported in the JSON body, not only the HTTP status, so an ok-status check alone\nwould reintroduce the silent-success bug this work exists to fix.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* docs: add the Save the Date address-submission implementation plan\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* feat(save-the-date): post address submissions to Formspree\n\nReplaces the simulated 1400ms resolve with a real browser POST to\nhttps://formspree.io/f/{id}. The seam''s signature is unchanged, so address-form.tsx\nneeds no edit — its sending/success/error machine already handles every outcome.\n\nFailure is detected from the response body as well as the status, because Formspree\nreports validation errors in the body with a 200; their own client never checks\nresponse.ok. Checking the status alone would tell a guest their address arrived when\nit had not, which is the bug this change exists to remove. A missing endpoint fails\nthe same way rather than falling back to simulated success.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* docs: document Formspree setup for the Save the Date address form\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* fix(save-the-date): address code review on the Formspree submission\n\n- Port Formspree''s full response decision tree, not just its error predicate.\n  The reference client resolves success only on a `next` token and treats an\n  unrecognised body as \"Unexpected response format\" — an error. The first pass\n  implemented only the error branch and treated \"not error-shaped\" as success,\n  so a `{}` or a half-recognised body with a 200 would have been reported to a\n  guest as delivered. Acceptance now requires the success token, which also\n  removes the `errors.length > 0` divergence review flagged: an empty errors\n  array is a failure again, matching the reference exactly.\n- Pin every one of those decisions with a test. Empty errors array, 200 with no\n  success token, and a mixed errors array matching neither predicate were all\n  previously unconstrained; dropping the success-token check now kills two tests\n  and dropping the error logging kills a third.\n- Test an absent endpoint variable as well as an empty one.\n- Document that NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined at build time, so Vercel needs a\n  redeploy and the dev server a restart after the variable changes. This was the\n  likeliest real-world failure and its symptom actively misleads: the console\n  says the variable \"is not set\" when it has in fact been set, just not rebuilt.\n- Warn against rewriting the env read to an indexed lookup, which would leave\n  every test green while shipping `undefined` to the browser.\n- Note in the README that Formspree''s own spam filtering should be enabled and\n  the submission quota watched, and that a failing live test is more likely the\n  form''s captcha settings than this code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtK4pCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAABvwQAIaxkkOu25EhRlLBjyM5CFsP\n69WKs0tL9CedAmeZ6grgNGfLrDSgHKE4E6KqRrN/welM43gRg3bnScdlAfBVlG1y\nbTo62affXIsB/i6EfwzYZvLJ35gZsko9gewHIAvLczB4aQTJaKiHHA6Pt8fJppQo\niIDawmcqoiP6q2dcrVDVpjxb7FyQLraXwoVGxB3PS/u8JgLwQHSBJ2VAYeeGsFiV\nUXk3S5tKUui+Iz0ITX0b0y7jHiO8L