l couple photograph\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(save-the-date): record the real image assets as landed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(save-the-date): replace the deprecated next/image priority prop\n\nNext 16 deprecates priority. Load the background with loading=\"eager\" and\nfetchPriority=\"high\", the seal with loading=\"eager\", and cover the opening\nphase in the seal test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8a2b31ec8d444dd833a5cfdb4e09e46d6b596c18","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/trees/8a2b31ec8d444dd833a5cfdb4e09e46d6b596c18"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/commits/5320993675969ba10697af55155a5f0799f6f568","verification":{"payload":"tree 8a2b31ec8d444dd833a5cfdb4e09e46d6b596c18\nparent f426eeb2e57156fc3147e882946d24915555d574\nauthor Peyton Nguyen <peytonn72@gmail.com> 1790225905 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790225905 -0700\n\nfeat(save-the-date): replace the image placeholders with the real Canva assets (#9)\n\n* docs: add the Save the Date real image assets design\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: add the Save the Date real image assets implementation plan\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(save-the-date): render the real floral background\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(save-the-date): render the real wax seal\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(save-the-date): render the real couple photograph\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(save-the-date): record the real image assets as landed\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(save-the-date): replace the deprecated next/image priority prop\n\nNext 16 deprecates priority. Load the background with loading=\"eager\" and\nfetchPriority=\"high\", the seal with loading=\"eager\", and cover the opening\nphase in the seal test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtK3xCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJ5IQACttnePzY801Dh/z+/B0cEFm\nWCI7We/zhycRI01O2AJLzUhXoCc1cf59+C2LqO0nkU0VhefDvPEu0LIhW4VcvdP/\nUVe8f9iM8yf/KOa1ZVS9Zt1ccm2p5xJ2KmWtQmuhRJGkr+oeznESZdY9n5576M7Y\ng5N9vt5e8cSwI4v5Ivn6W1XgZO3S0G98jA81TM4pRRIimYUGEvsu/ukyX7gBOmJX\ndpFkeJSzqUnGuTirJ0SskbGnBg6C/E6NUPl6Fu2kfCxNlAtoSd81NAeUFTb72uOF\nDnTrd4464JuflVIySMn+Qrdg/SiomqBieViVQY/cjoBqe5jxnDZuSkSo1pIZ7zs1\nviXYHrQx/qwy4GC+49nSXbb7GxEt+zjtGRKThZEP/mPFMWzjT3Jnt3CxjqgdwB7n\niDlkjZXE8ElsGIQaXZsH5LP4ily+7Et+rFo6xBrMECkSzB3D0kik2amMw+2UPuPG\nDZm47rrxZVorDTyNWxSZozBh7WUxbRiSDY2IK0QVsNno/QoOa9921UsF8bbdT+ec\ncCTU3rBWtDSMBaahLBRDdT1PnJ9LeO3R2K45WhpTt80M4lPKUSUhh7MASxOyiHoo\n/KNoCVzC8b5Y6L4mGx0wDkm3JqbycVRLyOSiub592dWBDGy259iEvOvxF5t1Dh/r\n/9N0r8FtzoOTGJnE+ryv\n=x38n\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T04:58:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72/mocha/commit/5320993675969ba10697af55155a5f0799f6f568","node_id":"C_kwDOT6yInNoAKDUzMjA5OTM2NzU5NjliYTEwNjk3YWY1NTE1NWE1ZjA3OTlmNmY1Njg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72/mocha/commit/f426eeb2e57156fc3147e882946d24915555d574","sha":"f426eeb2e57156fc3147e882946d24915555d574","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/f426eeb2e57156fc3147e882946d24915555d574"}],"sha":"5320993675969ba10697af55155a5f0799f6f568","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/5320993675969ba10697af55155a5f0799f6f568"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81111936?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72","id":81111936,"login":"penguyen72","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTExOTM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/f426eeb2e57156fc3147e882946d24915555d574/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T13:10:47Z","email":"peytonn72@gmail.com","name":"Peyton Nguyen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T13:10:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(save-the-date): port the save-the-date design into a third app (#8)\n\n* docs: add Save the Date source reference, design spec, and implementation plan\n\nExtracts the `Save the Date.dc.html` Claude Design prototype into a reference\ndoc, records the approved architecture for porting it into a third app, and\nbreaks the port into twelve test-driven tasks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* feat(save-the-date): scaffold the app with its design tokens and fonts\n\nMirrors apps/blackberry''s configuration by hand — no create-next-app. Dev port\n3002; Canton owns 3000 and Blackberry owns 3001. Overrides the shared --site-*\ncontract for the save-the-date palette, adds the app-local --std-* palette and\nthe composed ornament properties, defines the opening choreography as CSS\nkeyframes, and wires the five Google faces.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* feat(save-the-date): add invitation copy, floral sprig, and petal scatter\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* feat(save-the-date): add the invitation stage and the opening choreography\n\nBuilds the envelope, the three cards, the ribbon and the note, then wires them\nto a closed -> opening -> open phase machine. The stage is the route''s only\nclient component; page.tsx stays a Server Component and owns the page chrome.\nThe choreography itself is CSS keyframes scaled by a container query, so it\nneeds no measurement and no animation library.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* docs: record Save the Date as the repository''s third application\n\nAlso clears the remaining two-app wording the port''s edit list missed: the\n\"run both sites\" lead-in, the Vercel preview note, the packages/ui sharing\nrule, and \"regenerate either application\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* feat(save-the-date): add the address page, its form, and the /share-your-address route\n\nValidation mirrors the design prototype''s own rules, including its email regex,\nso a blank email passes and a malformed one does not. address-submit.ts is the\nsingle seam for a real endpoint; the form''s error state is driven by that\npromise rejecting, so the whole status machine is live code.\n\nAlso derives the stage''s #open entry state from useSyncExternalStore instead of\nan effect, so the server render, the hydration render and the client render\nagree without a cascading setState.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* chore(save-the-date): add the Next.js agent-rules file\n\n`next dev` writes this block itself; committing it keeps the tree clean and\nmatches apps/blackberry''s CLAUDE.md -> AGENTS.md split.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* fix(save-the-date): address code review\n\n- Move focus to the success heading as well as keeping role=\"status\". Submitting\n  unmounts the button the user was focused on, so focus fell back to <body> and a\n  keyboard user lost their place; a live region inserted together with its content\n  is also not reliably announced. The spec''s earlier reasoning for the live region\n  alone did not hold, so it is corrected too.\n- Restore the envelope''s hover and press lift, which the source design documents and\n  the port had dropped. It is the only affordance besides the cursor that tells a\n  mouse user the envelope is interactive, since the \"CLICK TO OPEN\" arc is decorative.\n  Stays CSS-only via `group-has-[button:hover]`, scoped precisely because that button\n  is the only one in the frame and exists only while the envelope is closed.\n- Drop the unreachable guard in `submitAddress`. The schema trims and requires both\n  fields and react-hook-form only submits parsed values, so it was dead code that read\n  like a real failure mode. The doc comment now says plainly how the error path is\n  reached and warns against re-adding a fake guard.\n- Fix an `invitation-stage` assertion that could not fail: the CTA already rendered\n  during `opening`, so advancing the timer proved nothing. It now asserts the seal\n  layer is dropped, which is what actually distinguishes the phases. Verified by\n  mutation — removing the timer now kills three tests.\n- Add the missing interactive coverage: the sending state and its disabled button,\n  email validation through the UI, focus restoration, and timer cleanup on unmount.\n- Restore the success check mark''s draw animation, `required` on the name and address\n  fields for aria-required, and remove the contradictory `normal-case`/`uppercase`\n  pair on the submit button.\n- Settle immediately if reduced motion is switched on mid-choreography; the ribbon has\n  keyframes but no resting state and would otherwise hang around until the timer fired.\n- Restore the curly apostrophes in the source reference doc. The source HTML uses\n  U+2019 throughout and writing the doc had normalised them, so the doc was not in\n  fact verbatim; the implementation was already correct.\n- Drop the dead `--std-photo-well` tokens and hide the decorative seal monogram from\n  assistive technology.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"02aea88227fc11b68c76e72955cde7547a1e3bc2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/trees/02aea88227fc11b68c76e72955cde7547a1e3bc2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/commits/f426eeb2e57156fc3147e882946d24915555d574","verification":{"payload":"tree 02aea88227fc11b68c76e72955cde7547a1e3bc2\nparent 8ac0142220b6ab393b1ca05873b64529ee40ecf7\nauthor Peyton Nguyen <peytonn72@gmail.com> 1790169047 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790169047 -0700\n\nfeat(save-the-date): port the save-the-date design into a third app (#8)\n\n* docs: add Save the Date source reference, design spec, and implementation plan\n\nExtracts the `Save the Date.dc.html` Claude Design prototype into a reference\ndoc, records the approved architecture for porting it into a third app, and\nbreaks the port into twelve test-driven tasks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* feat(save-the-date): scaffold the app with its design tokens and fonts\n\nMirrors apps/blackberry''s configuration by hand — no create-next-app. Dev port\n3002; Canton owns 3000 and Blackberry owns 3001. Overrides the shared --site-*\ncontract for the save-the-date palette, adds the app-local --std-* palette and\nthe composed ornament properties, defines the opening choreography as CSS\nkeyframes, and wires the five Google faces.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* feat(save-the-date): add invitation copy, floral sprig, and petal scatter\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* feat(save-the-date): add the invitation stage and the opening choreography\n\nBuilds the envelope, the three cards, the ribbon and the note, then wires them\nto a closed -> opening -> open phase machine. The stage is the route''s only\nclient component; page.tsx stays a Server Component and owns the page chrome.\nThe choreography itself is CSS keyframes scaled by a container query, so it\nneeds no measurement and no animation library.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* docs: record Save the Date as the repository''s third application\n\nAlso clears the remaining two-app wording the port''s edit list missed: the\n\"run both sites\" lead-in, the Vercel preview note, the packages/ui sharing\nrule, and \"regenerate either application\".\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* feat(save-the-date): add the address page, its form, and the /share-your-address route\n\nValidation mirrors the design prototype''s own rules, including its email regex,\nso a blank email passes and a malformed one does not. address-submit.ts is the\nsingle seam for a real endpoint; the form''s error state is driven by that\npromise rejecting, so the whole status machine is live code.\n\nAlso derives the stage''s #open entry state from useSyncExternalStore instead of\nan effect, so the server render, the hydration render and the client render\nagree without a cascading setState.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* chore(save-the-date): add the Next.js agent-rules file\n\n`next dev` writes this block itself; committing it keeps the tree clean and\nmatches apps/blackberry''s CLAUDE.md -> AGENTS.md split.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n* fix(save-the-date): address code review\n\n- Move focus to the success heading as well as keeping role=\"status\". Submitting\n  unmounts the button the user was focused on, so focus fell back to <body> and a\n  keyboard user lost their place; a live region inserted together with its content\n  is also not reliably announced. The spec''s earlier reasoning for the live region\n  alone did not hold, so it is corrected too.\n- Restore the envelope''s hover and press lift, which the source design documents and\n  the port had dropped. It is the only affordance besides the cursor that tells a\n  mouse user the envelope is interactive, since the \"CLICK TO OPEN\" arc is decorative.\n  Stays CSS-only via `group-has-[button:hover]`, scoped precisely because that button\n  is the only one in the frame and exists only while the envelope is closed.\n- Drop the unreachable guard in `submitAddress`. The schema trims and requires both\n  fields and react-hook-form only submits parsed values, so it was dead code that read\n  like a real failure mode. The doc comment now says plainly how the error path is\n  reached and warns against re-adding a fake guard.\n- Fix an `invitation-stage` assertion that could not fail: the CTA already rendered\n  during `opening`, so advancing the timer proved nothing. It now asserts the seal\n  layer is dropped, which is what actually distinguishes the phases. Verified by\n  mutation — removing the timer now kills three tests.\n- Add the missing interactive coverage: the sending state and its disabled button,\n  email validation through the UI, focus restoration, and timer cleanup on unmount.\n- Restore the success check mark''s draw animation, `required` on the name and address\n  fields for aria-required, and remove the contradictory `normal-case`/`uppercase`\n  pair on the submit button.\n- Settle immediately if reduced motion is switched on mid-choreography; the ribbon has\n  keyframes but no resting state and would otherwise hang around until the timer fired.\n- Restore the curly apostrophes in the source reference doc. The source HTML uses\n  U+2019 throughout and writing the doc had normalised them, so the doc was not in\n  fact verbatim; the implementation was already correct.\n- Drop the dead `--std-photo-well` tokens and hide the decorative seal monogram from\n  assistive technology.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mP2WQSjAs6bLLAkW58pkp\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqs8/XCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAgKQQACxAlK1tdYzNbnnGAcinU+FV\nxwXs8TPAdgf7HkHtbAPel1VjNiTgZiPWAudmnVsdfZKpKsVJlGDqXkDzy/FZdYWc\n3mmUdkMzBWfFL9qqa3wSvwCOOJAU8jF3DI1gom0qSIBCexieZDQ1CweFArA3CWpz\n6OzO9wVETdbX7hHCaQt/qagrp4YIOL5S0P8LMpdtUO9gtxiOIRoOLgoAVC+QCetR\nBL8JDYubdVmb8cDGUnvAX1RSVaFMNJUsWWINMqP+0/J7hHNaodUwM8YYF1FlCwBk\nmHPpJZelLtwBC6k4do+V86z3rPvGPnuvxYgunnkYJ5GfEbzuUtJDBO/+agcMIOfr\nY5U2J/n/xPcpszfr4YTjbg2t1oBf88O1MQkibdxbyS92nkXG2EAZ1ul/OGtjutoJ\nKbdJBp+FNh5X/0y6vjrnHShCESyULF56VonuBz2RoYnwY2NjDGXbFRDv7QUIcwN3\nviR0Hsomc386MPWgqj58T7/pq5pFHZvkWMV5vkyKP5Ojd83VO0qhDvaO9TNYofhd\nroUz6hGtUOG+4PDCrmj36CP+s5F+PKXREj7lzmoXcYURjLeiokcMf9cOr0rwKqP/\nlDsu0okKN/oHh0MyvzP0eIqhSsZaRFODhBy+VfAhbWNFbzexkkK5983KG4aMrlFE\nymVyPcObQJb+9l9UItG9\n=4cTr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T13:10:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72/mocha/commit/f426eeb2e57156fc3147e882946d24915555d574","node_id":"C_kwDOT6yInNoAKGY0MjZlZWIyZTU3MTU2ZmMzMTQ3ZTg4Mjk0NmQyNDkxNTU1NWQ1NzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72/mocha/commit/8ac0142220b6ab393b1ca05873b64529ee40ecf7","sha":"8ac0142220b6ab393b1ca05873b64529ee40ecf7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/8ac0142220b6ab393b1ca05873b64529ee40ecf7"}],"sha":"f426eeb2e57156fc3147e882946d24915555d574","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/f426eeb2e57156fc3147e882946d24915555d574"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81111936?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72","id":81111936,"login":"penguyen72","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTExOTM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/8ac0142220b6ab393b1ca05873b64529ee40ecf7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T23:30:49Z","email":"peytonn72@gmail.com","name":"Peyton Nguyen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T23:30:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: require PRs for every change, never push main directly (#7)\n\nIntroduces two accepted contribution paths: a lightweight Direct PR for\nsmall, well-scoped changes (docs, config/tooling, dependency bumps, test\nbackfills, obvious small fixes), and the full Superpowers workflow for\nanything creative, behavioral, or architectural. Both always land through\na pull request — main is never pushed or committed to directly.","tree":{"sha":"57716b97b5e963abcfff0a9e0b47497ad5921621","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/trees/57716b97b5e963abcfff0a9e0b47497ad5921621"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/commits/8ac0142220b6ab393b1ca05873b64529ee40ecf7","verification":{"payload":"tree 57716b97b5e963abcfff0a9e0b47497ad5921621\nparent 8c975678978a22bcd01b6f4a34a164a3dadc0021\nauthor Peyton Nguyen <peytonn72@gmail.com> 1787787049 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787787049 -0700\n\ndocs: require PRs for every change, never push main directly (#7)\n\nIntroduces two accepted contribution paths: a lightweight Direct PR for\nsmall, well-scoped changes (docs, config/tooling, dependency bumps, test\nbackfills, obvious small fixes), and the full Superpowers workflow for\nanything creative, behavioral, or architectural. Both always land through\na pull request — main is never pushed or committed to directly.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqj3cpCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJYEQAKVSzHLla1uHAMhRqU+4RTb0\n4QHnhNyd+JcRoDn6Ak8FOKXhaeW5SkpbII4HRy5GQPvR8eahj02+WrenGynyCBgB\njvBhcyGkxB2PPadopqZcQ7yUnvupTk61TbUjxYFjSHN1DhfCgM0HXYI/TMdchn+D\n7lU5B1lnKmhtilxN26Ll5r3bJtPBLiT+SUR/5pXcQDrMYRcI7C2qiGVcUSaaJ+ae\nyNlZxFo5UrcdGw1WtZW45nuciEe59YKBbhSBvYqHundJ64CdGReigppLKt/9do+0\nkl1G1535JRraqHN3kqy7DTAWORBtRmXldDkLKPLxofFHzsaaoYogjCPuIin37oUd\nTS0iln/uEtNisC5DfeuNj1xaZEb0+r0yfBrK0g2EXbZEpekpSM/thpUqPbxesQB1\nbQKObyjM7x4WZ9oic/xwdSYEUfiYoMGVOSfiG+jn4SoKDrhrcs3voE0r0ptHcMj9\nGh5GrbUxjPP