wers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72","id":81111936,"login":"penguyen72","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTExOTM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/8c975678978a22bcd01b6f4a34a164a3dadc0021/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T23:54:43Z","email":"peytonn72@gmail.com","name":"penguyen72"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T23:54:43Z","email":"peytonn72@gmail.com","name":"penguyen72"},"message":"test(blackberry): add coverage for Travel, Stay, Explore, Details, and FAQ\n\nThese five components had zero test coverage. Adds render/content tests\nfor all five, plus interaction tests for Stay''s and Explore''s tab\nswitching and FAQ''s accordion open/collapse behavior.\n\nAlso renames vitest.config.ts to vitest.config.mts, fixing a Vitest\nnative-config-loader warning (\"ESM syntax loaded as CommonJS\") surfaced\nwhile running these — the same class of fix already applied to\npackages/ui''s vitest config earlier in this project.","tree":{"sha":"caf7a6a834563a554b1df15a1466c568ba13f1ad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/trees/caf7a6a834563a554b1df15a1466c568ba13f1ad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/commits/8c975678978a22bcd01b6f4a34a164a3dadc0021","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81111936?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72","id":81111936,"login":"penguyen72","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTExOTM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72/mocha/commit/8c975678978a22bcd01b6f4a34a164a3dadc0021","node_id":"C_kwDOT6yInNoAKDhjOTc1Njc4OTc4YTIyYmNkMDFiNmY0YTM0YTE2NGEzZGFkYzAwMjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72/mocha/commit/849f74b45754ffc546274991f118efd1004c6bf2","sha":"849f74b45754ffc546274991f118efd1004c6bf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/849f74b45754ffc546274991f118efd1004c6bf2"}],"sha":"8c975678978a22bcd01b6f4a34a164a3dadc0021","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/8c975678978a22bcd01b6f4a34a164a3dadc0021"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81111936?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72","id":81111936,"login":"penguyen72","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTExOTM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/849f74b45754ffc546274991f118efd1004c6bf2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T23:09:31Z","email":"peytonn72@gmail.com","name":"Peyton Nguyen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T23:09:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(blackberry): add RSVP form (#6)\n\n* docs: design blackberry wedding RSVP form\n\nClient-only submission (matching source, real persistence deferred),\nstructured-fields-required/free-text-optional conditional validation\npolicy, and Blackberry-owned form logic on top of generic shadcn\nprimitives in packages/ui — all confirmed in brainstorming.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwW5iRophqSLLRKYtp8CeW\n\n* docs: plan blackberry wedding RSVP implementation\n\n11-task implementation plan for the RSVP form, executed via\nsubagent-driven-development.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwW5iRophqSLLRKYtp8CeW\n\n* feat(ui): add the destructive token slot for form validation errors\n\n* feat(ui): add Label, Input, and Textarea primitives\n\n* feat(ui): add Select primitive\n\nAdd Radix-based Select primitive with SelectTrigger, SelectContent, SelectItem,\nand SelectValue components, plus jsdom polyfills for pointer capture and scrollIntoView.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwW5iRophqSLLRKYtp8CeW\n\n* fix(ui): use generic placeholder text in Select test\n\nReplace Blackberry-specific \"Select guest count\" placeholder with generic\n\"Select an option\" to comply with content-agnostic primitive requirement.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwW5iRophqSLLRKYtp8CeW\n\n* feat(ui): add Checkbox primitive\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwW5iRophqSLLRKYtp8CeW\n\n* feat(ui): add RadioGroup primitive with the button-group visual\n\n* feat(ui): add Form primitive wrapper around react-hook-form\n\n* fix(ui): throw the intended error when useFormField is used outside Form\n\nuseFormContext() returns null (not a throw) when there''s no Form\nancestor, so destructuring getFieldState from it before the\nfieldContext/itemContext null-check produced a generic\n\"Cannot destructure property ''getFieldState'' of ''null''\" TypeError\ninstead of the actionable \"useFormField must be used within\n<FormField> and <FormItem>\" message. Reorder the null-check ahead of\nthe useFormContext()/useFormState() calls.\n\n* test(blackberry): add Vitest infrastructure and the RSVP Zod schema\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwW5iRophqSLLRKYtp8CeW\n\n* feat(blackberry): add the RSVP form with conditional validation\n\nWires every field through react-hook-form + zod, reveals the\nattending-yes-only fields, and shows a submitted/thank-you view with an\nEdit response affordance that preserves prior values.\n\nAlso polyfills window.ResizeObserver in vitest.setup.ts: Radix''s\nCheckbox/RadioGroup only mount their hidden \"bubble input\" (which calls\nuseSize -> ResizeObserver) when nested inside a real <form>, a path none\nof the prior standalone component tests exercised.\n\n* feat(blackberry): add the RSVP section wrapper\n\n* feat(blackberry): compose the RSVP section before the footer\n\n* fix(ui): address whole-branch review findings in packages/ui\n\nFixes surfaced by the final RSVP-branch code review that only became\nvisible when looking at packages/ui and apps/blackberry together:\n\n- package.json: add sideEffects: [\"*.css\"] so bundlers can tree-shake\n  the barrel export; Canton (which never touches RSVP/Select/RadioGroup/\n  Checkbox) was shipping those components + lucide-react unnecessarily.\n- form.tsx: add formLabelId to useFormField() and set it as the id on\n  FormLabel''s rendered <Label>, so consumers that can''t rely on\n  FormControl''s htmlFor (radiogroups, Select triggers) can wire\n  aria-labelledby to a stable, generated id.\n- select.tsx / button.tsx: SelectItem''s focus state and the outline\n  Button variant''s hover state used bg-background, which is invisible\n  against a bg-surface container on sites (like Blackberry) where those\n  two tokens collapse to the same value. Switched both to bg-primary/10\n  so the highlight is visible regardless of token collapse.\n- textarea.test.tsx: replace the leaked Blackberry RSVP copy\n  (\"Can''t wait to celebrate with you both!\") with a generic placeholder,\n  matching the same fix already applied to select/checkbox/radio-group\n  tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwW5iRophqSLLRKYtp8CeW\n\n* fix(blackberry): address whole-branch review findings in the RSVP form\n\nFixes surfaced by the final RSVP-branch code review:\n\n- Associate the attending/mealPreference/lodgingPreference RadioGroups\n  and the guestCount Select with their visible FormLabel text via\n  explicit id + aria-labelledby (a <div role=\"radiogroup\"> isn''t\n  labelable via <label for>, and a Select trigger''s accessible name\n  comes from its content, not from a <label for>). Also wrap the events\n  checkbox group in role=\"group\" with aria-labelledby, since it had no\n  group semantics at all.\n- Add noValidate to the <form> so a malformed email reaches Zod/\n  react-hook-form''s validation path (and the spec-required inline\n  FormMessage) instead of triggering the browser''s native constraint\n  validation bubble first.\n- Replace form.watch(\"attending\") with useWatch({ control, name }),\n  called unconditionally before the submitted early return, so it''s\n  compiler-friendly per react-hooks/incompatible-library.\n- Coerce the DOM-facing value passed to the 4 enum-backed RadioGroup/\n  Select controls to field.value ?? \"\" so Radix sees a defined string\n  from mount (silencing \"changing from uncontrolled to controlled\"),\n  while leaving react-hook-form''s actual field value untouched as\n  undefined when unset so Zod validation is unaffected.\n\nAlso extends test coverage: an accessible-name test locking in the\nlabel associations above, a malformed-email test proving the Zod\nvalidation path is reached, a schema test for attending omitted\nentirely, and an edit-response test proving attending-yes conditional\nfield values (guest count, meal preference, lodging preference) survive\na submit -> Edit response round trip.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwW5iRophqSLLRKYtp8CeW\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fd10fdc7e12dedf2a4ab73582417999afd3a9aab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/trees/fd10fdc7e12dedf2a4ab73582417999afd3a9aab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/commits/849f74b45754ffc546274991f118efd1004c6bf2","verification":{"payload":"tree fd10fdc7e12dedf2a4ab73582417999afd3a9aab\nparent 4fedbc8921cf3dd0ba3fe9e9e4ff890708c513d1\nauthor Peyton Nguyen <peytonn72@gmail.com> 1787440171 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787440171 -0700\n\nfeat(blackberry): add RSVP form (#6)\n\n* docs: design blackberry wedding RSVP form\n\nClient-only submission (matching source, real persistence deferred),\nstructured-fields-required/free-text-optional conditional validation\npolicy, and Blackberry-owned form logic on top of generic shadcn\nprimitives in packages/ui — all confirmed in brainstorming.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwW5iRophqSLLRKYtp8CeW\n\n* docs: plan blackberry wedding RSVP implementation\n\n11-task implementation plan for the RSVP form, executed via\nsubagent-driven-development.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwW5iRophqSLLRKYtp8CeW\n\n* feat(ui): add the destructive token slot for form validation errors\n\n* feat(ui): add Label, Input, and Textarea primitives\n\n* feat(ui): add Select primitive\n\nAdd Radix-based Select primitive with SelectTrigger, SelectContent, SelectItem,\nand SelectValue components, plus jsdom polyfills for pointer capture and scrollIntoView.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwW5iRophqSLLRKYtp8CeW\n\n* fix(ui): use generic placeholder text in Select test\n\nReplace Blackberry-specific \"Select guest count\" placeholder with generic\n\"Select an option\" to comply with content-agnostic primitive requirement.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwW5iRophqSLLRKYtp8CeW\n\n* feat(ui): add Checkbox primitive\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwW5iRophqSLLRKYtp8CeW\n\n* feat(ui): add RadioGroup primitive with the button-group visual\n\n* feat(ui): add Form primitive wrapper around react-hook-form\n\n* fix(ui): throw the intended error when useFormField is used outside Form\n\nuseFormContext() returns null (not a throw) when there''s no Form\nancestor, so destructuring getFieldState from it before the\nfieldContext/itemContext null-check produced a generic\n\"Cannot destructure property ''getFieldState'' of ''null''\" TypeError\ninstead of the actionable \"useFormField must be used within\n<FormField> and <FormItem>\" message. Reorder the null-check ahead of\nthe useFormContext()/useFormState() calls.\n\n* test(blackberry): add Vitest infrastructure and the RSVP Zod schema\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwW5iRophqSLLRKYtp8CeW\n\n* feat(blackberry): add the RSVP form with conditional validation\n\nWires every field through react-hook-form + zod, reveals the\nattending-yes-only fields, and shows a submitted/thank-you view with an\nEdit response affordance that preserves prior values.\n\nAlso polyfills window.ResizeObserver in vitest.setup.ts: Radix''s\nCheckbox/RadioGroup only mount their hidden \"bubble input\" (which calls\nuseSize -> ResizeObserver) when nested inside a real <form>, a path none\nof the prior standalone component tests exercised.\n\n* feat(blackberry): add the RSVP section wrapper\n\n* feat(blackberry): compose the RSVP section before the footer\n\n* fix(ui): address whole-branch review findings in packages/ui\n\nFixes surfaced by the final RSVP-branch code review that only became\nvisible when looking at packages/ui and apps/blackberry together:\n\n- package.json: add sideEffects: [\"*.css\"] so bundlers can tree-shake\n  the barrel export; Canton (which never touches RSVP/Select/RadioGroup/\n  Checkbox) was shipping those components + lucide-react unnecessarily.\n- form.tsx: add formLabelId to useFormField() and set it as the id on\n  FormLabel''s rendered <Label>, so consumers that can''t rely on\n  FormControl''s htmlFor (radiogroups, Select triggers) can wire\n  aria-labelledby to a stable, generated id.\n- select.tsx / button.tsx: SelectItem''s focus state and the outline\n  Button variant''s hover state used bg-background, which is invisible\n  against a bg-surface container on sites (like Blackberry) where those\n  two tokens collapse to the same value. Switched both to bg-primary/10\n  so the highlight is visible regardless of token collapse.\n- textarea.test.tsx: replace the leaked Blackberry RSVP copy\n  (\"Can''t wait to celebrate with you both!\") with a generic placeholder,\n  matching the same fix already applied to select/checkbox/radio-group\n  tests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwW5iRophqSLLRKYtp8CeW\n\n* fix(blackberry): address whole-branch review findings in the RSVP form\n\nFixes surfaced by the final RSVP-branch code review:\n\n- Associate the attending/mealPreference/lodgingPreference RadioGroups\n  and the guestCount Select with their visible FormLabel text via\n  explicit id + aria-labelledby (a <div role=\"radiogroup\"> isn''t\n  labelable via <label for>, and a Select trigger''s accessible name\n  comes from its content, not from a <label for>). Also wrap the events\n  checkbox group in role=\"group\" with aria-labelledby, since it had no\n  group semantics at all.\n- Add noValidate to the <form> so a malformed email reaches Zod/\n  react-hook-form''s validation path (and the spec-required inline\n  FormMessage) instead of triggering the browser''s native constraint\n  validation bubble first.\n- Replace form.watch(\"attending\") with useWatch({ control, name }),\n  called unconditionally before the submitted early return, so it''s\n  compiler-friendly per react-hooks/incompatible-library.\n- Coerce the DOM-facing value passed to the 4 enum-backed RadioGroup/\n  Select controls to field.value ?? \"\" so Radix sees a defined string\n  from mount (silencing \"changing from uncontrolled to controlled\"),\n  while leaving react-hook-form''s actual field value untouched as\n  undefined when unset so Zod validation is unaffected.\n\nAlso extends test coverage: an accessible-name test locking in the\nlabel associations above, a malformed-email test proving the Zod\nvalidation path is reached, a schema test for attending omitted\nentirely, and an edit-response test proving attending-yes conditional\nfield values (guest count, meal preference, lodging preference) survive\na submit -> Edit response round trip.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwW5iRophqSLLRKYtp8CeW\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiiwrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9KgQABpmPYRVWi2H2JNtVAK2HDn1\nqAUa84ZaKyYdWJQISOEhWYnXt5F9Ttd5sQ9mMKS9+n2htVUPdtOU3NKQ/pO5mfN2\njCb6sLtgXmkq0zlkzDh27B5WPqCXuE7CflMRP0EIcEY3ts/lG7EcFo5DCYJ5xqq7\nlGnQlQ+0UuR+MsDefzm9BFB6vBdscXj5ei7wv9Y2PJl5LiwDIdGCXgFGp0I9LwVv\nkaipJUWFB59/f72Le980Y5pZSknXTqesvwS1HMa7WcO8B+xI6spSmpxeeH3Zo1bc\nwoxKlfwFujMfH4XkhnA7H4NExt5puQyn3yCzbubHSnyQh466ZUH4xISiXSptXgPp\nSZpErTB6XAeE8OdZHsYsVTXK8Nn9QToQak3qWEoHs4UgRjG+h1UBsdZu1FztKw3r\ne4hHn7CRHJVHOd7l9UpA4aMmG2NzQ4qWgJkNlSO1XAnbolT7AQwc0ilon2Gk/I1x\nGBUmQroGKb1vno7bstZiy61axj3nxdLMR0P7JDuL4JAA/eOOdhV/buflRrnCqdY/\ne605z8B6Bgy7+so/KfUmbNZMNtieT7Wcnrwxqn6jLLlszKdQioEGWOFtbbDWstHm\ngY5MtA9whkBcBxpyvv3ixbTlhz/0ID0q5HTv673nIbKVYAEbpdvTdzCHquMIPpQn\nAxqnAT6AOjYR1+cc3EeG\n=czOE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T23:09:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72/mocha/commit/849f74b45754ffc546274991f118efd1004c6bf2","node_id":"C_kwDOT6yInNoAKDg0OWY3NGI0NTc1NGZmYzU0NjI3NDk5MWYxMThlZmQxMDA0YzZiZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72/mocha/commit/4fedbc8921cf3dd0ba3fe9e9e4ff890708c513d1","sha":"4fedbc8921cf3dd0ba3fe9e9e4ff890708c513d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/4fedbc8921cf3dd0ba3fe9e9e4ff890708c513d1"}],"sha":"849f74b45754ffc546274991f118efd1004c6bf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/849f74b45754ffc546274991f118efd1004c6bf2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81111936?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/penguyen72","id":81111936,"login":"penguyen72","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxMTExOTM2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/penguyen72","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/commits/4fedbc8921cf3dd0ba3fe9e9e4ff890708c513d1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-22T22:43:54Z","email":"peytonn72@gmail.com","name":"Peyton Nguyen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-22T22:43:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(blackberry): add Travel & Directions and Accommodations (Stay) sections (#5)\n\n* docs: add spec for Blackberry Schedule & Wedding Party sections\n\nSession 2 of the Blackberry wedding-site port — Schedule of Events\ntimeline and Wedding Party grid, built on Session 1''s foundation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ERZgEApyY74KJxjLV8aqQH\n\n* docs: design blackberry wedding RSVP form\n\nClient-only submission (matching source, real persistence deferred),\nstructured-fields-required/free-text-optional conditional validation\npolicy, and Blackberry-owned form logic on top of generic shadcn\nprimitives in packages/ui — all confirmed in brainstorming.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwW5iRophqSLLRKYtp8CeW\n\n* docs: design blackberry travel & stay sections\n\nSession 3 of 5 in the wedding-site port: Travel & Directions and\nAccommodations (Stay), including a shared Tabs primitive Session 4''s\nExplore section will reuse. Notes that Session 2 hasn''t merged yet,\ncontrary to the original brief''s assumption, and documents the\ninsertion-order plan for page.tsx accordingly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011RX5ter6UEHogsbfnHG77q\n\n* docs: design blackberry Explore/Details/FAQ sections\n\nCovers Session 4 of 5 in the wedding-site port: a reusable TabSwitch\nprimitive (available for Session 3''s Stay tabs), restyled shadcn\nTabs/Accordion, and the Explore/Details/FAQ section components with\ncolocated content.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Sinwe1keRAy4gvTpqhwMnh\n\n* docs: align travel/stay spec with Session 2''s content-colocation convention\n\nSession 2''s already-committed schedule/party spec settled on a\nsibling *-content.ts file per section (schedule.tsx + schedule-content.ts)\nrather than content inlined in the component file. Since Travel and Stay\nsit in the same directory and satisfy the identical brief instruction,\nswitch to that convention for consistency: travel.tsx + travel-content.ts,\nstay.tsx + stay-content.ts, imported via the app''s existing @/* alias.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011RX5ter6UEHogsbfnHG77q\n\n* docs: align explore/details/faq spec with Session 2''s content-colocation convention\n\nSession 2 (schedule-content.ts/schedule.tsx) and Session 3 (aligned to\nmatch) committed a flat apps/blackberry/src/components/*.tsx layout\nwith sibling *-content.ts files first. Switch this spec from its\noriginal inline-per-file colocation to the same convention so the\nfour content sessions don''t each invent a different file shape for\nthe same page, per coordination with the Session 3 peer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Sinwe1keRAy4gvTpqhwMnh\n\n* docs: plan blackberry Explore/Details/FAQ sections\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Sinwe1keRAy4gvTpqhwMnh\n\n* docs: depend on Session 4''s TabSwitch instead of building a competing Tabs\n\nConfirmed live with Session 4''s peer session (mocha-5f): they own\nTabs/Accordion/TabSwitch in packages/ui as Tasks 1-3 of their plan and\nwill notify this session once TabSwitch lands. Stay.tsx now stays a\npure Server Component that builds both hotel grids and passes them as\npanel props into TabSwitch, rather than this session adding its own\nTabs primitive - eliminates a duplicate-implementation risk and one\nwhole file (stay-tabs.tsx) from the design.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011RX5ter6UEHogsbfnHG77q\n\n* docs: plan blackberry travel & stay implementation\n\nSix tasks split into two independent tracks: Travel (fully unblocked)\nand Stay (content is unblocked, but the component itself is gated on\nSession 4 landing TabSwitch in packages/ui, per the live cross-session\ncoordination already recorded in the spec).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011RX5ter6UEHogsbfnHG77q\n\n* feat(blackberry): add Travel section content\n\n* fix(blackberry): remove unneeded next-image.d.ts\n\n* feat(blackberry): add Travel section component\n\n* feat(blackberry): compose Travel section into the page\n\n* chore(ui): pull Tabs/Accordion/TabSwitch from Session 4''s branch\n\nSession 4 (worktree-blackberry-explore-details-faq, commits 3c8f0fc,\n647daae, f07c852, ffe89e2) landed the restyled shadcn Tabs/Accordion\nprimitives and the TabSwitch wrapper this session''s Stay component\ndepends on, per the live cross-session coordination recorded in this\nsession''s spec. Not yet merged to main on their end - pulled directly\nfrom their branch (same repo, shared object database) to unblock Task\n5 rather than waiting. Verbatim copy of packages/ui/ at their branch\ntip ffe89e2; no changes made here. When Session 4 merges to main for\nreal, this should reconcile as a no-op (identical content).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011RX5ter6UEHogsbfnHG77q\n\n* feat(blackberry): add Stay section content\n\n* feat(blackberry): add Stay section component\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011RX5ter6UEHogsbfnHG77q\n\n* chore: update lockfile for pulled-in packages/ui dependencies\n\nFollow-up to 790e8ca: packages/ui/package.json gained new\ndependencies (radix-ui tabs/accordion, lucide-react,\n@testing-library/user-event) as part of Session 4''s TabSwitch pull,\nbut the lockfile update wasn''t committed alongside it. Regenerated by\npnpm install and committed here so the tree is reproducible.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011RX5ter6UEHogsbfnHG77q\n\n* feat(blackberry): compose Stay section into the page\n\n* fix(blackberry): address final review findings (tab contrast, token/class cleanup)\n\nWraps the Stay section''s TabSwitch in a div that locally overrides\n--color-foreground so the inactive \"Downtown Chattanooga\" tab label\nis readable against the dark section background (was ~2:1 contrast).\nAlso replaces a hardcoded bg-white with the existing\nbg-inverted-foreground token, drops a redundant text color class that\nduplicated the enclosing section''s inherited color, and aligns the\nplaceholder-photo comment placement between travel.tsx and stay.tsx.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011RX5ter6UEHogsbfnHG77q\n\n* fix(blackberry): use TabSwitch''s triggerClassName for tab contrast\n\nThe Round 1 fix overrode --color-foreground on a wrapper div, but Tailwind\nv4''s @theme inline compiles utilities like .text-foreground straight to\nvar(--site-foreground), so that override was inert. Session 4 shipped a\nproper mechanism on TabSwitch (triggerClassName, merged via twMerge), so\nuse that instead to set the inactive trigger''s text color directly.\n\n* chore(ui): pull TabSwitch styling passthrough from Session 4''s branch\n\nSession 4 (worktree-blackberry-explore-details-faq, commit c0ce729)\nindependently hit the same dark-background contrast problem from\ntheir own final review and added optional listClassName/\ntriggerClassName passthrough props to TabSwitch, merged via\ncn()/tailwind-merge in the underlying Tabs primitives. Pulled directly\nfrom their branch to replace this branch''s earlier CSS-variable\nworkaround (ec74321) with the proper fix. Verbatim copy of both files\nat their branch tip; no changes made here.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011RX5ter6UEHogsbfnHG77q\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cf76b5f3ae0dec1a3bd9457d402235d269ea2a2b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/trees/cf76b5f3ae0dec1a3bd9457d402235d269ea2a2b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/penguyen72/mocha/git/commits/4fedbc8921cf3dd0ba3fe9e9e4ff890708c513d1","verification":{"payload":"tree cf76b5f3ae0dec1a3bd9457d402235d269ea2a2b\nparent 0bc506bf2fc833def1324b55943ca705750bbfe8\nauthor Peyton Nguyen <peytonn72@gmail.com> 1787438634 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787438634 -0700\n\nfeat(blackberry): add Travel & Directions and Accommodations (Stay) sections (#5)\n\n* docs: add spec for Blackberry Schedule & Wedding Party sections\n\nSession 2 of the Blackberry wedding-site port — Schedule of Events\ntimeline and Wedding Party grid, built on Session 1''s foundation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ERZgEApyY74KJxjLV8aqQH\n\n* docs: design blackberry wedding RSVP form\n\nClient-only submission (matching source, real persistence deferred),\nstructured-fields-required/free-text-optional conditional validation\npolicy, and Blackberry-owned form logic on top of generic shadcn\nprimitives in packages/ui — all confirmed in brainstorming.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NwW5iRophqSLLRKYtp8CeW\n\n* docs: design blackberry travel & stay sections\n\nSession 3 of 5 in the wedding-site port: Travel & Directions and\nAccommodations (Stay), including a shared Tabs primitive Session 4''s\nExplore section will reuse. Notes that Session 2 hasn''t merged yet,\ncontrary to the original brief''s assumption, and documents the\ninsertion-order plan for page.tsx accordingly.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011RX5ter6UEHogsbfnHG77q\n\n* docs: design blackberry Explore/Details/FAQ sections\n\nCovers Session 4 of 5 in the wedding-site port: a reusable TabSwitch\nprimitive (available for Session 3''s Stay tabs), restyled shadcn\nTabs/Accordion, and the Explore/Details/FAQ section components with\ncolocated content.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Sinwe1keRAy4gvTpqhwMnh\n\n* docs: align travel/stay spec with Session 2''s content-colocation convention\n\nSession 2''s already-committed schedule/party spec settled on a\nsibling *-content.ts file per section (schedule.tsx + schedule-content.ts)\nrather than content inlined in the component file. Since Travel and Stay\nsit in the same directory and satisfy the identical brief instruction,\nswitch to that convention for consistency: travel.tsx + travel-content.ts,\nstay.tsx + stay-content.ts, imported via the app''s existing @/* alias.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011RX5ter6UEHogsbfnHG77q\n\n* docs: align explore/details/faq spec with Session 2''s content-colocation convention\n\nSession 2 (schedule-content.ts/schedule.tsx) and Session 3 (aligned to\nmatch) committed a flat apps/blackberry/src/components/*.tsx layout\nwith sibling *-content.ts files first. Switch this spec from its\noriginal inline-per-file colocation to the same convention so the\nfour content sessions don''t each invent a different file shape for\nthe same page, per coordination with the Session 3 peer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Sinwe1keRAy4gvTpqhwMnh\n\n* docs: plan blackberry Explore/Details/FAQ sections\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Sinwe1keRAy4gvTpqhwMnh\n\n* docs: depend on Session 4''s TabSwitch instead of building a competing Tabs\n\nConfirmed live with Session 4''s peer session (mocha-5f): they own\nTabs/Accordion/TabSwitch in packages/ui as Tasks 1-3 of their plan and\nwill notify this session once TabSwitch lands. Stay.tsx now stays a\npure Server Component that builds both hotel grids and passes them as\npanel props into TabSwitch, rather than this session adding its own\nTabs primitive - eliminates a duplicate-implementation risk and one\nwhole file (stay-tabs.tsx) from the design.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011RX5ter6UEHogsbfnHG77q\n\n* docs: plan blackberry travel & stay implementation\n\nSix tasks split into two independent tracks: Travel (fully unblocked)\nand Stay (content is unblocked, but the component itself is gated on\nSession 4 landing TabSwitch in packages/ui, per the live cross-session\ncoordination already recorded in the spec).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011RX5ter6UEHogsbfnHG77q\n\n* feat(blackberry): add Travel section content\n\n* fix(blackberry): remove unneeded next-image.d.ts\n\n* feat(blackberry): add Travel section component\n\n* feat(blackberry): compose Travel section into the page\n\n* chore(ui): pull Tabs/Accordion/TabSwitch from Session 4''s branch\n\nSession 4 (worktree-blackberry-explore-details-faq, commits 3c8f0fc,\n647daae, f07c852, ffe89e2) landed the restyled shadcn Tabs/Accordion\nprimitives and the TabSwitch wrapper this session''s Stay component\ndepends on, per the live cross-session coordination recorded i